ot exclude Alzheimer's disease)", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "FDG-PET brain", "modality": "nuclear", "preferred_when": "Atypical presentation or diagnostic uncertainty", "findings": [{"text": "Hypometabolism in temporoparietal and posterior cingulate regions", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Normal metabolic pattern (does not exclude early disease)", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Amyloid PET brain", "modality": "nuclear", "preferred_when": "Diagnostic uncertainty in specialized settings", "findings": [{"text": "Cortical amyloid deposition", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Negative scan (argues against Alzheimer's disease)", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "Anemia or infection can worsen cognition and mimic dementia"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Electrolyte imbalance, renal failure, and hypercalcemia are reversible causes of confusion"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Hypothyroidism is a common reversible cause of cognitive impairment"}, {"test": "b12", "why": "B12 deficiency is a reversible cause of memory loss and neuropathy"}, {"test": "folate", "why": "Low folate can contribute to cognitive impairment"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Diabetes is a vascular risk factor and poor control worsens cognition"}, {"test": "MRI brain without contrast", "why": "Excludes structural causes such as tumor, stroke, or hydrocephalus and assesses atrophy pattern"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "Neuropsychological testing", "why": "Formal cognitive testing documents the pattern and severity of deficits and supports the clinical diagnosis"}], "supporting": [{"test": "CT head without contrast", "why": "Alternative to MRI when MRI is unavailable or contraindicated", "only_if": "MRI is unavailable or contraindicated"}, {"test": "FDG-PET brain", "why": "May show characteristic hypometabolism when the diagnosis is uncertain", "only_if": "atypical presentation or diagnostic uncertainty"}, {"test": "Amyloid PET brain", "why": "Can detect