to 'Potassium hydroxide mount'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'fungal_culture' to 'Fungal culture'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'potassium_hydroxide_mount' to 'Potassium hydroxide mount'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'wood_lamp_examination' to 'Wood lamp examination'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'bacterial_culture_wound' to 'Bacterial culture wound'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'xray_foot' to 'Xray foot'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'mri_foot' to 'Mri foot'", "auto-repaired: workup: 'potassium hydroxide mount' was in ['initial', 'confirmatory'], kept ['initial']", "differential cellulitis: no profile yet", "differential contact-dermatitis: no profile yet", "differential psoriasis: no profile yet", "differential erythrasma: no profile yet", "differential pitted-keratolysis: no profile yet", "differential dyshidrotic-eczema: no profile yet"]}, "review": {"status": "pending"}}, "patient": {"age": {"typical_min": 16, "typical_max": 70, "peak": "20–40", "possible_min": 2, "possible_max": 90}, "sex": "male_predominant", "demographics": ["More common in adolescents and adult men", "Common in people who use communal showers, pools, or gyms", "More frequent in warm, humid climates and in the summer months"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Walking barefoot in locker rooms, public showers, or pool decks", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Excessive sweating of the feet or wearing occlusive shoes all day", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Sharing shoes, socks, or towels with an affected person", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Peripheral vascular disease or venous stasis", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Immunosuppression (e.g., HIV, transplant, chronic corticosteroids)", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Male sex", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Obesity", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Diabetes mellitus", "Peripheral arterial disease", "Venous insufficiency", "Immunosuppression", "Onychomycosis", "Tinea cruris or tinea corporis"], "family_history": ["Often a household member with the same foot rash or fungal nail infection"], "social_history": ["Athlete or regular gym-goer", "Military service or communal living", "Occupational exposure to wet floors (e.g., pool staff, cleaners)"], "exposures": ["Communal showers or locker room floors", "Swimming pools", "Shared footwear or towels", "Hot, humid weather"], "risk_medications": ["Prednisone", "Tacrolimus", "Cyclosporine", "Methotrexate", "Adalimumab", "Infliximab"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "The skin between my toes is itchy and peeling", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "My feet itch and burn, especially at night", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "The skin on my feet is cracked and scaly", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My feet smell bad and the skin looks white and soggy", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual over days to weeks; often noticed after a gym, pool, or shower exposure", "duration": "Usually present for 1–4 weeks before the patient seeks care; may be recurrent over months or years", "progression": "Starts between the toes, especially the fourth and fifth web space, then spreads to the sole or dorsum; may wax and wane", "location": "Most often the web spaces between the toes, especially between the fourth and fifth toes; can involve the sole, heel, or top of the foot", "radiation": "Not applicable", "quality": "Itchy, burning, peeling, cracked, or macerated skin", "severity": "Mild to moderate; itching can be intense and disrupt sleep", "timing": "Itching is often worse at night or after removing shoes and socks", "aggravating": ["Sweating", "Wearing closed shoes all day", "Warm, humid weather", "Walking barefoot in public showers or locker rooms"], "relieving": ["Keeping feet dry", "Wearing sandals or open shoes", "Over-the-counter antifungal cream", "Cool water soaks"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Peeling or scaling between the toes", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Itching", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Burning or stinging of the feet", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "White, soggy, macerated skin between the toes", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Thickened, discolored toenails", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Foul foot odor", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Small blisters or vesicles on the sole or instep", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Painful cracking or fissures of the heel or sole", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Red, scaly rash in the groin or on the hands", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Fever", "Redness spreading rapidly up the leg", "Severe pain out of proportion to the rash", "Purulent drainage or foul-smelling pus", "Numbness or loss of sensation in the feet", "Black or necrotic skin", "Recent antibiotic use", "Known psoriasis or eczema of the feet"]}, "ros": [{"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Itchy, scaly rash between the toes", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Peeling or flaking skin on the soles", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Small blisters on the foot", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Thickened or yellow toenails", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Rash on the palms or trunk", "Pustules", "Skin ulcers", "Hair loss"], "argues_against": ["Rash involving the palms and soles with nail pitting (psoriasis)", "Honey-colored crusted lesions (impetigo)", "Sharply demarcated plaques with silvery scale"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Mild soreness when walking", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Joint swelling", "Joint redness", "Inability to bear weight"], "argues_against": ["Acute monoarthritis of the great toe (gout)", "Cellulitis with severe limb pain"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Fever", "Chills", "Weight loss", "Night sweats"], "argues_against": ["Systemic infection or cellulitis"]}, {"system": "neurologic", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Numbness or tingling in the feet", "Weakness", "Loss of balance"], "argues_against": ["Diabetic peripheral neuropathy as the primary cause of foot symptoms"]}, {"system": "allergic_immunologic", "positives": [], "negatives": ["New soap, detergent, or shoe material exposure", "Known contact allergy"], "argues_against": ["Contact dermatitis from footwear or topical products"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Often presents with itching and peeling between the toes, but young children may not localize symptoms and instead show fussiness or scratching at the feet; the rash may be mistaken for eczema or diaper rash if it involves the soles.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear description of itching between the toes"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "May have less itching and more dry, cracked, scaly skin on the soles, which can be mistaken for dry skin or eczema; diabetes and poor circulation increase the risk of more extensive or stubborn infection.", "missing_classic_features": ["Prominent itching", "Maceration between the toes"]}, {"population": "diabetes", "how_it_differs": "Athlete's foot can be more extensive, slower to heal, and more likely to lead to bacterial cellulitis or foot ulcers; sensory neuropathy may blunt the itching and pain.", "missing_classic_features": ["Itching as the main symptom"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "The infection may be more widespread, involve the soles and dorsum extensively, and respond more slowly to topical therapy; risk of secondary bacterial infection is higher.", "missing_classic_features": ["Localized rash limited to the toe web spaces"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Well-appearing, comfortable, no distress; normal gait", "moderate": "Well-appearing; may scratch at the feet or shift weight off the affected foot", "severe": "Well-appearing but uncomfortable; limping or avoiding weight on a fissured foot", "critical": "Ill-appearing with systemic signs (fever, spreading erythema, purulence) suggesting secondary bacterial infection rather than uncomplicated tinea pedis"}, "findings": [{"id": "interdigital-maceration", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the web spaces between all toes, spreading the toes apart", "finding": "White, soggy, macerated skin with peeling and fissuring, most often between the fourth and fifth toes", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "interdigital-erythema-scaling", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the interdigital skin after drying", "finding": "Erythema with fine scaling and a slightly raised, advancing edge", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "plantar-scaling", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the soles and heels", "finding": "Diffuse dry scaling, sometimes in a moccasin-like distribution over the sole and heel", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "plantar-vesicles", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the instep and sole", "finding": "Small grouped vesicles or blisters", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "fissures", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the heel and interdigital spaces", "finding": "Painful cracks or fissures of the skin", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "dermatophyte-odor", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Note any odor when removing socks or examining the feet", "finding": "Musty or foul foot odor", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "onychomycosis", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Inspect all toenails", "finding": "Thickened, yellow-brown, crumbling, or distally separated nails", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "dorsal-extension", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the dorsum of the foot", "finding": "Scaling or erythema extending onto the top of the foot", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-pustules", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the rash for pustules or honey-colored crust", "finding": "No pustules or honey-colored crust", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-cellulitis", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Palpate the leg and foot for warmth, tenderness, and spreading erythema", "finding": "No warmth, tenderness, or erythema extending up the leg", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "no-ulcer", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the sole and between the toes for breaks in the skin", "finding": "No ulcer or full-thickness skin defect", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-neuropathy", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Test sensation with monofilament or light touch, especially if diabetes is present", "finding": "Intact sensation in the feet", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-joint-swelling", "region": "musculoskeletal", "maneuver": "Inspect and palpate the joints of the foot and ankle", "finding": "No joint swelling, warmth, or redness", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-palmoplantar-pustulosis", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the palms and soles", "finding": "No sterile pustules or sharply demarcated silvery plaques on the palms and soles", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {}, "labs": [], "imaging": [], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "Potassium hydroxide mount", "why": "First-line bedside test: scraped scale from the active edge or macerated web space shows branching septate hyphae, confirming a dermatophyte infection"}, {"test": "Fungal culture", "why": "Identifies the species when the diagnosis is uncertain or the rash fails topical therapy", "only_if": "KOH is negative but tinea pedis is still suspected, or the infection is not responding to treatment"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "Wood lamp examination", "why": "Helps distinguish dermatophyte infection from erythrasma or other causes of interdigital scaling", "only_if": "the diagnosis is unclear after KOH testing"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "No role in a localized superficial fungal infection; a normal white count is expected"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Inflammatory markers are not useful for tinea pedis"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "Not helpful in superficial fungal skin infection"}, {"test": "glucose", "why": "Not needed to diagnose athlete's foot; check only if diabetes is suspected or already known"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Not part of the workup for athlete's foot"}, {"test": "Bacterial culture wound", "why": "Only if secondary bacterial infection is suspected; not routine for uncomplicated tinea pedis"}, {"test": "Xray foot", "why": "No bony abnormality in athlete's foot; imaging does not help"}, {"test": "Mri foot", "why": "Not indicated for a superficial skin infection"}], "decision_points": ["Confirm the diagnosis with KOH microscopy before starting systemic therapy or when the rash does not respond to topical antifungals", "Look for onychomycosis and treat it, since infected nails are a reservoir for recurrent tinea pedis", "In diabetes or immunosuppression, examine carefully for fissures, ulcers, and secondary bacterial infection"], "criteria": [], "scores": []}, "differential": [{"name": "Cellulitis", "slug": "cellulitis", "why_considered": "Both cause a red, warm, painful foot; cellulitis can complicate or mimic tinea pedis.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Rapidly spreading redness, fever, or systemic symptoms", "discriminators": {"history": ["Acute onset over hours to days", "Fever and chills", "Pain out of proportion to skin findings"], "exam": ["Diffuse erythema, warmth, and tenderness without scaling or maceration", "Lymphangitic streaking", "No interdigital maceration"], "labs": ["Leukocytosis", "Elevated inflammatory markers (CRP, ESR)"], "imaging": ["Not routinely needed; consider ultrasound if abscess suspected"]}}, {"name": "Contact dermatitis", "slug": "contact-dermatitis", "why_considered": "Itchy, red, scaly rash on the feet, often triggered by shoes or topical products.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Exposure to new shoes, socks, or topical agents", "Itching and burning without a musty odor", "No improvement with antifungals"], "exam": ["Erythema and scaling on the dorsum or areas of contact, often sparing the web spaces", "Sharp demarcation at the shoe line", "No maceration between toes"], "labs": ["KOH negative"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Psoriasis", "slug": "psoriasis", "why_considered": "Scaly plaques on the soles and between toes can resemble tinea pedis.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Chronic, persistent rash", "Personal or family history of psoriasis", "Nail pitting or separation"], "exam": ["Well-demarcated plaques with silvery scale, often on soles and palms", "Nail changes (pitting, oil spots, onycholysis)", "No central clearing or advancing border"], "labs": ["KOH negative"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Erythrasma", "slug": "erythrasma", "why_considered": "Interdigital scaling and maceration caused by Corynebacterium minutissimum.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Mild itching or asymptomatic", "Often in toe web spaces", "May have similar rash in groin or axillae"], "exam": ["Sharply demarcated, brownish-red, scaly patches", "Wood's lamp shows coral-red fluorescence", "KOH negative"], "labs": ["Wood's lamp examination", "Bacterial culture if needed"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Pitted keratolysis", "slug": "pitted-keratolysis", "why_considered": "Causes small pits and maceration on the soles, often with odor.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Hyperhidrosis", "Foul odor", "Mild or no itching"], "exam": ["Multiple small punched-out pits on the soles, especially weight-bearing areas", "No interdigital maceration", "KOH negative"], "labs": ["Clinical diagnosis; KOH negative"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Dyshidrotic eczema", "slug": "dyshidrotic-eczema", "why_considered": "Vesicular rash on the soles and palms that can be itchy.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recurrent episodes of itchy vesicles", "Often associated with atopy or stress", "No response to antifungals"], "exam": ["Deep-seated vesicles on the instep and palms", "Scaling and fissures after vesicles resolve", "No interdigital maceration"], "labs": ["KOH negative"], "imaging": []}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Mild itching and scaling limited to the toe web spaces; no fissures or secondary infection.", "moderate": "More extensive scaling, maceration, and fissures involving the sole or multiple web spaces; itching interferes with sleep.", "severe": "Extensive involvement of the sole and dorsum, painful fissures, and possible secondary bacterial infection; may require systemic antifungal therapy."}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Rapidly spreading redness, warmth, and swelling of the foot or leg", "meaning": "Suggests bacterial cellulitis, which requires prompt antibiotic treatment."}, {"finding": "Fever, chills, or systemic symptoms", "meaning": "Indicates possible systemic infection or severe secondary bacterial infection."}, {"finding": "Purulent drainage or foul-smelling pus", "meaning": "Suggests secondary bacterial infection or abscess."}, {"finding": "Severe pain out of proportion to skin findings", "meaning": "May indicate deeper infection such as abscess or necrotizing fasciitis."}, {"finding": "Black or necrotic skin", "meaning": "Suggests necrotizing infection or severe vascular compromise; emergency."}, {"finding": "Numbness or loss of sensation in the feet", "meaning": "May indicate peripheral neuropathy, increasing risk of unnoticed injury and infection."}], "complications": [{"name": "Secondary bacterial infection (cellulitis)", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Increasing redness, warmth, and pain", "Fever", "Purulent drainage"]}, {"name": "Onychomycosis", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Thickened, discolored, crumbling toenails", "Persistent tinea pedis despite treatment"]}, {"name": "Chronic fissures and pain", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Persistent heel or interdigital fissures", "Pain with walking"]}, {"name": "Recurrence", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["History of previous episodes", "Untreated onychomycosis or continued exposure to damp environments"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "children", "differences": "May present with itching and peeling between toes, but young children may not localize symptoms; rash may be mistaken for eczema."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Less itching and more dry, cracked, scaly skin on the soles; may be mistaken for dry skin or eczema; diabetes and poor circulation increase risk of complications."}, {"population": "diabetes", "differences": "More extensive, slower to heal, and higher risk of bacterial cellulitis or foot ulcers; sensory neuropathy may blunt itching and pain."}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "differences": "Infection may be more widespread, involve soles and dorsum extensively, respond more slowly to topical therapy, and have higher risk of secondary bacterial infection."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "Where exactly on your feet did the rash start, and where is it now?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Starts between the toes, especially the fourth and fifth web space, then may spread to the sole or top of the foot"}, {"question": "How long has it been there, and is it getting better or worse?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Gradual onset over days to weeks; may wax and wane or recur over months"}, {"question": "What does the skin look like and feel like?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Itchy, peeling, cracked, scaly, or white and soggy skin between the toes"}, {"question": "Does it itch or burn, and when is it worst?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Itching or burning, often worse at night or after removing shoes and socks"}, {"question": "What makes it better or worse?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Worse with sweating, closed shoes, warm humid weather; better with dry feet, sandals, or antifungal cream"}, {"question": "Do you walk barefoot in locker rooms, public showers, or around pools?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Exposure to damp communal floors, a classic risk factor"}, {"question": "Do your feet sweat a lot, or do you wear closed shoes all day?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Hyperhidrosis or occlusive footwear"}, {"question": "Does anyone at home have the same foot rash or thick, discolored toenails?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Household member with tinea pedis or onychomycosis; shared footwear or towels"}, {"question": "Have you had this before, and did anything treat it?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prior episodes or partial response to over-the-counter antifungals"}, {"question": "Do you have diabetes, poor circulation, or a weakened immune system?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Diabetes, peripheral arterial disease, venous insufficiency, or immunosuppression; raises risk of complications"}, {"question": "Are you taking any medicines that suppress the immune system, like prednisone or a biologic?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Corticosteroids, tacrolimus, cyclosporine, methotrexate, or TNF inhibitors"}, {"question": "Have you used any creams, powders, or home remedies on it?", "category": "medications", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Antifungal use, steroid creams, or other topical products that may change the appearance"}, {"question": "Have you had a fever, chills, or redness spreading up your leg?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent in uncomplicated tinea pedis; present suggests cellulitis or systemic infection"}, {"question": "Is the pain severe, or is there pus or a foul-smelling discharge?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; present suggests secondary bacterial infection or deeper infection"}, {"question": "Any numbness, tingling, or loss of feeling in your feet?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Absent; present suggests peripheral neuropathy and higher risk of unnoticed injury"}, {"question": "Any rash in your groin, on your hands, or elsewhere?", "category": "associated", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Tinea cruris or tinea manuum, which often accompany tinea pedis"}], "accepted_names": ["Athlete's foot", "Tinea pedis", "Dermatophyte infection of the foot", "Foot fungus", "Fungal foot infection"], "reasoning_points": ["Itchy, scaly, peeling rash that begins in the toe web spaces, especially between the fourth and fifth toes", "Maceration, fissuring, or a moccasin-like pattern of scaling on the sole", "Exposure to damp communal floors such as locker rooms, showers, or pool decks", "Risk factors such as hyperhidrosis, occlusive footwear, diabetes, or immunosuppression", "Associated onychomycosis or tinea cruris supporting a dermatophyte process", "No fever, spreading erythema, purulence, or severe pain to suggest bacterial cellulitis", "KOH microscopy showing branching septate hyphae confirms the diagnosis"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Young adult athlete or gym-goer", "Classic itchy, peeling rash between the fourth and fifth toes", "Recent exposure to locker room or pool floors", "No systemic symptoms"], "medium": ["Moccasin distribution of dry scaling on the sole without prominent interdigital findings", "Coexisting onychomycosis or tinea cruris", "Older adult with dry, cracked soles mistaken for dry skin", "Partial improvement with over-the-counter antifungal cream"], "hard": ["Patient with diabetes and neuropathy where itching is blunted and the rash is extensive", "Immunocompromised patient with widespread sole and dorsum involvement", "Vesicular or bullous presentation on the instep mimicking dyshidrotic eczema", "Rash that fails topical therapy and requires KOH or culture to separate from psoriasis or contact dermatitis", "Secondary bacterial cellulitis complicating the picture"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
on conflict (slug) do update set name = excluded.name, primary_clerkship = excluded.primary_clerkship, clerkships = excluded.clerkships, organ_systems = excluded.organ_systems, validation = excluded.validation, review = excluded.review, profile = excluded.profile, updated_at = now();

insert into private.condition_profiles (slug, name, primary_clerkship, clerkships, organ_systems, validation, review, profile) values ($rounds_kb$atrial-fibrillation$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$Atrial Fibrillation$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, array[$rounds_kb$internalMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$emergency$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$familyMedicine$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$neurology$rounds_kb$]::text[], array[$rounds_kb$cardiovascular$rounds_kb$]::text[], $rounds_kb$passed$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb$pending$rounds_kb$, $rounds_kb${"schema_version": "0.2", "slug": "atrial-fibrillation", "triage": {"name": "Atrial Fibrillation", "case_suitable": true, "reason": "Very common arrhythmia presenting with palpitations, dyspnea or incidentally; diagnosis by ECG with rich teaching on stroke risk and rate/rhythm management.", "kind": "disease", "category": "arrhythmia", "organ_systems": ["cardiovascular"], "primary_clerkship": "internalMedicine", "secondary_clerkships": ["emergency", "familyMedicine", "neurology"], "commonness": "very_common", "settings": ["clinic", "emergency", "inpatient", "icu"], "is_cancer": false}, "generation": {"stages": [{"stage": "triage", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "prompt_version": "7", "generated_at": "2026-10-05T04:15:53Z"}, {"stage": "patient_presentation", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "prompt_version": "8", "generated_at": "2026-10-05T04:48:24Z"}, {"stage": "exam_vitals", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "prompt_version": "8", "generated_at": "2026-10-05T04:48:30Z"}, {"stage": "diagnostics", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "prompt_version": "8", "generated_at": "2026-10-05T04:48:55Z"}, {"stage": "differential_course", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "prompt_version": "8", "generated_at": "2026-10-05T04:49:08Z"}, {"stage": "teaching", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "prompt_version": "8", "generated_at": "2026-10-05T04:49:15Z"}], "validation": {"status": "passed", "rule_errors": [], "review_issues": ["auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'ecg' to 'ECG'", "auto-repaired: workup: renamed 'ecg' to 'ECG'", "auto-repaired: workup: 'ecg' was in ['initial', 'confirmatory'], kept ['initial']", "auto-repaired: ecg: dropped extra keys ['leads'] (findings carry their own leads)", "differential atrial-flutter: no profile yet", "differential multifocal-atrial-tachycardia: no profile yet", "differential sinus-tachycardia: no profile yet", "differential supraventricular-tachycardia: no profile yet", "differential ventricular-tachycardia: no profile yet", "differential wolff-parkinson-white: no profile yet", "differential sick-sinus-syndrome: no profile yet", "differential panic-disorder: no profile yet", "differential hyperthyroidism: no profile yet"]}, "review": {"status": "pending"}}, "patient": {"age": {"typical_min": 55, "typical_max": 90, "peak": "65–85", "possible_min": 18, "possible_max": 110}, "sex": "either", "demographics": ["Risk rises steadily with age; most patients are over 65", "More common in people of European ancestry than in other groups", "Men are affected somewhat more often than women"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Age over 65", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "High blood pressure", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Heart failure", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Valvular heart disease, especially mitral valve disease", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Heavy alcohol use", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Obesity", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Diabetes", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Obstructive sleep apnea", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Hyperthyroidism", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Chronic kidney disease", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "COPD or other chronic lung disease", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Coronary artery disease", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Family history of atrial fibrillation", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Recent heart, lung, or esophageal surgery", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Stimulant drug use such as cocaine or methamphetamine", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Congenital heart disease", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Hypertension", "Heart failure", "Coronary artery disease", "Valvular heart disease", "Diabetes", "Obesity", "Obstructive sleep apnea", "Chronic kidney disease", "COPD", "Hyperthyroidism"], "family_history": ["Atrial fibrillation in a parent or sibling", "Early heart disease in the family"], "social_history": ["Regular or heavy alcohol use", "Current or past smoking", "Stimulant drug use"], "exposures": ["Recent cardiothoracic or esophageal surgery", "Acute illness or infection"], "risk_medications": ["levothyroxine", "albuterol", "pseudoephedrine", "cocaine"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "My heart is racing and fluttering in my chest", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I get tired so easily, even just walking to the mailbox", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I feel like my heart is skipping beats", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I get short of breath when I do anything", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I felt lightheaded and almost passed out", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "My doctor told me my pulse was irregular at my checkup", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Often sudden, over seconds to minutes; sometimes noticed only when a clinician checks the pulse or on a routine ECG", "duration": "Episodes may last minutes to hours and stop on their own, or the rhythm may stay irregular for days, weeks, or longer", "progression": "Variable: some people have brief episodes that come and go, others have episodes that last longer over time, and some remain in the irregular rhythm continuously", "location": "Chest, with the sensation of the heartbeat felt in the chest and sometimes the neck", "radiation": "Usually none", "quality": "Fast, irregular, fluttering or pounding heartbeat; often described as a fish flopping or a drumroll rather than a steady beat", "severity": "Mild to moderate for most; can be severe when the rate is very fast or when heart failure or low blood pressure develops", "timing": "Episodes can start at any time, often at rest or at night; exercise and alcohol can bring them on", "aggravating": ["Alcohol", "Caffeine", "Exercise or exertion", "Stress", "Dehydration or acute illness"], "relieving": ["Resting and sitting down", "Episodes may stop on their own", "Rate-controlling medication"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Fatigue or low energy", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath with activity", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Feeling lightheaded or dizzy", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath when lying flat", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Chest discomfort or pressure", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Swelling in the ankles or legs", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Waking up at night short of breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Fainting", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Sudden weakness or numbness on one side, trouble speaking, or vision loss (from a clot causing a stroke)", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Crushing chest pain that radiates to the arm or jaw and comes on with exertion", "Fever", "Coughing up blood", "Recent long car ride, flight, or leg surgery with one-sided leg swelling", "Sudden sharp chest pain that worsens with a deep breath", "Known prior heart attack with the same pain", "Vomiting or diarrhea causing dehydration"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Tiredness or low energy", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Poor exercise tolerance", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Fever", "Unintentional weight loss", "Night sweats"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [{"text": "Palpitations or fluttering in the chest", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Irregular or racing pulse", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chest discomfort", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Swelling in the legs or ankles", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Pain that radiates to the arm or jaw", "Pain brought on reliably by exertion and relieved by rest", "Fainting with exertion"], "argues_against": ["Angina from blocked coronary arteries", "Aortic dissection"]}, {"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Shortness of breath with activity", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Shortness of breath when lying flat", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Waking at night short of breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Coughing up blood", "Pleuritic chest pain", "Recent immobility with leg swelling"], "argues_against": ["Pulmonary embolism", "Pneumonia"]}, {"system": "neurologic", "positives": [{"text": "Lightheadedness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Fainting", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Sudden one-sided weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Severe sudden headache", "New confusion or trouble finding words", "Loss of vision in one eye"], "argues_against": ["Intracranial hemorrhage", "Stroke as the only problem"]}, {"system": "psychiatric", "positives": [{"text": "Anxiety or worry about the heartbeat", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Panic attacks that reliably precede the palpitations", "Depressed mood"]}, {"system": "endocrine", "positives": [{"text": "Heat intolerance, tremor, or weight loss", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Cold intolerance", "Polyuria and polydipsia"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable, no distress; may be unaware of the rhythm", "moderate": "Mildly anxious or restless, aware of the heartbeat", "severe": "Dyspneic at rest or with minimal effort, diaphoretic, prefers sitting upright", "critical": "Ill-appearing, pale and clammy, confused or lethargic, may be hypotensive"}, "findings": [{"id": "irregularly-irregular-pulse", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Palpate the radial pulse for at least 30 seconds (or auscultate the heart)", "finding": "Irregularly irregular rhythm with a variable rate and pulse deficit relative to the apical rate", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "irregular-heart-sounds", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the heart at the apex and base", "finding": "Irregularly irregular heart sounds with variable intensity of S1", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "tachycardia", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Count the heart rate by auscultation or on the monitor", "finding": "Heart rate above 100/min", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "pulse-deficit", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Compare the apical rate by auscultation with the radial rate by palpation simultaneously", "finding": "Radial rate lower than the apical rate", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "s3-gallop", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the apex with the bell while the patient lies on the left side", "finding": "Third heart sound suggesting heart failure", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "rales", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lung bases posteriorly", "finding": "Crackles at the bases from pulmonary congestion", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "jvd", "region": "neck", "maneuver": "Inspect the internal jugular venous pulsation with the patient at 30–45 degrees", "finding": "Elevated jugular venous pressure", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "peripheral-edema", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Press over the dorsum of the foot and lower shin for several seconds", "finding": "Pitting edema of the lower extremities", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "murmur", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate all valve areas for murmurs", "finding": "Murmur suggesting valvular disease, such as mitral stenosis or regurgitation", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "hypotension", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Measure the blood pressure in both arms", "finding": "Low blood pressure or a narrow pulse pressure", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "altered-mental-status", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Assess orientation and level of alertness", "finding": "Confusion or lethargy from poor perfusion", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "critical", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "focal-neuro-deficit", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Perform a focused neurologic exam including strength, speech, and facial symmetry", "finding": "Focal weakness, sensory loss, or speech difficulty from a cardioembolic stroke", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "regular-pulse", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Palpate the radial pulse", "finding": "Regular rhythm with a normal rate", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-murmur", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the heart", "finding": "No murmur or gallop", "frequency": "common", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "clear-lungs", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lungs", "finding": "Clear breath sounds without crackles or wheezing", "frequency": "common", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {"hr": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 110}, "moderate": {"min": 90, "max": 140}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 170}, "critical": {"min": 150, "max": 220}}, "rr": {"moderate": {"min": 18, "max": 24}, "severe": {"min": 22, "max": 30}, "critical": {"min": 26, "max": 36}}, "sbp": {"severe": {"min": 90, "max": 110}, "critical": {"min": 70, "max": 95}}, "dbp": {"severe": {"min": 50, "max": 70}, "critical": {"min": 40, "max": 60}}, "spo2": {"moderate": {"min": 92, "max": 96}, "severe": {"min": 88, "max": 93}, "critical": {"min": 82, "max": 90}}}, "labs": [{"test_id": "tsh", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 0.01, "max": 0.3}, "moderate": {"min": 0.01, "max": 0.2}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Hyperthyroidism is a reversible cause; check in every new diagnosis. Values shown are for hyperthyroid patients; most patients with AFib have a normal TSH."}, {"test_id": "ft4", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.9, "max": 2.6}, "moderate": {"min": 2.2, "max": 3.5}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Only abnormal when thyrotoxicosis is the driver."}, {"test_id": "hgb", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 10.0, "max": 11.9}, "moderate": {"min": 8.5, "max": 10.5}, "severe": {"min": 7.0, "max": 9.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Anemia worsens symptoms and can precipitate AFib; also matters before anticoagulation."}, {"test_id": "plt", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 149}, "moderate": {"min": 60, "max": 120}, "severe": {"min": 30, "max": 80}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low platelets affect the choice and safety of anticoagulation."}, {"test_id": "cr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.6}, "moderate": {"min": 1.5, "max": 2.2}, "severe": {"min": 2.0, "max": 3.5}, "critical": {"min": 3.0, "max": 6.0}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Kidney function drives anticoagulant dosing and is part of stroke and bleeding risk scores."}, {"test_id": "k", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 3.2, "max": 3.4}, "moderate": {"min": 2.8, "max": 3.2}, "severe": {"min": 2.4, "max": 2.9}, "critical": {"min": 2.0, "max": 2.6}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hypokalemia (diuretics) promotes AFib; hyperkalemia can widen the QRS and mimic other rhythms."}, {"test_id": "mg", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.5, "max": 1.7}, "moderate": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.6}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low magnesium makes rate control harder and predisposes to arrhythmia."}, {"test_id": "hs_tnt", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 15, "max": 30}, "moderate": {"min": 25, "max": 80}, "severe": {"min": 60, "max": 300}, "critical": {"min": 200, "max": 2000}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Mild elevations are common from demand ischemia with a fast rate; a rising pattern suggests acute coronary syndrome and changes management."}, {"test_id": "bnp", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 120, "max": 400}, "moderate": {"min": 300, "max": 900}, "severe": {"min": 700, "max": 2000}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated in heart failure, which is both a cause and a consequence of AFib."}, {"test_id": "nt_probnp", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 150, "max": 500}, "moderate": {"min": 400, "max": 1200}, "severe": {"min": 900, "max": 3000}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional"}, {"test_id": "inr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.5}, "moderate": {"min": 1.5, "max": 2.5}, "severe": {"min": 2.5, "max": 4.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Baseline before starting warfarin; therapeutic range for AFib is usually 2.0–3.0. Normal if the patient is not on warfarin."}, {"test_id": "aptt", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 36, "max": 45}, "moderate": {"min": 45, "max": 70}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Prolonged only if the patient is on heparin or has a coagulopathy."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "moderate": {"min": 6.5, "max": 8.0}, "severe": {"min": 8.0, "max": 11.0}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Diabetes is common and adds to stroke risk."}, {"test_id": "ldl", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 129}, "moderate": {"min": 130, "max": 159}, "severe": {"min": 160, "max": 220}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Guides vascular risk reduction."}, {"test_id": "d_dimer", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 0.6, "max": 1.5}, "moderate": {"min": 1.5, "max": 4.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Not part of AFib workup; only if pulmonary embolism is being considered."}], "ecg": {"findings": [{"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Irregularly irregular ventricular response with no consistent pattern", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "p_wave", "finding": "No discrete P waves; instead a fine, chaotic undulating baseline (fibrillatory waves), best seen in V1", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "rate", "finding": "Ventricular rate usually 100–160/min when untreated; may be normal or slow with rate-controlling drugs or conduction disease", "frequency": "common"}, {"feature": "qrs", "finding": "Narrow QRS unless there is a bundle branch block or pre-excitation", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "conduction", "finding": "Coarse or fine fibrillatory activity in V1; R-R intervals vary by more than 10%", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "Pre-excited AFib: irregular, very fast, wide-complex rhythm with varying QRS width (must-not-miss; avoid AV nodal blockers)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "Left ventricular hypertrophy or prior Q waves suggesting hypertensive or ischemic heart disease", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "qt", "finding": "QT interval may be prolonged by antiarrhythmic drugs; measure after rate control", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "st", "finding": "ST depression or T-wave inversion from demand ischemia during rapid rates", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"feature": "other", "finding": "Complete heart block with a regular slow escape rhythm argues against AFib as the sole rhythm", "frequency": "rare"}]}, "imaging": [{"study": "Transthoracic echocardiogram", "modality": "echo", "findings": [{"text": "Left atrial enlargement", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Left ventricular hypertrophy from hypertension", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Reduced left ventricular ejection fraction (heart failure)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Mitral stenosis or significant mitral regurgitation", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Left atrial thrombus (rare on TTE; better seen on TEE)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Normal study", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Transesophageal echocardiogram", "modality": "echo", "preferred_when": "Before cardioversion when the duration of AFib is over 48 hours or unknown, or when anticoagulation has been inadequate", "findings": [{"text": "Left atrial appendage thrombus", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Spontaneous echo contrast (smoke) in the left atrium", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "No thrombus, allowing cardioversion", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "findings": [{"text": "Enlarged cardiac silhouette", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pulmonary venous congestion or edema when heart failure is present", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Normal study", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "CT head without contrast", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "New focal neurologic deficit or altered mental status", "findings": [{"text": "No acute hemorrhage (allows consideration of anticoagulation)", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Hypodense area in a vascular territory consistent with ischemic stroke", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Intracranial hemorrhage", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "Cardiac CT or MRI", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Planning catheter ablation or when echocardiography is inconclusive", "findings": [{"text": "Left atrial and pulmonary vein anatomy for ablation planning", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Left atrial appendage thrombus", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "ECG", "why": "Confirms the diagnosis by showing an irregularly irregular rhythm without P waves"}, {"test": "cbc", "why": "Anemia, infection, or thrombocytopenia affecting anticoagulation"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Potassium, magnesium-related electrolytes, and kidney function for drug dosing"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Reversible cause; hyperthyroidism must be excluded"}, {"test": "hs_tnt", "why": "Looks for acute coronary syndrome or demand ischemia with rapid rates"}, {"test": "bnp", "why": "Assesses for heart failure as a cause or consequence"}, {"test": "coag", "why": "Baseline INR/aPTT before starting anticoagulation"}, {"test": "Chest x-ray", "why": "Heart size and pulmonary congestion", "only_if": "dyspnea, heart failure signs, or suspected pulmonary disease"}, {"test": "Transthoracic echocardiogram", "why": "Evaluates chamber size, valves, and ejection fraction; guides anticoagulation and rhythm strategy"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "Holter monitor", "why": "Captures paroxysmal AFib when the resting ECG is normal", "only_if": "symptoms are intermittent and the ECG does not show AFib"}, {"test": "event monitor", "why": "Longer monitoring for infrequent symptoms", "only_if": "symptoms occur less than once a day"}], "supporting": [{"test": "Transesophageal echocardiogram", "why": "Rules out left atrial thrombus before cardioversion", "only_if": "AFib duration over 48 hours or unknown, or anticoagulation inadequate"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Diabetes adds to stroke risk and guides risk factor control"}, {"test": "lipids", "why": "Vascular risk reduction"}, {"test": "mg", "why": "Corrects magnesium before rate or rhythm control"}, {"test": "CT head without contrast", "why": "Evaluates for stroke or hemorrhage", "only_if": "new focal neurologic deficit or altered mental status"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "d_dimer", "why": "No role in diagnosing AFib; only if pulmonary embolism is suspected"}, {"test": "lipase", "why": "Not needed unless abdominal pain suggests pancreatitis"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "No role unless urinary infection is suspected as a trigger"}, {"test": "csf", "why": "Not indicated for AFib; only if meningitis or subarachnoid hemorrhage is suspected"}, {"test": "procalcitonin", "why": "Not indicated unless sepsis is suspected as a trigger"}, {"test": "Cardiac CT or MRI", "why": "Not part of routine workup; reserved for ablation planning", "only_if": "catheter ablation is being planned"}], "decision_points": ["Confirm AFib on ECG before starting treatment; if paroxysmal and not captured, use ambulatory monitoring", "Check TSH in every new diagnosis to exclude hyperthyroidism", "Assess stroke risk with CHA2DS2-VASc and bleeding risk with HAS-BLED before starting anticoagulation", "If duration over 48 hours or unknown, anticoagulate for at least 3 weeks or perform TEE before cardioversion", "In pre-excited AFib with a wide, fast, irregular rhythm, avoid AV nodal blockers and use electrical cardioversion", "Unstable patients (hypotension, ischemia, pulmonary edema, altered mental status) get urgent synchronized cardioversion"], "criteria": [{"name": "CHA2DS2-VASc stroke risk", "summary": "Assigns points for heart failure, hypertension, age 75 or older, diabetes, prior stroke or transient ischemic attack, vascular disease, age 65–74, and female sex. Higher scores mean higher yearly stroke risk and support anticoagulation.", "items": ["Heart failure", "Hypertension", "Age 75 or older", "Diabetes", "Prior stroke or TIA", "Vascular disease", "Age 65–74", "Female sex"]}, {"name": "HAS-BLED bleeding risk", "summary": "Estimates major bleeding risk on anticoagulation using hypertension, abnormal kidney or liver function, stroke, bleeding history, labile INR, age over 65, and drugs or alcohol. High scores prompt closer monitoring rather than withholding anticoagulation.", "items": ["Hypertension", "Abnormal renal or liver function", "Stroke", "Bleeding history or predisposition", "Labile INR", "Age over 65", "Drugs or alcohol"]}], "scores": ["cha2ds2_vasc", "has_bled"]}, "differential": [{"name": "Atrial flutter", "slug": "atrial-flutter", "why_considered": "Also causes a fast, irregular-feeling heartbeat in older patients with the same risk factors, and often coexists with atrial fibrillation.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Palpitations that feel rapid and steady rather than chaotic", "Often paroxysmal with abrupt onset and offset"], "exam": ["Pulse may be regular when the conduction ratio is fixed, or irregular when it varies", "Similar fatigue and dyspnea"], "ecg": ["Sawtooth flutter waves at about 300/min, best seen in II, III, aVF and V1", "Ventricular rate often close to 150/min (2:1 conduction)", "Regular atrial activity rather than a chaotic fibrillatory baseline"]}}, {"name": "Multifocal atrial tachycardia", "slug": "multifocal-atrial-tachycardia", "why_considered": "Irregular tachycardia in older patients with chronic lung disease, a group that also develops atrial fibrillation.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Severe COPD or another chronic lung disease", "Recent respiratory infection or theophylline use"], "exam": ["Tachycardia with an irregular pulse", "Signs of lung disease such as wheezing or prolonged expiration"], "ecg": ["Discrete P waves of at least three different morphologies", "Rate over 100/min with varying P-P, P-R, and R-R intervals", "P waves are present, unlike atrial fibrillation"]}}, {"name": "Sinus tachycardia", "slug": "sinus-tachycardia", "why_considered": "Fast heartbeat with palpitations and dyspnea, and a common response to fever, pain, anemia, or dehydration.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Gradual onset and offset rather than sudden", "Identifiable trigger such as fever, pain, exercise, or blood loss"], "exam": ["Regular pulse and regular heart sounds", "Signs of the underlying cause such as fever or pallor"], "ecg": ["Regular rhythm with a consistent P wave before every QRS", "Rate typically under 150/min and varies with the trigger"]}}, {"name": "Supraventricular tachycardia (AV nodal reentrant)", "slug": "supraventricular-tachycardia", "why_considered": "Sudden-onset rapid palpitations in a patient without structural heart disease.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Abrupt onset and abrupt termination, often with a single triggering event", "Younger age and prior similar episodes"], "exam": ["Regular, rapid pulse", "No pulse deficit"], "ecg": ["Regular narrow-complex tachycardia at 150–250/min", "P waves hidden in or just after the QRS", "Regular R-R intervals"]}}, {"name": "Ventricular tachycardia", "slug": "ventricular-tachycardia", "why_considered": "Fast rhythm causing palpitations, dyspnea, and hypotension, and can be mistaken for a rapid irregular rhythm on a monitor.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Wide-complex tachycardia, especially with known coronary disease or heart failure, or any tachycardia with hemodynamic collapse", "discriminators": {"history": ["Prior myocardial infarction or cardiomyopathy", "Syncope or near-syncope at onset"], "exam": ["May be hemodynamically unstable with hypotension or altered mental status", "Cannon A waves in the neck from AV dissociation"], "ecg": ["Wide QRS over 120 ms with a regular or slightly irregular rhythm", "AV dissociation with occasional capture or fusion beats", "No fibrillatory baseline"]}}, {"name": "Wolff-Parkinson-White with pre-excited atrial fibrillation", "slug": "wolff-parkinson-white", "why_considered": "Irregular, very fast tachycardia that can be fatal if AV nodal blockers are given.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Irregular wide-complex tachycardia faster than 200/min, especially in a younger patient", "discriminators": {"history": ["Prior episodes of rapid palpitations since youth", "Family history of sudden cardiac death"], "exam": ["Very fast, irregular pulse with hemodynamic compromise", "May have hypotension or syncope"], "ecg": ["Irregularly irregular, wide-complex tachycardia with varying QRS width", "Delta wave and short PR interval on a baseline ECG in sinus rhythm"]}}, {"name": "Atrial fibrillation with aberrancy or bundle branch block", "why_considered": "Irregular rhythm with wide QRS that can be confused with ventricular tachycardia.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Known prior bundle branch block", "Similar appearance on prior ECGs"], "ecg": ["Irregularly irregular rhythm with a consistent wide QRS morphology", "No AV dissociation", "Fibrillatory baseline in V1"]}}, {"name": "Sick sinus syndrome with tachy-brady episodes", "slug": "sick-sinus-syndrome", "why_considered": "Older patients with palpitations alternating with dizziness or syncope, and it frequently coexists with atrial fibrillation.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Alternating fast and slow heart rates", "Syncope or near-syncope between episodes"], "ecg": ["Sinus bradycardia, sinus pauses, or sinoatrial exit block between episodes of tachycardia", "P waves present during slow periods"]}}, {"name": "Anxiety or panic attack", "slug": "panic-disorder", "why_considered": "Palpitations, chest discomfort, and breathlessness in a patient with a racing heartbeat.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Episodes tied to stress or specific situations", "Fear of dying or losing control during episodes", "Symptoms resolve with calming"], "exam": ["Regular pulse with normal rate between episodes", "No pulse deficit or irregular heart sounds"], "ecg": ["Normal sinus rhythm", "No fibrillatory waves"]}}, {"name": "Hyperthyroidism", "slug": "hyperthyroidism", "why_considered": "A reversible cause of palpitations, tachycardia, and atrial fibrillation itself.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Heat intolerance, weight loss, tremor, diarrhea", "Neck swelling or prior thyroid disease"], "exam": ["Diffuse goiter, tremor, warm moist skin, lid lag", "Tachycardia that may be regular"], "labs": ["Low TSH with elevated free T4 or T3"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Paroxysmal or persistent AFib with a controlled rate, no or minimal symptoms, hemodynamically stable, no heart failure", "moderate": "Symptomatic with fatigue, dyspnea on exertion, or palpitations; rate 90–140/min; may have mild pulmonary congestion or lower extremity edema", "severe": "Rapid ventricular response 120–170/min with dyspnea at rest, pulmonary crackles, elevated JVP, hypotension, or new heart failure decompensation", "critical": "Hemodynamic instability with hypotension, altered mental status, shock, pulmonary edema, or acute coronary ischemia; also includes pre-excited AFib with a very fast wide-complex rhythm"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Hypotension or systolic blood pressure under 90 mmHg", "meaning": "Poor perfusion from the rapid rate; needs urgent synchronized cardioversion"}, {"finding": "Altered mental status or confusion", "meaning": "Cerebral hypoperfusion or embolic stroke; urgent evaluation"}, {"finding": "Chest pain with ST changes on ECG", "meaning": "Demand ischemia or acute coronary syndrome; urgent cardiology involvement"}, {"finding": "Acute pulmonary edema with crackles and hypoxia", "meaning": "Rate-related heart failure; needs urgent rate control or cardioversion"}, {"finding": "Irregular wide-complex tachycardia faster than 200/min", "meaning": "Pre-excited AFib; avoid AV nodal blockers and cardiovert"}, {"finding": "New focal neurologic deficit or speech difficulty", "meaning": "Cardioembolic stroke; activate stroke pathway and obtain urgent head imaging"}, {"finding": "Syncope", "meaning": "Severe hypoperfusion or another arrhythmia such as ventricular tachycardia"}], "complications": [{"name": "Cardioembolic stroke", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Sudden focal weakness, numbness, or speech difficulty", "No anticoagulation or subtherapeutic anticoagulation", "High CHA2DS2-VASc score"]}, {"name": "Heart failure from tachycardia-mediated cardiomyopathy", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Weeks to months of uncontrolled rapid rates", "Progressive dyspnea, edema, and reduced ejection fraction", "Improves with rate or rhythm control"]}, {"name": "Systemic arterial embolism", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Sudden limb pain, pallor, or pulselessness", "Acute abdominal pain from mesenteric ischemia", "Left atrial thrombus on echocardiography"]}, {"name": "Acute decompensated heart failure", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Rapid ventricular rate with crackles, orthopnea, and elevated JVP", "Hypoxia and increased work of breathing"]}, {"name": "Sudden cardiac arrest", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Collapse with no pulse", "Pre-excited AFib degenerating to ventricular fibrillation", "Severe underlying structural heart disease"]}, {"name": "Bleeding from anticoagulation", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Melena, hematuria, or unexplained bruising", "High HAS-BLED score", "Supratherapeutic INR or recent NSAID use"]}, {"name": "Cognitive impairment and dementia", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Progressive memory difficulty over years", "Silent cerebral infarcts on imaging", "Long-standing or inadequately treated AFib"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Often present with fatigue, falls, or confusion rather than palpitations; higher stroke risk and higher bleeding risk, so anticoagulation decisions need careful weighing."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "AFib is uncommon in pregnancy; when present, evaluate for structural heart disease and hyperthyroidism. Rate control and anticoagulation choices must account for fetal safety, and anticoagulation is usually with heparin rather than warfarin."}, {"population": "renal_impairment", "differences": "Kidney function determines dosing of anticoagulants such as apixaban, rivaroxaban, and dabigatran; direct oral anticoagulants may be contraindicated in advanced kidney disease, and warfarin may be preferred."}, {"population": "hepatic_impairment", "differences": "Coagulopathy and impaired drug metabolism increase bleeding risk; anticoagulant choice and dose need adjustment, and HAS-BLED scores are higher."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Obesity is a modifiable risk factor; weight loss reduces AFib burden. Direct oral anticoagulant dosing may need adjustment at higher body weights."}, {"population": "diabetes", "differences": "Diabetes adds to stroke risk and is part of the CHA2DS2-VASc score; glucose control is part of overall risk reduction."}, {"population": "children", "differences": "AFib is rare in children and usually occurs with congenital heart disease, after cardiac surgery, or with hyperthyroidism; management focuses on the underlying cause."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "What does the racing or fluttering feel like, and did it start suddenly?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Fast, chaotic, fluttering or pounding heartbeat with abrupt onset, unlike a steady rapid beat"}, {"question": "When did this episode start, and how long has it lasted?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Duration matters: over 48 hours or unknown duration changes cardioversion planning"}, {"question": "Has this happened before, and how did those episodes end?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Paroxysmal pattern that stops on its own versus persistent rhythm; prior episodes and prior cardioversions"}, {"question": "What were you doing when it started?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Onset at rest or at night is typical; exertion or alcohol as a trigger"}, {"question": "How much alcohol do you drink, and how often?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Heavy or binge drinking is a strong, modifiable trigger"}, {"question": "Do you use cocaine, methamphetamine, or other stimulants?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Stimulant use as a precipitant"}, {"question": "Do you have chest pain, and is it pressure that comes with exertion?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Exertional pressure radiating to arm or jaw suggests ischemia rather than AFib alone"}, {"question": "Have you fainted or nearly fainted?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Syncope or near-syncope suggests severe hypoperfusion or another arrhythmia"}, {"question": "Any sudden weakness on one side, trouble speaking, or vision loss?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Cardioembolic stroke; activates the stroke pathway"}, {"question": "Are you more short of breath lying flat, or do you wake up at night gasping?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Orthopnea or paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea suggests heart failure"}, {"question": "Have your ankles or legs been swelling?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Volume overload from heart failure"}, {"question": "How is your energy level compared with a few months ago?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Fatigue is the most common symptom and may be the only one"}, {"question": "Do you have high blood pressure, heart failure, valve disease, diabetes, or sleep apnea?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Conditions that cause AFib and add to stroke risk"}, {"question": "Have you ever had a stroke, TIA, or a blood clot?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Prior stroke or TIA strongly raises stroke risk and pushes toward anticoagulation"}, {"question": "Have you had heart, lung, or esophageal surgery recently?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Recent cardiothoracic surgery is a common trigger in the early postoperative weeks"}, {"question": "What medications do you take, including over-the-counter ones?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Thyroid hormone, albuterol, pseudoephedrine, and diuretics that lower potassium or magnesium"}, {"question": "Do you take any blood thinners, aspirin, or NSAIDs?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Current anticoagulation status and bleeding risk before starting therapy"}, {"question": "Have you ever had bleeding problems, ulcers, or a fall with a head injury?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Bleeding history that affects anticoagulant choice"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have atrial fibrillation or early heart disease?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Family history of AFib or early heart disease"}, {"question": "Do you smoke, and have you ever smoked?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Tobacco use as a vascular risk factor"}, {"question": "Any fever, cough, or recent infection?", "category": "ros", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Acute illness or infection as a precipitant"}], "accepted_names": ["Atrial fibrillation", "AFib", "AF", "A-fib"], "reasoning_points": ["Palpitations with an irregularly irregular pulse and variable heart sounds", "ECG shows no discrete P waves with a chaotic fibrillatory baseline and irregular R-R intervals", "Symptoms of fatigue, exertional dyspnea, or lightheadedness consistent with loss of atrial kick", "Risk factors such as age over 65, hypertension, heart failure, or valvular disease", "Hyperthyroidism excluded with TSH as a reversible cause", "Stroke risk assessed with CHA2DS2-VASc and bleeding risk with HAS-BLED before anticoagulation", "Hemodynamic stability assessed; instability requires urgent synchronized cardioversion", "Duration over 48 hours or unknown requires anticoagulation or TEE before cardioversion"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Older adult with hypertension and classic palpitations", "Irregularly irregular pulse with a pulse deficit", "ECG with no P waves and chaotic baseline", "Symptoms of fatigue and exertional dyspnea"], "medium": ["Paroxysmal AFib with a normal ECG in the office; needs ambulatory monitoring", "Patient presenting with fatigue or falls rather than palpitations", "AFib with a controlled rate and few symptoms found incidentally", "Coexisting heart failure where it is unclear which came first"], "hard": ["Pre-excited AFib with a fast, irregular wide-complex rhythm where AV nodal blockers must be avoided", "AFib with aberrancy mistaken for ventricular tachycardia", "Hyperthyroidism as the reversible driver", "Postoperative AFib after cardiothoracic surgery", "Patient on anticoagulation presenting with a cardioembolic stroke"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
