{"text": "No acute fracture or dislocation", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Degenerative joint changes (osteophytes, joint space narrowing) if coexisting osteoarthritis", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Calcification within the bursa", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "Ultrasound of the affected bursa", "modality": "ultrasound", "preferred_when": "When the diagnosis is uncertain or aspiration is planned", "findings": [{"text": "Distended bursa with fluid and thickened synovial wall", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Increased Doppler flow in the bursal wall (hyperemia)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Guidance for diagnostic or therapeutic aspiration", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "MRI of the affected joint", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Persistent symptoms despite treatment or suspicion of a deeper process", "findings": [{"text": "Bursal fluid collection with surrounding soft tissue edema", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Bursal wall thickening and enhancement", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Associated tendon or muscle abnormality", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "X-ray of the affected joint", "why": "Rules out fracture, dislocation, or advanced arthritis and shows soft tissue swelling"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Baseline inflammatory marker; helps screen for septic bursitis", "only_if": "fever, marked warmth, or concern for infection"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "Adds to CRP when infection or inflammatory arthritis is considered", "only_if": "fever, marked warmth, or concern for infection"}, {"test": "cbc", "why": "Leukocytosis supports septic bursitis", "only_if": "fever, systemic symptoms, or concern for infection"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "Bursal aspiration with cell count, Gram stain, and culture", "why": "Distinguishes aseptic from septic bursitis and identifies the organism", "only_if": "Distinguishes aseptic from septic bursitis and identifies the organism"}], "supporting": [{"test"