, "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "ulcer-size", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Estimate the diameter of the ulcer relative to a known reference (e.g., millimeters on a tongue blade)", "finding": "Most ulcers are small (under 1 cm); larger ulcers over 1 cm suggest major aphthous ulcers or another cause", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "ulcer-tenderness", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Gently palpate the ulcer and surrounding mucosa with a gloved finger or cotton swab", "finding": "Marked tenderness of the ulcer and surrounding mucosa; the ulcer is soft and not indurated", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-vesicles", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the oral mucosa for vesicles, bullae or intact blisters", "finding": "No vesicles or intact blisters; lesions are ulcers from the start", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-gingival-involvement", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the gingiva and hard palate", "finding": "Gingiva and hard palate are spared; lesions are on movable mucosa", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-perioral-lesions", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the lips, perioral skin and vermilion border", "finding": "No crusted vesicles or erosions on the outer lips or around the mouth", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "cervical-lymphadenopathy", "region": "lymph", "maneuver": "Palpate the cervical lymph node chains bilaterally", "finding": "Mildly tender, mobile cervical lymphadenopathy", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-fever", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Measure temperature and assess for