r heavy alcohol use raises concern for oral squamous cell carcinoma, especially with a nonhealing ulcer"}, {"question": "Has this ulcer lasted more than three weeks, or does it feel hard or raised?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "An ulcer persisting beyond 3 weeks or with indurated, rolled edges needs biopsy to exclude malignancy"}], "accepted_names": ["Canker sores", "Canker sore", "Aphthous ulcers", "Aphthous ulcer", "Recurrent aphthous stomatitis", "Recurrent aphthous ulcers", "Aphthous stomatitis", "RAS"], "reasoning_points": ["Recurrent crops of painful shallow oral ulcers on movable mucosa, each lasting about 7–14 days and healing without scarring", "A gray-white or yellow fibrinous center with an erythematous halo, without vesicles or blisters", "Sparing of the gingiva, hard palate and outer lips, which argues against herpes simplex", "No fever, systemic symptoms, genital ulcers, eye inflammation, skin rash or GI symptoms to suggest Behçet syndrome, inflammatory bowel disease or infection", "No new culprit medication such as an NSAID, methotrexate or nicorandil", "Nutritional screen for iron, folate and vitamin B12 deficiency as treatable contributors", "An ulcer persisting beyond 3 weeks, indurated, or nonhealing requires biopsy to exclude malignancy"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Young adult with a long history of recurrent small painful mouth ulcers", "Classic shallow ulcer with a gray-white center and red halo on the buccal mucosa or inside the lip", "No fever, no systemic symptoms, no genital or eye involvement", "Heals without scarring in under two weeks"], "medium": ["Child who cannot describe the sore and presents with crying, drooling and refusal to eat", "Patient with several ulcers at once and tender cervical lymph nodes", "Patient with a history of iron-deficiency anemia or heavy menstrual bleeding", "Ulcer triggered by recent dental work, braces or a new toothpaste"], "hard": ["Older adult with a new, nonhealing 