ase when vomiting, anxiety, or tachycardia is prominent."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "almost_always", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Negative. Required in anyone who could be pregnant before attributing nausea and vomiting to cannabis."}, {"test_id": "lipase", "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Ordered when epigastric pain is prominent to exclude pancreatitis."}], "ecg": {"findings": [{"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Sinus tachycardia", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate"}, {"feature": "rate", "finding": "Normal sinus rhythm at 60–100 bpm", "frequency": "common"}, {"feature": "qt", "finding": "Normal QT interval", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "conduction", "finding": "Normal PR and QRS intervals without block", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "st", "finding": "No ST elevation or depression", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"feature": "t_wave", "finding": "No T-wave inversion", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, "imaging": [{"study": "Abdominal x-ray", "modality": "xray", "findings": [{"text": "Usually normal; no dilated loops or free air", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, {"study": "CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Severe or atypical abdominal pain, or when another cause is suspected", "findings": [{"text": "No bowel obstruction, perforation, or inflammatory mass", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Gastric distension or air-fluid levels from vomiting", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Ultrasound of the right upper quadrant", "modality": "ultrasound", "preferred_when": "Epigastric or right upper quadrant pain to exclude biliary disease", "findings": [{"text": "No gallstones or gallbladder wall thickening", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "hcg", "why": "Rules out pregnancy before attributing nausea and vomiting to cannabis"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Assesses dehydration, electrolyte losses, and 