 flick sign", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Neck pain", "Radicular symptoms in the lower extremities", "Bowel or bladder dysfunction", "Visual changes", "Headaches"], "argues_against": ["Cervical radiculopathy", "Multiple sclerosis", "Stroke"]}, {"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Dry skin on the fingers", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Rash", "Ulcers", "Color changes in the fingers (Raynaud's)"], "argues_against": ["Vasculitis", "Raynaud's phenomenon"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Fever", "Weight loss", "Night sweats", "Fatigue"], "argues_against": ["Systemic inflammatory or infectious process"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Symptoms often begin in the second or third trimester and are frequently bilateral; they typically resolve after delivery.", "missing_classic_features": ["Gradual onset over months", "Unilateral dominant hand involvement"]}, {"population": "diabetes", "how_it_differs": "Symptoms may be attributed to diabetic peripheral neuropathy, and the distribution may be less clear; carpal tunnel syndrome is more common and can be more severe.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear median nerve distribution", "Nocturnal predominance"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "May present with more constant numbness and thenar muscle wasting rather than intermittent tingling; pain may be less prominent.", "missing_classic_features": ["Intermittent nocturnal symptoms", "Pain"]}, {"population": "obesity", "how_it_differs": "Higher risk and often more severe symptoms; may be bilateral and less responsive to conservative treatment.", "missing_classic_features": ["Unilateral symptoms"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable, no distress; hand exam findings are subtle", "moderate": "Comfortable at rest; winces or shakes the hand when symptoms are provoked during testing", "severe": "Frequent shaking or flicking of the hand; may have visible clumsiness handling objects", "critical": "Marked thenar wasting with poor hand function; may be unable to perform fine motor tasks"}, "findings": [{"id": "median-distribution-sensory-loss", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Test light touch and pinprick over the palmar surfaces of the thumb, index, middle, and ring fingers, and compare with the little finger", "finding": "Decreased sensation in the median nerve distribution (thumb, index, middle, and radial half of the ring finger) with sparing of the little finger", "frequency": "common", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "tinel-sign", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Tap lightly over the carpal tunnel at the volar wrist crease", "finding": "Tingling or electric shock-like sensation radiating into the median-innervated fingers", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "phalen-sign", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Ask the patient to hold both wrists in full flexion (or press the dorsal surfaces of the hands together) for up to 60 seconds", "finding": "Numbness or tingling in the median nerve distribution within 60 seconds", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "thenar-wasting", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Inspect the thenar eminence and compare both hands", "finding": "Flattening or atrophy of the thenar muscles", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "thumb-abduction-weakness", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Ask the patient to abduct the thumb against resistance (or oppose the thumb to the little finger against resistance)", "finding": "Weak thumb abduction/opposition", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "flick-sign", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Ask the patient what they do when symptoms wake t