ian nerve distribution", "discriminators": {"history": ["Neck pain or stiffness", "Symptoms radiate from the neck down the arm in a dermatomal pattern", "Symptoms worsened by neck extension or rotation", "No nocturnal predominance"], "exam": ["Positive Spurling maneuver reproducing arm symptoms", "Decreased biceps or triceps reflex", "Dermatomal sensory loss that may include the little finger or forearm", "Normal Tinel and Phalen tests"], "imaging": ["MRI of the cervical spine showing nerve root compression", "Cervical spine x-ray showing degenerative changes or foraminal narrowing"]}}, {"name": "Diabetic peripheral neuropathy", "slug": "diabetic-peripheral-neuropathy", "why_considered": "Diabetes is a common comorbidity and cause of hand numbness and tingling", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Known diabetes with symmetric numbness, or symptoms extending beyond the median nerve distribution", "discriminators": {"history": ["Long-standing diabetes", "Symmetric stocking-and-glove numbness", "Symptoms in the feet as well as the hands", "No clear nocturnal predominance or flick sign"], "exam": ["Symmetric sensory loss in a stocking-and-glove pattern", "Reduced vibration and pinprick sensation in the feet", "Reduced ankle reflexes", "Tinel and Phalen tests may be negative"], "labs": ["Elevated A1c or fasting glucose", "Nerve conduction studies showing a symmetric, length-dependent polyneuropathy rather than focal median nerve compression"]}}, {"name": "Ulnar neuropathy at the elbow (cubital tunnel syndrome)", "slug": "ulnar-neuropathy", "why_considered": "Another common entrapment neuropathy causing hand numbness and weakness", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Numbness in the little finger and ulnar half of the ring finger", "Symptoms worse with elbow flexion or leaning on the elbow"], "exam": ["Sensory loss in the ulnar distribution including the little finger", "Weak finger abduction or a positive Froment sign", "Tinel sign at the elbow rather