 "Median neuropathy at the wrist"], "reasoning_points": ["Numbness and tingling in the median nerve distribution (thumb, index, middle, and radial half of the ring finger) with sparing of the little finger", "Nocturnal predominance, often waking the patient from sleep, worse with the wrists flexed", "Relief by shaking or flicking the hand (flick sign)", "Positive Tinel or Phalen test on exam", "Sensory loss in the median distribution and, in more advanced disease, thenar wasting or weak thumb abduction", "Symptoms and signs confined to the median nerve, with a normal cervical spine exam and normal ulnar nerve function", "Contributing conditions considered, such as diabetes, hypothyroidism, pregnancy, obesity, rheumatoid arthritis, or prior wrist injury", "Nerve conduction studies confirm focal median nerve compression at the wrist and grade severity when the diagnosis is uncertain or surgery is considered"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Middle-aged woman with classic nocturnal median-distribution numbness and tingling", "Symptoms wake her from sleep and she shakes her hand to relieve them", "Positive Tinel and Phalen tests", "Little finger spared"], "medium": ["Bilateral symptoms in a pregnant patient in the third trimester", "Patient with diabetes whose hand numbness is attributed to peripheral neuropathy", "Mild symptoms with normal sensation on exam and no weakness", "Symptoms provoked by driving or holding a phone rather than only at night"], "hard": ["Older adult with constant numbness and thenar wasting rather than intermittent tingling", "Patient with neck pain and paresthesias that extend beyond the median distribution (cervical radiculopathy)", "Symptoms in a patient with known hypothyroidism or rheumatoid arthritis, where the underlying condition must also be addressed", "Atypical presentation with forearm radiation and no clear nocturnal pattern"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
