onary or other cardiopulmonary causes", "Men tend to present with chest pain from coronary causes at younger ages than women"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Coronary artery disease or prior myocardial infarction", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Hypertension", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Hyperlipidemia", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Current or recent tobacco smoking", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Family history of premature coronary artery disease", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Recent immobilization, surgery, or long travel (venous thromboembolism risk)", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Known gastroesophageal reflux disease", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Recent heavy lifting or new strenuous exercise", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Recent viral illness with coughing", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Coronary artery disease", "Heart failure", "Atrial fibrillation", "Diabetes mellitus", "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease", "Gastroesophageal reflux disease", "Anxiety or panic disorder", "Prior venous thromboembolism"], "family_history": ["Premature coronary artery disease in a first-degree relative", "Sudden cardiac death in a first-degree relative", "Venous thromboembolism in a first-degree relative"], "social_history": ["Tobacco use", "Alcohol use", "Cocaine or stimulant use", "Sedentary lifestyle", "Occupational or recreational heavy lifting"], "exposures": ["Recent long-distance travel", "Recent surgery or hospitalization", "Recent immobilization or cast", "Sick contacts with respiratory illness"], "risk_medications": ["estrogen-containing contraceptives", "hormone replacement therapy", "cocaine", "amphetamines", "triptans", "nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs", "chemotherapy agents"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I have pain in my chest", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "It feels like pressure or tightness in the middle of my chest", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "The pain gets worse when I breathe in or lie down", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "I feel like I can't catch my breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Varies by cause: sudden and maximal at onset suggests a vascular or pulmonary event, while gradual onset over minutes to hours is more typical of coronary or gastrointestinal causes", "duration": "From minutes to weeks depending on cause; cardiac pain often lasts minutes to tens of minutes, while musculoskeletal and gastrointestinal pain can persist for days", "progression": "May be constant, intermittent, or crescendo; pain that is worsening or occurring at rest is concerning for an acute coronary syndrome", "location": "Often substernal or left-sided, but can be anywhere in the chest, epigastrium, back, or shoulders", "radiation": "May radiate to the left arm, both arms, jaw, neck, back, or epigastrium", "quality": "Described as pressure, tightness, squeezing, heaviness, burning, sharp, or tearing depending on the cause", "severity": "Ranges from mild discomfort to severe; severity alone does not distinguish dangerous from benign causes", "timing": "May be exertional, postprandial, positional, pleuritic, or constant", "aggravating": ["Exertion", "Emotional stress", "Deep breathing", "Coughing", "Lying flat", "Pressing on the chest wall", "Eating a large meal"], "relieving": ["Rest", "Nitroglycerin", "Sitting upright or leaning forward", "Antacids", "Analgesics"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Shortness of breath", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Sweating", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nausea or vomiting", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Lightheadedness or dizziness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Palpitations", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Heartburn or sour taste in the mouth", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Cough", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pain worsened by movement or breathing", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Fever", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Coughing up blood", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Fainting", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Tearing pain radiating to the back", "Pain that is maximal at the very first instant", "Coughing up blood", "Unilateral leg swelling or calf pain", "Recent long travel or immobilization", "Fever with productive cough", "Pain reproduced only by pressing on the chest wall", "Symptoms that resolve completely with antacids"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Feeling sweaty or clammy", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Fatigue", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Feeling feverish", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Night sweats"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [{"text": "Palpitations", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pain brought on by exertion", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Leg swelling", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Fainting", "Known heart murmur", "Prior heart attack"], "argues_against": ["Pain that is purely positional and reproducible on chest wall palpation"]}, {"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Shortness of breath", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Cough", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pain worse with deep breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Coughing up blood", "Wheezing", "Recent pneumonia"], "argues_against": ["Pleuritic pain with clear lungs and no dyspnea"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Heartburn or acid regurgitation", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pain after meals or when lying down", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Vomiting blood", "Black or bloody stools", "Difficulty swallowing"], "argues_against": ["Pain clearly related to meals and relieved by antacids"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Pain reproduced by pressing on the chest", "frequency": "sometimes"},