 low glucose favors a viral cause over bacterial meningitis."}], "imaging": [{"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "preferred_when": "Adults or immunocompromised patients with respiratory symptoms", "findings": [{"text": "Diffuse bilateral reticulonodular or patchy alveolar opacities", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Normal chest x-ray despite symptoms (early disease)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pleural effusion", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "CT chest without contrast", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Suspected varicella pneumonia when chest x-ray is normal or equivocal", "findings": [{"text": "Diffuse bilateral ground-glass opacities", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Small nodular or micronodular opacities", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Mediastinal lymphadenopathy", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "CT head without contrast", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Altered mental status or focal neurologic deficit", "findings": [{"text": "Usually normal in uncomplicated varicella", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Hypodense lesions in the basal ganglia or cortex (vasculopathy, encephalitis)", "frequency": "rare"}]}, {"study": "MRI brain with and without contrast", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Suspected encephalitis, cerebellitis or vasculopathy", "findings": [{"text": "T2 hyperintensities in the cerebellum, basal ganglia or cortex", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Leptomeningeal enhancement", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Normal study", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "Assesses for leukocytosis suggesting bacterial superinfection or leukopenia in severe disease"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Checks hydration and electrolytes in patients with poor intake or vomiting"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Supports concern for bacterial superinfection when elevated", "only_if": "bacterial superinfection is suspected"}, {"test": "Chest x-ray", "why": "Evaluates for varicella pneumonia", 