ociated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Mild prodrome 1 to 2 days before the rash, especially in adults; in children the rash is often first"}, {"question": "Have you had chickenpox before, or have you received the chickenpox vaccine?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "No prior chickenpox and no or incomplete vaccination; prior disease makes chickenpox unlikely"}, {"question": "Has anyone around you had chickenpox, a similar rash, or shingles?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Close contact with chickenpox or shingles 10 to 21 days before the rash; household or school exposure"}, {"question": "Do you take any medicines that weaken the immune system, such as steroids or biologics?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Corticosteroids, methotrexate, biologics or other immunosuppressants, which raise the risk of severe disease"}, {"question": "Do you have any condition that weakens your immune system?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Leukemia, lymphoma, HIV, transplant or other immunocompromising condition"}, {"question": "Are you pregnant, or could you be pregnant?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Pregnancy without immunity, which raises the risk of severe varicella pneumonia and neonatal varicella"}, {"question": "Is it hard to breathe, or do you have chest pain or a cough?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Respiratory symptoms suggesting varicella pneumonia, especially in adults, pregnant or immunocompromised patients"}, {"question": "Any severe headache, stiff neck, confusion, seizures or trouble walking?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "CNS involvement such as encephalitis, cerebellitis or meningitis"}, {"question": "Are you able to drink, and are you urinating normally?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "important