ted INR", "Ultrasound shows a nodular liver with splenomegaly and ascites"], "medium": ["Patient with obesity and type 2 diabetes found to have abnormal liver tests and no alcohol history", "Compensated cirrhosis detected only by thrombocytopenia and mild transaminase elevation", "Ascites attributed to central adiposity, delaying recognition", "Older adult presenting with confusion or falls rather than abdominal swelling"], "hard": ["Cirrhosis masked by coexisting heart failure with edema and elevated jugular venous pressure", "Young patient with neuropsychiatric symptoms and hemolysis suggesting Wilson disease", "Patient presenting first with variceal bleeding or spontaneous bacterial peritonitis before cirrhosis is known", "Pregnant patient with pruritus and jaundice overlapping with intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy", "New focal liver lesion with rising alpha-fetoprotein suggesting hepatocellular carcinoma"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
