s are seropositive)", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Close contact with someone who has an active cold sore (kissing, sharing utensils, towels)", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Sun exposure or wind to the lips", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Physical or emotional stress, fatigue", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Fever or another concurrent illness", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Menstruation", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Recent dental work or lip trauma", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Atopic dermatitis (higher risk of eczema herpeticum)", "Immunosuppression from illness or medication"], "family_history": [], "social_history": ["Sharing drinks, utensils, or lip balm with others", "Contact sports such as wrestling"], "exposures": ["Contact with a person who has an active cold sore", "Sun or wind exposure"], "risk_medications": ["tacrolimus", "prednisone", "methotrexate", "cyclosporine", "azathioprine"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I get a tingling bump on my lip that turns into a sore", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "My lip is burning and it hurts", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I have a blister on my mouth", "frequency": "common"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Often begins with tingling, itching, or burning at the lip for a few hours to a day before a bump appears; first-ever episode may start with fever and mouth pain", "duration": "Sores crust and heal over 7–14 days; first episode may last up to 2–3 weeks", "progression": "Tingling or burning, then a small cluster of fluid-filled blisters, then crusting and healing without a scar", "location": "Usually on or around the outer lip, sometimes at the corner of the mouth or the nostril; inside the mouth on the gums or hard palate in a first episode", "radiation": "None", "quality": "Tender, burning, or stinging; the blisters are painful to touch", "severity": "Mild to moderate; uncomfortable but not disabling", "timing": "Recurrent episodes can be triggered by sun