ected side", "Tachycardia and tachypnea with hypoxemia on pulse oximetry", "Chest x-ray showing a visible pleural line with no lung markings peripheral to it, or patchy opacity with volume loss for atelectasis", "Tension pneumothorax considered and excluded when hypotension, distended neck veins, or tracheal deviation are present", "Pregnancy excluded before imaging when applicable", "Alternative diagnoses such as pulmonary embolism, acute coronary syndrome, and pneumonia considered and addressed"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Tall, thin young male smoker with sudden sharp one-sided chest pain and dyspnea", "Decreased breath sounds and hyperresonance on the affected side", "Chest x-ray clearly shows a pleural line with absent lung markings"], "medium": ["Older adult with COPD and milder pain but significant breathlessness", "Small pneumothorax with subtle exam findings and a less obvious pleural line on chest x-ray", "Postoperative patient with gradual dyspnea and focal decreased breath sounds due to atelectasis", "Woman of reproductive age with chest pain requiring pregnancy testing before imaging"], "hard": ["Tension pneumothorax with hypotension and distended neck veins requiring immediate decompression before imaging", "Patient on mechanical ventilation with sudden desaturation and rising airway pressures", "Chest x-ray equivocal or normal in a small anterior pneumothorax, requiring CT or ultrasound", "Pneumothorax mimicking acute coronary syndrome on ECG with ST changes", "Child or infant with vague chest or abdominal pain, irritability, and tachypnea without localizing findings"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
