st; positive result requires colonoscopy", "only_if": "screening is being done by a stool-based strategy rather than colonoscopy"}, {"test": "Cologuard", "why": "Multitarget stool DNA screening test; positive result requires colonoscopy", "only_if": "patient prefers a noninvasive screening test and is at average risk"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "ferritin", "why": "Confirms iron deficiency when anemia or low MCV is present"}, {"test": "iron", "why": "Supports iron deficiency anemia from chronic blood loss"}, {"test": "Ct colonography", "why": "Alternative structural evaluation when colonoscopy is incomplete or contraindicated", "only_if": "Alternative structural evaluation when colonoscopy is incomplete or contraindicated"}, {"test": "Flexible sigmoidoscopy", "why": "Evaluates the left colon when full colonoscopy is not available or not desired"}, {"test": "CEA", "why": "Not for polyp detection; may be sent if a malignant-appearing lesion is found", "only_if": "colonoscopy shows a suspicious mass or confirmed colorectal cancer"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "Ct colonography", "why": "Not first-line when colonoscopy is available; does not allow removal or biopsy"}, {"test": "Abdominal x-ray", "why": "Does not detect polyps and is not part of the workup"}, {"test": "Ct abdomen pelvis with contrast", "why": "Not a screening or diagnostic test for polyps; reserve for suspected complications"}, {"test": "CEA", "why": "Not a screening or diagnostic test for colonic polyps"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "No role in the evaluation of colonic polyps"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "No role in the evaluation of colonic polyps"}, {"test": "lipase", "why": "Not indicated for this presentation"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Not indicated for this presentation"}], "decision_points": ["Colonoscopy is both diagnostic and therapeutic: polyps are removed at the time of detection and sent for histology.", "A positive stool-based screening test (FIT or stool DNA) requires diagnostic