 screening colonoscopy", "Colonoscopy shows one or more discrete mucosal protrusions", "Polyps removed by snare polypectomy and sent for histology", "No anemia, no weight loss, no bowel habit change"], "medium": ["Intermittent bright red blood on toilet paper with a normal exam", "Positive FIT in an average-risk adult", "Mild iron deficiency anemia with no visible bleeding", "Multiple polyps found at colonoscopy"], "hard": ["Older adult with iron deficiency anemia and no GI symptoms", "Right-sided or flat/sessile polyp not seen on flexible sigmoidoscopy", "Patient with a strong family history suggesting a hereditary syndrome", "Large polyp requiring piecemeal resection or referral", "Post-polypectomy bleeding or perforation after colonoscopy"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
