ot explained by COPD itself."}, {"test_id": "eos_pct", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 3, "max": 6}, "severe": {"min": 4, "max": 8}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "A higher eosinophil count predicts a better response to inhaled corticosteroids."}, {"test_id": "hco3", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 26, "max": 30}, "severe": {"min": 28, "max": 34}, "critical": {"min": 30, "max": 38}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated bicarbonate is a compensatory response to chronic carbon dioxide retention; a normal bicarbonate does not exclude hypercapnia."}, {"test_id": "ph", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 7.35, "max": 7.45}, "moderate": {"min": 7.33, "max": 7.44}, "severe": {"min": 7.3, "max": 7.42}, "critical": {"min": 7.2, "max": 7.38}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Measured on arterial blood gas. Chronic retention is usually compensated with a near-normal pH; a low pH indicates acute-on-chronic respiratory failure."}, {"test_id": "paco2", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 42, "max": 50}, "severe": {"min": 48, "max": 60}, "critical": {"min": 55, "max": 80}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Measured on arterial blood gas. Rising PaCO2 with a falling pH signals impending respiratory failure and need for ventilatory support."}, {"test_id": "pao2", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 70, "max": 85}, "moderate": {"min": 55, "max": 75}, "severe": {"min": 45, "max": 65}, "critical": {"min": 35, "max": 55}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Measured on arterial blood gas. Hypoxemia is common in moderate to severe disease and worsens during exacerbations."}, {"test_id": "sao2", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 92, "max": 96}, "moderate": {"min": 88, "max": 93}, "severe": {"min": 82, "max": 90}, "critical": {"min": 70, "max": 86}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Measured on arterial blood gas; correlates with pulse oximetry b