ssue over the pressure point", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Underlying bony prominence, such as a prominent metatarsal head, bunion, or hammertoe, that explains the pressure point", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "No fracture, dislocation, or bone destruction", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, {"study": "MRI foot without contrast", "modality": "mri", "findings": [{"text": "Focal thickening of the epidermis and dermis over the pressure point with no soft tissue mass", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "No bone marrow edema, abscess, or soft tissue mass", "frequency": "almost_always"}]}, {"study": "Ultrasound of the foot", "modality": "ultrasound", "findings": [{"text": "Thickened hyperechoic epidermis over the lesion with no discrete mass or fluid collection", "frequency": "common"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "Focused skin and foot examination", "why": "Confirms the diagnosis by showing a well-circumscribed area of hyperkeratosis with preserved skin markings and no ulceration, drainage, or surrounding cellulitis"}, {"test": "Footwear and activity history", "why": "Identifies the pressure or friction source that must be removed for the lesion to resolve"}, {"test": "Foot x-ray", "why": "Looks for an underlying bony prominence or deformity that explains the pressure point", "only_if": "the lesion is atypical, recurrent, or a bony deformity is suspected"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "MRI foot without contrast", "why": "Distinguishes a corn or callus from a soft tissue mass, abscess, or bone infection", "only_if": "a deep mass, abscess, or osteomyelitis is suspected"}, {"test": "Ultrasound of the foot", "why": "Can confirm a thickened epidermis and exclude a fluid collection or mass when the diagnosis is uncertain", "only_if": "the diagnosis is uncertain or a fluid collection is suspected"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "No role in an uninfected pressure lesion; a normal white count does not change management"}, {"test": "