"Low with fat malabsorption and vitamin D deficiency; check the corrected calcium when albumin is low."}, {"test_id": "crp", "ranges": {"severe": {"min": 10.0, "max": 25.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "A very high CRP with fever and focal tenderness should prompt imaging for abscess."}, {"test_id": "procalcitonin", "ranges": {"severe": {"min": 0.5, "max": 2.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Not routinely needed; a high value favors bacterial infection or abscess over a Crohn's flare."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "almost_always", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Negative. Required in anyone who could be pregnant before imaging and before starting immunosuppressive therapy."}], "imaging": [{"study": "CT enterography", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Adults and older children; best for small bowel and extraluminal complications", "findings": [{"text": "Segmental bowel wall thickening with mural hyperenhancement (target sign)", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Mesenteric fat stranding and engorged vasa recta (comb sign)", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Skip lesions with normal bowel between involved segments", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Creeping fat and fibrofatty proliferation along the mesenteric border", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Stricture with upstream dilation suggesting obstruction", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Fistula tract or sinus between bowel loops, bladder, vagina or skin", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Abscess as a rim-enhancing fluid collection", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Mesenteric lymphadenopathy", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "MRI enterography", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Children, pregnancy, and when repeated imaging is expected (no ionizing radiation)", "findings": [{"text": "Segmental bowel wall thickening with increased T2 signal and enhancement", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Skip lesions", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Stricture, fistula or abscess", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Perianal fistula or abscess on pelvic sequences", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Colonoscopy with ileoscopy and biopsy", "modality": "endoscopy", "preferred_when": "First-line for tissue diagnosis in most patients", "findings": [{"text": "Patchy, discontinuous inflammation with skip areas", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Deep linear or serpiginous ulcers and aphthous erosions", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Cobblestone mucosa from intersecting ulcers and edema", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Terminal ileum involved with a normal-appearing cecum or right colon", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Rectal sparing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Stricture or stenosis that cannot be passed", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Perianal fistula or fissure seen on retroflexion", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Biopsies showing transmural inflammation, crypt architectural distortion and noncaseating granulomas", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "Upper endoscopy (EGD)", "modality": "endoscopy", "preferred_when": "Upper GI symptoms or suspected gastroduodenal involvement, especially in children", "findings": [{"text": "Gastric or duodenal aphthous ulcers and erythema", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Granulomas on biopsy", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Abdominal x-ray (supine and upright)", "modality": "xray", "preferred_when": "Suspected obstruction, perforation or toxic presentation", "findings": [{"text": "Dilated small bowel loops with air-fluid levels (obstruction)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Free air under the diaphragm (perforation)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Nonspecific bowel gas pattern", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "Pelvic MRI", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Perianal pain, drainage or suspected fistula", "findings": [{"text": "Fistula tract with its relationship to the sphincter complex", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Perianal or ischiorectal abscess", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Horseshoe extension or secondary tracts", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Small bowel follow-through (upper GI series with barium)", "modality": "xray", "preferred_when": "When CT or MR enterography is unavailable", "findings": [{"text": "Segmental narrowing with a string sign", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Cobblestone appearance and separation of loops", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "Anemia, leukocytosis and reactive thrombocytosis support chronic inflammation and blood loss"}, {"test": "cmp_extra", "why": "Albumin, liver enzymes and electrolytes; low albumin marks severe disease"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Baseline inflammatory marker to follow activity"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "Second inflammatory marker; often elevated in Crohn's"}, {"test": "Stool culture", "why": "Excludes bacterial colitis before attributing symptoms to Crohn's"}, {"test": "Stool ova and parasites", "why": "Excludes parasitic infection, especially with travel or exposure"}, {"test": "C. difficile stool toxin/PCR", "why": "Excludes C. difficile, which can mimic or complicate a flare"}, {"test": "Fecal calprotectin", "why": "Distinguishes inflammatory diarrhea from irritable bowel syndrome"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Rules out pregnancy before imaging and immunosuppression", "only_if": "patient could be pregnant"}, {"test": "CT enterography", "why": "Defines extent, skip lesions and complications such as stricture, fistula or abscess", "only_if": "suspected complication or need to map small bowel"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "Colonoscopy with ileoscopy and biopsy", "why": "Establishes the diagnosis with patchy inflammation, skip lesions and granulomas on histology"}], "supporting": [{"test": "ferritin", "why": "Evaluates iron deficiency anemia"}, {"test": "b12", "why": "Low with terminal ileal disease or resection"}, {"test": "folate", "why": "Nutritional deficiency common in active disease"}, {"test": "ca", "why": "Low with fat malabsorption and vitamin D deficiency"}, {"test": "MRI enterography", "why": "Avoids radiation", "only_if": "child, pregnant, or repeated imaging needed"}, {"test": "Upper endoscopy (EGD)", "why": "Evaluates gastroduodenal involvement", "only_if": "upper GI symptoms or growth failure in a child"}, {"test": "Pelvic MRI", "why": "Maps perianal fistulas and abscesses before surgery", "only_if": "perianal pain, drainage or suspected fistula"}, {"test": "Abdominal x-ray (supine and upright)", "why": "Looks for obstruction or perforation", "only_if": "suspected obstruction or perforation"}, {"test": "procalcitonin", "why": "Helps separate bacterial infection or abscess from a flare", "only_if": "fever with focal tenderness and diagnostic uncertainty"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "Abdominal x-ray (supine and upright)", "why": "Rarely changes management in uncomplicated disease"}, {"test": "Small bowel follow-through (upper GI series with barium)", "why": "Superseded by CT or MR enterography"}, {"test": "d_dimer", "why": "No role in the evaluation of chronic diarrhea and abdominal pain"}, {"test": "lipase", "why": "Not needed unless the pain is epigastric or pancreatic disease is suspected"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Not part of the workup unless urinary symptoms suggest a fistula or infection"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Not routinely needed; consider only if diarrhea persists without inflammation"}], "decision_points": ["Exclude infection with stool studies before starting immunosuppression", "Pregnancy test before CT or immunosuppressive therapy in anyone who could be pregnant", "Use MRI instead of CT in children and pregnancy to avoid radiation", "Colonoscopy with biopsy is required for tissue diagnosis; imaging alone does not confirm Crohn's", "Fever with focal tenderness or a mass should prompt imaging for abscess before any surgery"], "criteria": [{"name": "Diagnosis of Crohn's disease", "summary": "A compatible chronic relapsing history plus objective evidence of segmental, transmural inflammation on endoscopy, histology or cross-sectional imaging, after excluding infection and other causes of colitis.", "items": ["Chronic diarrhea, abdominal pain, weight loss or growth failure", "Endoscopic patchy inflammation with skip lesions and rectal sparing", "Biopsy showing transmural inflammation, crypt distortion or noncaseating granulomas", "Cross-sectional imaging showing bowel wall thickening, stricture, fistula or abscess", "Negative stool studies for infection"]}], "scores": ["harvey_bradshaw", "crohns_disease_activity_index", "montreal_classification"]}, "differential": [{"name": "Ulcerative Colitis", "slug": "ulcerative-colitis", "why_considered": "The other major inflammatory bowel disease; chronic diarrhea and abdominal cramping in a young adult", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Bloody diarrhea with tenesmus and urgency", "discriminators": {"history": ["Bloody diarrhea as the predominant symptom", "Tenesmus and small-volume, frequent stools", "Continuous symptoms rather than discrete flares with normal intervals", "No perianal pain or drainage"], "exam": ["No perianal fistula, fissure or abscess", "Tenderness along the colon rather than right lower quadrant"], "labs": ["Positive p-ANCA more often than ASCA", "Fecal calprotectin elevated in both, so it does not separate them"], "imaging": ["Continuous inflammation starting at the rectum and extending proximally without skip lesions", "No terminal ileum involvement (backwash ileitis only with severe pancolitis)", "Lead pipe colon with loss of haustra in chronic disease"]}}, {"name": "Intestinal Tuberculosis", "slug": "intestinal-tuberculosis", "why_considered": "Granulomatous ileocecal inflammation that mimics Crohn's on biopsy and imaging", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Granulomas on biopsy with fever, night sweats, weight loss, or a history of travel or residence in a high-prevalence area", "discriminators": {"history": ["Fever, drenching night sweats and weight loss", "Travel to or residence in a country with high tuberculosis prevalence", "Known tuberculosis exposure or prior pulmonary disease", "No chronic relapsing diarrhea pattern"], "exam": ["Lymphadenopathy or pulmonary findings", "Right lower quadrant mass or tenderness"], "labs": ["Positive interferon-gamma release assay or tuberculin skin test", "Acid-fast bacilli or caseating granulomas on biopsy", "Positive mycobacterial culture or PCR from tissue"], "imaging": ["Caseating granulomas rather than noncaseating granulomas", "Circumferential ileocecal thickening with enlarged necrotic lymph nodes", "Chest radiograph showing active or prior pulmonary tuberculosis"]}}, {"name": "Infectious Colitis", "slug": "infectious-colitis", "why_considered": "Acute diarrhea, cramping and fever can look like a Crohn's flare", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Acute onset over days, sick contacts, recent travel, or antibiotic exposure", "discriminators": {"history": ["Acute onset over hours to days rather than weeks to months", "Sick contacts with similar diarrhea or a common food exposure", "Recent antibiotic use suggesting C. difficile", "Recent travel to an area with endemic infection"], "exam": ["Diffuse abdominal tenderness without a right lower quadrant mass", "Signs of dehydration rather than chronic weight loss"], "labs": ["Positive stool culture, C. difficile toxin/PCR, or ova and parasites", "Leukocytosis that resolves with treatment", "Fecal calprotectin may be elevated, so it does not exclude infection"], "imaging": ["Diffuse colonic inflammation without skip lesions or terminal ileum thickening", "No stricture, fistula or creeping fat"]}}, {"name": "Celiac Disease", "slug": "celiac-disease", "why_considered": "Chronic diarrhea, weight loss and fatigue in a young adult", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Diarrhea and bloating triggered by gluten-containing foods", "Symptoms improve on a gluten-free diet", "No perianal disease or mouth ulcers", "Family history of celiac disease"], "exam": ["Signs of malabsorption such as dermatitis herpetiformis or glossitis", "No abdominal mass or perianal findings"], "labs": ["Positive tissue transglutaminase IgA with elevated total IgA", "Iron deficiency anemia and low folate", "Fecal calprotectin usually normal"], "imaging": ["Small bowel biopsy showing villous atrophy and crypt hyperplasia", "No skip lesions, stricture or fistula on cross-sectional imaging"]}}, {"name": "Irritable Bowel Syndrome", "slug": "irritable-bowel-syndrome", "why_considered": "Chronic abdominal pain and altered bowel habits in a young adult", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Pain relieved by defecation and associated with a change in stool frequency or form", "No weight loss, fever, or nocturnal diarrhea", "Symptoms fluctuate with stress rather than following a progressive inflammatory course", "No family history of inflammatory bowel disease"], "exam": ["Normal abdominal exam without tenderness, mass or perianal findings", "No signs of malnutrition or anemia"], "labs": ["Normal CRP, ESR, hemoglobin and albumin", "Normal fecal calprotectin"], "imaging": ["Normal colonoscopy and cross-sectional imaging", "No bowel wall thickening, skip lesions or stricture"]}}, {"name": "Behçet Disease", "slug": "behcet-disease", "why_considered": "Mouth and intestinal ulcers with abdominal pain can mimic Crohn's", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recurrent painful oral and genital ulcers", "Eye inflammation with redness and photophobia", "Skin lesions such as acneiform nodules or a positive pathergy response", "No chronic diarrhea as the dominant symptom"], "exam": ["Genital ulcers and oral aphthae", "Uveitis on eye exam", "Pathergy reaction at a needle puncture site"], "labs": ["No specific serologic test; diagnosis is clinical", "Inflammatory markers may be elevated during flares"], "imaging": ["Ileocecal ulcers that are deep and round rather than serpiginous", "No creeping fat or noncaseating granulomas on biopsy"]}}, {"name": "Diverticulitis", "slug": "diverticulitis", "why_considered": "Left lower quadrant pain, fever and leukocytosis in an older adult", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Acute onset over hours to days rather than a chronic relapsing course", "Pain localized to the left lower quadrant", "Constipation more common than chronic diarrhea", "No weight loss or extraintestinal manifestations"], "exam": ["Left lower quadrant tenderness with guarding", "No perianal fistula or oral ulcers"], "labs": ["Leukocytosis that resolves with antibiotics", "Normal hemoglobin and albumin in uncomplicated cases"], "imaging": ["Colonic diverticula with segmental wall thickening and pericolic fat stranding", "No terminal ileum involvement or skip lesions"]}}, {"name": "Ischemic Colitis", "slug": "ischemic-colitis", "why_considered": "Abdominal pain and bloody diarrhea in an older adult with vascular risk factors", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden onset of crampy pain followed by urgency to defecate", "Older age with atrial fibrillation, heart failure or vascular disease", "Symptoms often resolve over days to weeks", "No chronic waxing and waning pattern"], "exam": ["Mild abdominal tenderness without a mass", "No perianal disease or extraintestinal findings"], "labs": ["Lactate may be elevated", "Leukocytosis and anemia from acute blood loss"], "imaging": ["Segmental colonic wall thickening, often in a watershed distribution such as the splenic flexure", "No terminal ileum involvement or creeping fat"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Ambulatory, fewer than 4 loose stools per day, minimal cramping, no fever, no weight loss, normal or near-normal inflammatory markers and albumin; no anemia or dehydration", "moderate": "4 to 6 loose stools per day, intermittent cramping, low-grade fever, some weight loss, mildly elevated CRP or ESR, mild anemia, no obstruction or abscess", "severe": "More than 6 loose stools per day, persistent pain, fever, significant weight loss, anemia, hypoalbuminemia, elevated inflammatory markers, or imaging showing stricture, fistula or phlegmon", "critical": "Toxic presentation with high fever, tachycardia, hypotension, severe abdominal tenderness or distension, marked leukocytosis, and imaging showing abscess, perforation or bowel obstruction requiring urgent intervention"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "High fever with focal abdominal tenderness or a palpable mass", "meaning": "Suggests intra-abdominal abscess or phlegmon; needs urgent imaging and possible drainage"}, {"finding": "Diffuse abdominal rigidity or rebound tenderness", "meaning": "Suggests perforation with peritonitis; surgical emergency"}, {"finding": "Vomiting, abdominal distension and absent or high-pitched bowel sounds", "meaning": "Suggests bowel obstruction from stricture or adhesions; needs urgent imaging and surgical evaluation"}, {"finding": "Tachycardia, hypotension or altered mental status", "meaning": "Suggests sepsis or hypovolemia from severe inflammation or blood loss; resuscitate and investigate urgently"}, {"finding": "Grossly bloody stools with hemodynamic instability", "meaning": "Suggests severe lower gastrointestinal bleeding; needs urgent resuscitation and endoscopy"}, {"finding": "Severe perianal pain with fluctuance or drainage", "meaning": "Suggests perianal or ischiorectal abscess; needs urgent surgical drainage"}], "complications": [{"name": "Intestinal stricture with obstruction", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Progressive cramping and distension after meals", "Vomiting and inability to pass stool or gas", "Dilated bowel loops with air-fluid levels on abdominal x-ray"]}, {"name": "Fistula formation", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Drainage of stool or pus from the perianal skin, vagina or abdominal wall", "Recurrent urinary tract infections or pneumaturia from an enterovesical fistula", "Fistula tract on pelvic MRI or CT enterography"]}, {"name": "Intra-abdominal or perianal abscess", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["High fever with focal tenderness or a palpable mass", "Marked leukocytosis and very high CRP", "Rim-enhancing fluid collection on CT or MRI"]}, {"name": "Perforation with peritonitis", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Sudden severe abdominal pain with rigidity", "Free air under the diaphragm on upright chest or abdominal x-ray", "Hypotension and tachycardia"]}, {"name": "Severe lower gastrointestinal bleeding", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Large-volume bloody stools", "Falling hemoglobin and hemodynamic instability", "Active bleeding on colonoscopy"]}, {"name": "Malnutrition and micronutrient deficiency", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Weight loss and muscle wasting", "Low albumin, iron, vitamin B12, folate, calcium or vitamin D", "Growth failure in children"]}, {"name": "Venous thromboembolism", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Unilateral leg swelling and pain", "Sudden dyspnea or pleuritic chest pain", "Risk is highest during active flares and hospitalization"]}, {"name": "Colorectal cancer", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Long-standing colonic disease, especially more than 8 to 10 years", "New anemia, rectal bleeding or change in bowel habit", "Dysplasia or mass on surveillance colonoscopy"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "children", "differences": "Growth failure, delayed puberty and poor weight gain may be the presenting features rather than prominent diarrhea or pain; upper GI involvement is more common and MRI is preferred to avoid radiation."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "A second peak occurs in the 50s to 60s; presentation may be milder or mistaken for diverticular or ischemic colitis, and complications such as stricture and cancer are more common."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Active disease increases the risk of preterm birth and low birth weight; some medications need adjustment, and MRI without gadolinium is preferred for imaging when possible."}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "differences": "Infectious colitis and medication-related colitis are more likely and must be excluded before attributing symptoms to a Crohn's flare; immunosuppressive therapy increases the risk of serious infections."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "How long have you had diarrhea, and how many loose stools a day?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Chronic diarrhea lasting weeks to months, often 4 or more loose stools per day during flares"}, {"question": "Where is the pain, and what is it like?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Crampy, colicky pain, often right lower quadrant or periumbilical, coming in waves before a bowel movement"}, {"question": "Have you lost weight without trying?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Unintentional weight loss, often 5-10% or more, supporting chronic inflammatory disease"}, {"question": "Do your symptoms come and go, or are they continuous?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Waxing and waning flares with relatively normal intervals, typical of Crohn's"}, {"question": "Does the diarrhea wake you at night?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Nocturnal diarrhea, which favors organic inflammatory disease over irritable bowel syndrome"}, {"question": "Is there blood or mucus in your stool?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Blood less prominent than in ulcerative colitis; mucus may be present"}, {"question": "Do you have pain, itching, or drainage around your bottom?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Perianal pain, fissure, fistula drainage, or abscess, which strongly supports Crohn's"}, {"question": "Have you had mouth sores, joint pain, eye redness, or skin bumps?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Extraintestinal manifestations such as aphthous ulcers, arthritis, uveitis, or erythema nodosum"}, {"question": "Any fever, chills, or night sweats?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Low-grade fever in flares; high fever with chills suggests abscess or infection"}, {"question": "Has anyone in your family had Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, or another autoimmune disease?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Family history of inflammatory bowel disease in a first-degree relative"}, {"question": "Do you smoke or have you ever smoked?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Current or past smoking, a strong risk factor for Crohn's"}, {"question": "What medications do you take, including NSAIDs, birth control pills, or antibiotics?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "NSAIDs, oral contraceptives, or recent antibiotics, which may increase risk or worsen symptoms"}, {"question": "Have you traveled recently or been around anyone with similar diarrhea?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Travel or sick contacts that would suggest infectious colitis instead"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy status, which affects imaging and treatment choices"}, {"question": "Have you had any abdominal surgery or bowel resections?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prior surgery for Crohn's complications or other abdominal conditions"}], "accepted_names": ["Crohn's disease", "Crohn disease", "Regional enteritis", "Regional ileitis", "CD"], "reasoning_points": ["Chronic diarrhea, crampy abdominal pain, and unintentional weight loss over weeks to months", "Waxing and waning course with flares and relatively normal intervals", "Right lower quadrant or periumbilical tenderness on exam", "Perianal findings such as fissure, fistula, or abscess supporting Crohn's over ulcerative colitis", "Extraintestinal manifestations such as aphthous ulcers, arthritis, uveitis, or erythema nodosum", "Elevated inflammatory markers (CRP, ESR) and anemia of chronic disease or iron deficiency", "Fecal calprotectin elevated, distinguishing inflammatory diarrhea from irritable bowel syndrome", "Stool studies negative for infection, including C. difficile, before attributing symptoms to Crohn's", "Colonoscopy showing patchy, discontinuous inflammation with skip lesions, rectal sparing, and terminal ileum involvement", "Biopsy showing transmural inflammation, crypt architectural distortion, or noncaseating granulomas", "Cross-sectional imaging (CT or MR enterography) showing bowel wall thickening, stricture, fistula, or abscess", "Pregnancy test negative before imaging and immunosuppressive therapy when applicable"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Young adult with months of diarrhea, crampy right lower quadrant pain, and weight loss", "Perianal fistula or fissure found on exam", "Family history of Crohn's disease", "Elevated CRP and ESR with anemia", "Colonoscopy with classic skip lesions and cobblestoning"], "medium": ["Symptoms overlap with ulcerative colitis; bloody diarrhea is minimal or absent", "Predominantly ileal disease with normal colonoscopy unless terminal ileum is intubated", "Extraintestinal manifestations such as joint pain or eye redness dominate the presentation", "Older adult with a second peak of incidence, symptoms mistaken for diverticulitis", "Normal CRP despite active isolated ileal disease"], "hard": ["Child with growth failure and delayed puberty but minimal GI symptoms", "Pregnant patient with abdominal pain and diarrhea; imaging and treatment must be adjusted", "Immunocompromised patient where infectious colitis must be excluded first", "Presentation with a complication such as stricture, fistula, or abscess rather than classic symptoms", "Granulomas on biopsy raising intestinal tuberculosis as a mimic in a patient with relevant travel history"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
