es overall", "More common in Black adults than in White or Asian adults in US data", "Often occurs during or shortly after a hospital stay or after surgery"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Recent major surgery, especially hip or knee replacement", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Prolonged immobility (bed rest, long-haul travel, cast immobilization)", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Active cancer or cancer chemotherapy", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Prior venous thromboembolism", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Inherited thrombophilia (factor V Leiden, prothrombin gene mutation, protein C or S deficiency, antithrombin deficiency)", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Pregnancy and the postpartum period", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Combined oral contraceptive or hormone replacement therapy", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Obesity", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Heart failure or recent myocardial infarction", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Inflammatory bowel disease", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Nephrotic syndrome", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Antiphospholipid antibody syndrome", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Older age", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Smoking", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Varicose veins", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Active malignancy", "Heart failure", "Recent stroke with immobility", "Inflammatory bowel disease", "Nephrotic syndrome", "Antiphospholipid antibody syndrome", "Inherited thrombophilia", "Obesity"], "family_history": ["Venous thromboembolism in a first-degree relative, especially before age 50", "Known inherited thrombophilia in the family"], "social_history": ["Recent long-distance travel by plane, car or train", "Prolonged bed rest or reduced mobility", "Recent hospitalization or surgery", "Current or recent smoking"], "exposures": ["Recent major surgery or trauma", "Central venous catheter placement", "Prolonged immobilization"], "risk_medications": ["combined oral contraceptive pills", "estrogen hormone replacement therapy", "tamoxifen", "raloxifene", "heparin", "thalidomide", "lenalidomide", "erythropoietin"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "My left leg is swollen and achy", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "The calf is tender and feels warm", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My leg hurts when I stand or walk", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "The skin on my leg looks red or discolored", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual over hours to a few days; often noticed on waking or after a period of sitting still", "duration": "Usually present for 1-7 days at presentation", "progression": "Swelling and discomfort build over the first day or two, then plateau; may worsen with activity or dependency", "location": "Most often the calf or thigh of one leg; can involve the popliteal or femoral veins; upper extremity DVT occurs with central lines or effort thrombosis", "radiation": "Aching may extend up the inner thigh or into the groin; does not radiate down the leg in a dermatomal pattern", "quality": "Dull, heavy, tight or cramping ache; sometimes a pulling sensation in the calf", "severity": "Mild to moderate, typically 3-6/10; severe pain is unusual unless extensive iliofemoral thrombosis", "timing": "Constant, worse after standing or walking and better with elevation", "aggravating": ["Standing or walking", "Prolonged sitting with the leg down", "Pressing on the calf"], "relieving": ["Elevating the leg", "Resting", "Warm compresses", "Analgesics such as acetaminophen or ibuprofen"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Unilateral leg swelling", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Calf tenderness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Warmth over the affected vein", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Skin redness or discoloration", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Increased calf circumference compared with the other leg", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Low-grade fever", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Dilated superficial collateral veins", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Bilateral leg swelling", "Chest pain or shortness of breath", "Coughing up blood", "Fever with chills and spreading skin redness", "Recent leg trauma or muscle tear", "Chronic venous insufficiency with skin staining and ulcers", "Cellulitis with a clear portal of entry", "Calf pain that is reproducible only with exercise and relieved by rest"]}, "ros": [{"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [{"text": "Swelling of one leg", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Warmth over the affected area", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Chest pain", "Palpitations", "Syncope"], "argues_against": ["Pulmonary embolism with hemodynamic compromise"]}, {"system": "respiratory", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Shortness of breath", "Pleuritic chest pain", "Coughing up blood"], "argues_against": ["Pulmonary embolism"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Calf pain with walking", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Recent trauma", "Muscle tear", "Joint swelling"], "argues_against": ["Baker cyst rupture", "Gastrocnemius tear", "Cellulitis"]}, {"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Redness or discoloration of the leg", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Open wound", "Draining ulcer", "Spreading erythema"], "argues_against": ["Cellulitis", "Chronic venous stasis changes"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [], "negatives": ["High fever", "Weight loss", "Night sweats"], "argues_against": ["Systemic infection", "Malignancy as the sole cause"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "May present with only vague leg discomfort or worsening edema, and swelling can be attributed to chronic venous insufficiency or heart failure.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear unilateral swelling", "Calf tenderness", "Warmth"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Leg swelling and discomfort are common in normal pregnancy, so DVT is often mistaken for normal pregnancy changes; left leg is more commonly affected due to compression of the left iliac vein.", "missing_classic_features": ["Marked asymmetry", "Clear warmth or redness"]}, {"population": "obesity", "how_it_differs": "Bilateral leg swelling and chronic skin changes are common, making asymmetry harder to detect and masking the classic unilateral presentation.", "missing_classic_features": ["Obvious unilateral swelling", "Palpable cord"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "DVT is uncommon and usually occurs with central venous catheters, malignancy or inherited thrombophilia; presentation may be pain and swelling around a line or an extremity.", "missing_classic_features": ["Typical adult risk profile", "Calf vein involvement"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable, ambulatory, no distress", "moderate": "Mild discomfort, favors the affected leg, otherwise well-appearing", "severe": "Ill-appearing, in pain, reluctant to bear weight on the affected leg", "critical": "Toxic-appearing, pale, diaphoretic, tachypneic, or in shock (suggests massive iliofemoral thrombosis or pulmonary embolism)"}, "findings": [{"id": "unilateral-leg-swelling", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Inspect both legs from groin to ankle with the patient standing or supine", "finding": "Unilateral swelling of the calf, thigh, or entire leg", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "calf-circumference-difference", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Measure the calf circumference 10 cm below the tibial tuberosity on both legs", "finding": "Calf circumference increased by 3 cm or more on the affected side compared with the unaffected side", "frequency": "common", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "calf-tenderness", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Palpate the calf muscles and along the deep veins", "finding": "Tenderness over the