no profile yet", "differential serotonin-syndrome: no profile yet", "differential neuroleptic-malignant-syndrome: no profile yet", "differential malingering: no profile yet"]}, "review": {"status": "pending"}}, "patient": {"age": {"typical_min": 18, "typical_max": 65, "peak": "late teens to 30s", "possible_min": 12, "possible_max": 90}, "sex": "either", "demographics": ["Men are more likely to use most illicit drugs and to have drug use disorders; women progress from first use to dependence more quickly and are more likely to present in primary care or emergency settings", "Highest prevalence of illicit drug use is in adults ages 18–25", "Non-Hispanic American Indian or Alaska Native and multiracial adults have the highest rates of substance use disorder; Asian adults have the lowest", "Sexual and gender minority youth and adults have higher rates of substance use than the general population", "Lower household income and less education are associated with higher rates of drug-related harm"], "risk_factors": [{"text": "Family history of substance use disorder", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Untreated mental health condition such as depression, anxiety, PTSD, or ADHD", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Initiation of drug use in adolescence", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Peer or social network that uses drugs", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Adverse childhood experiences, including abuse, neglect, or household substance use", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Easy access to prescription opioids, benzodiazepines, or stimulants, including a personal or household prescription", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Male sex", "strength": "weak"}, {"text": "Unstable housing or incarceration", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Chronic pain treated with opioids", "strength": "moderate"}], "comorbidities": ["Major depressive disorder", "Generalized anxiety disorder", "Post-traumatic stress disorder", "Attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder", "Bipolar disorder", "Chronic pain", "Hepatitis C", "HIV", "Alcohol use disorder", "Tobacco use disorder", "Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease"], "family_history": ["Substance use disorder in a parent or sibling", "Alcohol use disorder", "Mood or anxiety disorder"], "social_history": ["Lives with or spends most time with people who use drugs", "Trouble at school, work, or in relationships", "Loss of job, housing, or custody", "Recent release from jail or prison", "Sex work or exchange of sex for drugs or money", "Shares injection equipment"], "exposures": ["Prescription opioids, benzodiazepines, or stimulants", "Heroin or illicitly manufactured fentanyl", "Cocaine or methamphetamine", "Cannabis", "Club drugs such as MDMA or GHB", "Inhalants", "Anabolic steroids", "Over-the-counter medications used to get high, such as dextromethorphan or loperamide"], "risk_medications": ["oxycodone", "hydrocodone", "morphine", "fentanyl", "alprazolam", "lorazepam", "diazepam", "clonazepam", "methylphenidate", "amphetamine", "dextroamphetamine", "zolpidem", "gabapentin", "pregabalin", "tramadol", "codeine", "promethazine"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I just can't stop using, even though it's ruining my life", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I've been feeling awful and shaky since I tried to cut back", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My family says I have a problem and made me come in", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I need something for my pain, my usual pills ran out early", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "I've been sleeping terribly and my mood is all over the place", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "I overdosed last week and woke up in the ER", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Usually begins in adolescence or early adulthood, often with a first exposure at a party, from a friend, or through a prescription after an injury; escalation to a problem pattern typically builds over months to years", "duration": "Weeks to decades; most patients describe a pattern lasting at least a year by the time they seek care", "progression": "Use becomes more frequent and in larger amounts than intended; the person spends more time obtaining, using, and recovering; tolerance develops so more is needed for the same effect; withdrawal appears when use stops; use continues despite clear harm to health, work, money, and relationships", "location": "Not applicable", "radiation": "Not applicable", "quality": "The patient describes a loss of control over use, strong craving, and preoccupation with the drug that crowds out other interests", "severity": "Varies; patients often describe it as moderate to severe and worse during withdrawal or after a recent overdose", "timing": "Often daily or several times a day; some use in binges separated by days of crash and recovery", "aggravating": ["Stress", "Being around people who use", "Depression or anxiety", "Physical pain", "Money or relationship problems", "Being in places linked to past use"], "relieving": ["Using the drug", "Being in treatment or a structured program", "Support from family or a recovery group", "Stopping contact with people who use"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Craving the drug", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Needing more of the drug to get the same effect", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Withdrawal symptoms when cutting down or stopping", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Neglecting work, school, or family duties", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Sleep problems, either too little or too much", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Low mood, irritability, or anxiety", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Appetite change and weight change", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Lying about or hiding use", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Spending more money than planned on the drug", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Blackouts or memory gaps", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Overdose requiring emergency care", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Injection-related skin infections or abscesses", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Seizures during withdrawal from alcohol or benzodiazepines", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Painless scrotal or testicular mass", "New focal weakness or aphasia of sudden onset", "Fevers with a new heart murmur", "Weight loss with night sweats and enlarged lymph nodes", "Bloody diarrhea with tenesmus", "Polyuria and polydipsia with unintentional weight loss"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Fatigue", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Weight loss", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Night sweats", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Low-grade fevers", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["High fever with rigors", "Drenching night sweats with weight loss"]}, {"system": "psychiatric", "positives": [{"text": "Craving", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Irritability", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Depressed mood", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Anxiety", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Poor concentration", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Suicidal thoughts", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Hallucinations or paranoia during stimulant intoxication", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Persistent grandiosity lasting weeks outside of intoxication", "Catatonia"], "argues_against": ["Psychosis that persists for weeks after the drug clears"]}, {"system": "neurologic", "positives": [{"text": "Tremor", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Headache", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dizziness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Numbness or tingling in the hands and feet", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Memory problems", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Seizures during withdrawal", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Sudden focal weakness", "New severe headache with neck stiffness"], "argues_against": ["Acute stroke or meningitis"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Nausea and vomiting", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Abdominal cramping", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Diarrhea", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Constipation", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Poor appetite", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Bloody stools", "Jaundice"], "argues_against": ["Acute abdomen"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [{"text": "Palpitations", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Chest tightness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Elevated blood pressure and heart rate", "frequency": "common"}], "negatives": ["Exertional chest pain relieved by rest", "Leg swelling"], "argues_against": ["Acute coronary syndrome", "Heart failure"]}, {"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Shortness of breath", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Cough", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Wheezing", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Slow, shallow breathing after opioid use", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Coughing up blood", "Pleuritic chest pain"], "argues_against": ["Pneumonia", "Pulmonary embolism"]}, {"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Track marks or scars at injection sites", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Skin abscesses or cellulitis", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Itching or picking at the skin during stimulant use", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Painless ulcer with a clean base", "New rash covering the palms and soles"], "argues_against": ["Primary syphilis", "Disseminated infection"]}, {"system": "genitourinary", "positives": [{"text": "Decreased libido", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Erectile dysfunction", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Painful urination", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Blood in urine", "Flank pain with fever"], "argues_against": ["Pyelonephritis", "Kidney stone"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Muscle aches and cramps", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Joint pain", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Hot, swollen single joint", "Proximal muscle weakness with a rash"], "argues_against": ["Septic arthritis", "Inflammatory myopathy"]}, {"system": "endocrine", "positives": [{"text": "Increased thirst", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Increased urination", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Unintentional weight loss with polyuria and polydipsia"], "argues_against": ["New-onset diabetes"]}, {"system": "hematologic", "positives": [{"text": "Easy bruising", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Bleeding gums", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Painless swollen lymph nodes", "Recurrent infections with low blood counts"], "argues_against": ["Lymphoma", "Leukemia"]}, {"system": "allergic_immunologic", "positives": [{"text": "Frequent infections", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Recurrent sinopulmonary infections since childhood"], "argues_against": ["Primary immunodeficiency"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Often begins with a prescribed opioid, benzodiazepine, or sedative after surgery or for chronic pain; patients may underreport use, present with falls, confusion, or worsening chronic disease rather than a request for help, and are more sensitive to sedation and withdrawal.", "missing_classic_features": ["Adolescent or young-adult onset", "Obvious social or legal consequences", "Self-identification as an addict"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Patients often hide use because of fear of child protective services; presentation may be late or no prenatal care, and withdrawal in the newborn after delivery is a common first sign. Opioid use in pregnancy is treated with methadone or buprenorphine rather than abrupt withdrawal.", "missing_classic_features": ["Volunteered history of use", "Typical social decline story"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Adolescents may present with declining grades, truancy, new peer group, mood swings, or an overdose; younger children present after accidental ingestion of a household medication or an adult's drug.", "missing_classic_features": ["Self-reported craving or loss of control", "Long-standing use history"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "Injection drug use with immune suppression raises the risk of unusual infections such as invasive fungal infections and atypical pneumonia, so fever and focal findings may dominate the picture.", "missing_classic_features": ["Typical withdrawal-focused presentation"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Alert, well-groomed, cooperative; may appear tired or restless", "moderate": "Ill-appearing, poor grooming or hygiene, restless or sedated, avoids eye contact", "severe": "Markedly disheveled, malodorous, thin, agitated or drowsy, poor insight", "critical": "Obtunded or unresponsive, cyanotic, shallow or agonal breathing, pinpoint or dilated pupils"}, "findings": [{"id": "pupil-size", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect both pupils in dim light and test reactivity to light", "finding": "Pinpoint pupils (opioid effect) or dilated pupils (stimulant or anticholinergic effect)", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "nasal-septum", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the nasal mucosa and septum with a light", "finding": "Septal perforation, crusting, or bleeding from intranasal use", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "oral-hygiene", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the teeth, gums, and oral mucosa", "finding": "Dental caries, missing teeth, gingivitis, or oral candidiasis", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "track-marks", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Inspect the antecubital fossae, forearms, hands, feet, and neck for puncture marks", "finding": "Linear scars, hyperpigmented tracks, or fresh injection sites", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "skin-abscess", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Palpate any red, warm, or fluctuant area near injection sites", "finding": "Abscess, cellulitis, or induration", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "skin-picking", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the face, arms, and legs for excoriations", "finding": "Excoriations or sores from picking (stimulant use)", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "tremor", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Ask the patient to hold both arms outstretched with fingers spread", "finding": "Fine tremor of the hands", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "gait", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Observe the patient walking and turning", "finding": "Ataxia, unsteady gait, or wide-based gait", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "mentation", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Assess orientation, attention, and recall during the interview", "finding": "Impaired attention, disorientation, or memory gaps", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "mood-affect", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Ask about mood, anhedonia, and anxiety over the past two weeks", "finding": "Depressed or irritable mood, anxious affect", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "suicidal-ideation", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Ask directly about thoughts of self-harm or suicide", "finding": "Passive or active suicidal ideation", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "psychosis", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Ask about hearing voices or feeling watched or persecuted", "finding": "Paranoia, hallucinations, or disorganized speech during intoxication", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "conjunctival-injection", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the conjunctivae and sclerae", "finding": "Red, injected conjunctivae (cannabis or stimulant use)", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "cardiac-regular-rate", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the heart at the apex and base", "finding": "Regular rate and rhythm without murmur", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "lung-clear", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate all lung fields", "finding": "Clear breath sounds without crackles or wheeze", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "abdomen-nontender", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Palpate all four quadrants", "finding": "Soft, non-tender abdomen without organomegaly", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "neuro-nonfocal", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Test strength, sensation, and deep tendon reflexes", "finding": "No focal motor or sensory deficit", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}]}, "vitals": {"temp": {"mild": {"min": 97.8, "max": 99.1}, "moderate": {"min": 98.6, "max": 100.4}, "severe": {"min": 99.5, "max": 101.5}, "critical": {"min": 100.0, "max": 103.0}}, "hr": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 90, "max": 120}, "severe": {"min": 110, "max": 140}, "critical": {"min": 40, "max": 150}}, "rr": {"mild": {"min": 12, "max": 20}, "moderate": {"min": 16, "max": 24}, "severe": {"min": 22, "max": 30}, "critical": {"min": 6, "max": 34}}, "sbp": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 130}, "moderate": {"min": 120, "max": 150}, "severe": {"min": 140, "max": 180}, "critical": {"min": 70, "max": 200}}, "dbp": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 85}, "moderate": {"min": 75, "max": 95}, "severe": {"min": 90, "max": 110}, "critical": {"min": 40, "max": 120}}, "spo2": {"mild": {"min": 95, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 92, "max": 98}, "severe": {"min": 88, "max": 95}, "critical": {"min": 70, "max": 92}}}, "labs": [{"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "almost_always", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Required in anyone who could be pregnant before imaging or starting medication; a positive result changes the entire treatment plan."}, {"test_id": "glucose", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 100, "max": 180}, "severe": {"min": 180, "max": 350}, "critical": {"min": 40, "max": 500}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hyperglycemia from stimulant use or stress; hypoglycemia can mimic intoxication or withdrawal."}, {"test_id": "na", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 128, "max": 134}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 127}, "critical": {"min": 110, "max": 119}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hyponatremia from MDMA, excessive water intake, or poor nutrition; can cause seizures."}, {"test_id": "k", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 3.0, "max": 3.4}, "severe": {"min": 2.5, "max": 2.9}, "critical": {"min": 1.8, "max": 2.4}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hypokalemia from vomiting, diarrhea, or stimulant use; check before starting some medications."}, {"test_id": "hco3", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 18, "max": 21}, "severe": {"min": 12, "max": 17}, "critical": {"min": 6, "max": 11}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low bicarbonate suggests metabolic acidosis from starvation, alcohol, or toxin ingestion."}, {"test_id": "bun", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 21, "max": 35}, "severe": {"min": 30, "max": 60}, "critical": {"min": 50, "max": 100}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated from dehydration or poor intake; helps assess volume status."}, {"test_id": "cr", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 1.2, "max": 2.0}, "severe": {"min": 1.8, "max": 3.5}, "critical": {"min": 3.0, "max": 8.0}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Rises with dehydration, rhabdomyolysis, or nephrotoxic drugs."}, {"test_id": "ast", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 41, "max": 120}, "severe": {"min": 100, "max": 400}, "critical": {"min": 300, "max": 2000}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated in hepatitis, alcohol use, or muscle injury; AST>ALT suggests alcohol or muscle source."}, {"test_id": "alt", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 57, "max": 150}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 500}, "critical": {"min": 400, "max": 2000}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated with hepatitis or drug-induced liver injury."}, {"test_id": "ggt", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 49, "max": 150}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 400}, "critical": {"min": 300, "max": 1000}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Supports alcohol or medication effect on the liver."}, {"test_id": "tbili", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 1.3, "max": 3.0}, "severe": {"min": 2.5, "max": 8.0}, "critical": {"min": 6.0, "max": 20.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional"}, {"test_id": "albumin", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 2.8, "max": 3.4}, "severe": {"min": 2.0, "max": 2.7}, "critical": {"min": 1.5, "max": 1.9}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Low with poor nutrition or chronic liver disease."}, {"test_id": "ck", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 310, "max": 1000}, "severe": {"min": 800, "max": 5000}, "critical": {"min": 4000, "max": 50000}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Markedly elevated with rhabdomyolysis from stimulants, seizures, or prolonged immobility; risk of acute kidney injury."}, {"test_id": "wbc", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 11.1, "max": 15.0}, "severe": {"min": 14.0, "max": 22.0}, "critical": {"min": 20.0, "max": 35.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Leukocytosis suggests infection such as cellulitis, abscess, endocarditis, or pneumonia."}, {"test_id": "hgb", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 9.0, "max": 11.9}, "severe": {"min": 7.0, "max": 8.9}, "critical": {"min": 4.0, "max": 6.9}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Anemia from poor nutrition, chronic disease, or gastrointestinal bleeding."}, {"test_id": "plt", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 100, "max": 149}, "severe": {"min": 50, "max": 99}, "critical": {"min": 10, "max": 49}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Thrombocytopenia with liver disease, sepsis, or bone marrow suppression."}, {"test_id": "tsh", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 4.1, "max": 10.0}, "severe": {"min": 8.0, "max": 20.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Thyroid disease can mimic or worsen mood and anxiety symptoms."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "severe": {"min": 6.5, "max": 9.0}, "critical": {"min": 8.0, "max": 14.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Screens for diabetes, which is more common with some antipsychotics and poor nutrition."}, {"test_id": "ua_blood", "qualitative": {"moderate": "1+", "severe": "2+"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Hematuria can reflect rhabdomyolysis, urinary infection, or trauma."}, {"test_id": "ua_ketones", "qualitative": {"moderate": "Small", "severe": "Moderate"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Ketones from poor intake or starvation."}, {"test_id": "ua_le", "qualitative": {"moderate": "1+", "severe": "2+"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Suggests urinary infection; common in patients with poor hygiene or catheter use."}, {"test_id": "ua_nitrite", "qualitative": {"moderate": "Positive"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Supports urinary 