 in function before drug use began"], "exam": ["Psychosis present during prolonged abstinence", "Negative symptoms such as flat affect"], "labs": ["Negative toxicology during active psychosis"]}}, {"name": "Hypoglycemia", "slug": "hypoglycemia", "why_considered": "Confusion, agitation, tremor, and diaphoresis that mimic intoxication or withdrawal", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Altered mental status with sweating and tremor; check a bedside glucose", "discriminators": {"history": ["Diabetes with insulin or sulfonylurea use", "Missed meal", "Symptoms relieved by eating"], "exam": ["Diaphoresis", "Tremor", "Improves rapidly with glucose"], "labs": ["Low serum glucose that corrects with dextrose"]}}, {"name": "Sepsis from injection-related infection", "slug": "sepsis", "why_considered": "Fever, tachycardia, and altered mental status in a patient who injects drugs", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fever with tachycardia and hypotension in a patient with injection sites", "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent injection", "Skin infection or abscess", "Chills and rigors"], "exam": ["Fever", "Cellulitis or abscess", "New heart murmur"], "labs": ["Leukocytosis", "Elevated lactate", "Positive blood cultures"], "imaging": ["Echocardiogram may show vegetations"]}}, {"name": "Acute coronary syndrome from stimulant use", "slug": "acute-coronary-syndrome", "why_considered": "Chest pain, palpitations, and dyspnea after cocaine or methamphetamine use", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Chest pain with stimulant use or ST changes on ECG", "discriminators": {"history": ["Chest pain after cocaine or methamphetamine", "Pressure-like pain radiating to the arm or jaw"], "exam": ["Tachycardia", "Diaphoresis", "Hypertension"], "labs": ["Elevated troponin", "Positive cocaine or amphetamine on toxicology"], "ecg": ["ST elevation or depression", "Sinus tachycardia"]}}, {"name": "Serotonin syndrome", "slug": "serotonin-syndrome", "why_considered": "Agitation, tremor, clonus, and hyperthermia in a patient taking serotonergic drugs", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Clonus and hyperthermia after starting or combining serotonergic agents", "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent addition or dose increase of an SSRI, SNRI, MAOI, or tramadol", "Use of MDMA or other stimulants"], "exam": ["Clonus, especially in the lower extremities", "Hyperreflexia", "Dilated pupils", "Hyperthermia"], "labs": ["Elevated CK", "Leukocytosis", "Normal or elevated bicarbonate"]}}, {"name": "Neuroleptic malignant syndrome", "slug": "neuroleptic-malignant-syndrome", "why_considered": "Rigidity, fever, and altered mental status in a patient taking antipsychotics", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Lead-pipe rigidity with high fever and autonomic instability after an antipsychotic", "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent antipsychotic start or dose increase", "Recent discontinuation of a dopaminergic drug"], "exam": ["Lead-pipe rigidity", "High fever", "Altered mental status", "Autonomic instability"], "labs": ["Markedly elevated CK", "Leukocytosis", "Elevated liver enzymes"]}}, {"name": "Malingering or secondary gain", "slug": "malingering", "why_considered": "Requests for controlled substances or exaggerated symptoms for external benefit", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Request for a specific controlled drug", "Symptoms that shift with observers", "Legal or financial incentive"], "exam": ["Findings inconsistent with reported severity", "No objective signs of intoxication or withdrawal"], "labs": ["Toxicology negative for the drug the patient claims to use"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Two to three criteria for a substance use disorder met; use continues despite some harm but most obligations are met; no physiologic dependence or withdrawal", "moderate": "Four to five criteria met; clear loss of control, craving, and role impairment; tolerance or withdrawal may be present; still able to engage in treatment", "severe": "Six or more criteria met; daily or binge use, physiologic dependence with withdrawal, major health, legal, and social consequences, and repeated failed attempts to stop", "critical": "Life-threatening presentation: opioid overdose with respiratory depression, severe alcohol or benzodiazepine withdrawal with seizures or delirium, stimulant-induced myocardial infarction or hyperthermia, or sepsis from injection-related infection"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Pinpoint pupils with respiratory rate under 10 or unresponsiveness", "meaning": "Opioid overdose; give naloxone and support ventilation"}, {"finding": "Seizure or confusion after stopping alcohol or benzodiazepines", "meaning": "Impending or active withdrawal delirium; treat immediately"}, {"finding": "Fever with a new heart murmur in a patient who injects drugs", "meaning": "Infective endocarditis; obtain blood cultures and echocardiogram"}, {"finding": "Chest pain with ST changes after stimulant use", "meaning": "Stimulant-induced myocardial ischemia or infarction"}, {"finding": "Temperature above 104 °F with rigidity or clonus", "meaning": "Serotonin syndrome or neuroleptic malignant syndrome; a medical emergency"}, {"finding": "Active suicidal ideation with a plan", "meaning": "High risk of self-harm; requires immediate psychiatric evaluation"}, {"finding": "Hypotension with tachycardia and elevated lactate", "meaning": "Sepsis; start fluids and antibiotics"}], "complications": [{"name": "Opioid overdose with respiratory arrest", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Pinpoint pupils", "Slow, shallow breathing", "Unresponsiveness", "Response to naloxone"]}, {"name": "Withdrawal seizures and delirium tremens", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Last drink or benzodiazepine 6–72 hours ago", "Tremor and diaphoresis", "Disorientation and hallucinations"]}, {"name": "Infective endocarditis", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Fever", "New murmur", "Positive blood cultures", "Vegetations on echocardiogram"]}, {"name": "Skin and soft tissue infection or abscess", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Red, warm, tender injection site", "Purulent drainage", "Fever and leukocytosis"]}, {"name": "Blood-borne infections such as HIV and hepatitis C", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Shared injection equipment", "Positive HIV or hepatitis C antibody", "Abnormal liver enzymes"]}, {"name": "Stimulant-induced myocardial infarction or arrhythmia", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Chest pain after cocaine or methamphetamine", "Elevated troponin", "ST changes on ECG"]}, {"name": "Rhabdomyolysis and acute kidney injury", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Severe agitation, seizure, or prolonged immobility", "Markedly elevated CK", "Dark urine with positive dipstick for blood"]}, {"name": "Relapse after a period of abstinence", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Return to people or places linked to past use", "Untreated craving or mood symptoms", "Loss of a structured program"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Opioid use disorder is treated with methadone or buprenorphine rather than abrupt withdrawal; untreated withdrawal risks fetal loss. Newborns may show withdrawal after delivery, and patients often avoid care because of fear of child protective services."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Use often starts with a prescribed opioid, benzodiazepine, or sedative after surgery or for chronic pain; patients may present with falls, confusion, or worsening chronic disease rather than a request for help and are more sensitive to sedation and withdrawal."}, {"population": "children", "differences": "Adolescents may present with declining grades, truancy, a new peer group, mood swings, or an overdose; younger children present after accidental ingestion of a household medication or an adult's drug."}, {"population": "hepatic_impairment", "differences": "Liver disease changes drug metabolism and raises the risk of toxicity; many medications used for addiction treatment need dose adjustment, and coagulopathy increases bleeding risk."}, {"population": "renal_impairment", "differences": "Reduced clearance raises the risk of drug accumulation and toxicity; some medications used for opioid use disorder need dose adjustment, and rhabdomyolysis is more likely to cause acute kidney injury."}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "differences": "Injection drug use with immune suppression raises the risk of unusual infections such as invasive fungal infections and atypical pneumonia, so fever and focal findings may dominate the picture."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "Tell me about your drug use — what do you use, how much, and how often?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Specific substances, route (oral, snorting, smoking, injection), amount, and frequency; ask about each class separately"}, {"question": "When did you last use, and what happens when you stop or cut back?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Timing of last use and withdrawal symptoms; determines risk of seizures or delirium"}, {"question": "Have you ever tried to cut down or stop? What happened?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Unsuccessful attempts to quit or control use — a core feature of a substance use disorder"}, {"question": "Do you need more of the drug than you used to for the same effect?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Tolerance"}, {"question": "Do you ever use more than you planned, or for longer than you meant to?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Loss of control over amount or duration of use"}, {"question": "How much of your day goes to getting, using, or recovering from the drug?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Time spent obtaining, using, and recovering; craving and preoccupation"}, {"question": "Has your use caused problems at work, school, or home, or with people close to you?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Failure to meet obligations and continued use despite social or interpersonal problems"}, {"question": "Have you given up activities or hobbies you used to enjoy?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Giving up important social, occupational, or recreational activities"}, {"question": "Have you used in situations where it was physically dangerous, like driving or operating machinery?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Use in hazardous situations"}, {"question": "Have you kept using even though you knew it was hurting your health or your mind?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Continued use despite physical or psychological harm"}, {"question": "Have you ever overdosed or woken up in an emergency room after using?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Prior overdose — a strong marker of severe disorder and high risk of another"}, {"question": "Do you inject? Do you ever share needles, syringes, or other equipment?", "category": "social", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Injection use and sharing — drives risk of HIV, hepatitis B and C, and endocarditis"}, {"question": "How do you get the drug, and how do you pay for it?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prescription sources, illicit supply, sex work or selling drugs, financial strain"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have a problem with drugs or alcohol?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Family history of substance use disorder — a strong risk factor"}, {"question": "Have you been feeling depressed, anxious, or unable to sleep? Any thoughts of hurting yourself?", "category": "ros", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Co-occurring depression, anxiety, PTSD, or ADHD and any suicidal ideation"}, {"question": "Have you ever heard voices or felt paranoid or watched when you were using or coming down?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Stimulant-induced paranoia or hallucinations; whether psychosis clears with abstinence"}, {"question": "Are you taking any prescribed medicines, especially opioids, benzodiazepines, or stimulants?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Prescribed controlled substances, who prescribes them, and whether they are taken as directed"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy changes treatment entirely; opioid use disorder in pregnancy is treated with methadone or buprenorphine, not withdrawal"}, {"question": "Where are you living now, and who do you spend most of your time with?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Unstable housing, incarceration, or a social network that uses drugs"}, {"question": "Any fevers, chills, or sores where you inject?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Skin infection, abscess, or systemic infection such as endocarditis"}], "accepted_names": ["Drug use and addiction", "Substance use disorder", "Drug use disorder", "Drug addiction", "Substance abuse", "Drug abuse", "Opioid use disorder", "Stimulant use disorder", "Cannabis use disorder", "Sedative use disorder", "Addiction"], "reasoning_points": ["A problematic pattern of use causing impairment or distress, with at least two features in a 12-month period", "Features include using more or longer than intended, unsuccessful attempts to cut down, craving, and time spent obtaining or recovering", "Continued use despite physical, psychological, or social harm, and giving up important activities", "Tolerance and withdrawal indicate physiologic dependence and raise severity", "Severity is graded by the number of features: mild (2–3), moderate (4–5), severe (6 or more)", "Route of use matters: injection raises risk of HIV, hepatitis B and C, skin infection, and endocarditis", "Screen for co-occurring depression, anxiety, PTSD, ADHD, and suicide risk", "Assess for withdrawal risk, especially alcohol and benzodiazepines, which can cause seizures or delirium", "Pregnancy must be checked because it changes the entire treatment plan"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Young adult with a clear story of escalating use, craving, and loss of control", "Obvious consequences such as job loss, arrest, or relationship breakdown", "Physical signs such as track marks or pinpoint pupils", "Patient openly reports the drug and pattern of use"], "medium": ["Patient minimizes use or presents with a physical complaint such as an abscess or chest pain", "Co-occurring depression or anxiety that masks the substance problem", "Prescription opioid use that started legitimately after surgery or injury", "Withdrawal symptoms that bring the patient in without a stated drug history"], "hard": ["Older adult started on a prescribed opioid or benzodiazepine who presents with falls or confusion", "Pregnant patient who hides use for fear of child protective services", "Adolescent with declining grades and mood swings but no self-reported use", "Stimulant-induced psychosis that must be distinguished from a primary psychotic disorder", "Patient with a normal exam and normal labs who is seeking controlled substances"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
