such as perforation with otorrhea and persistent effusion with hearing loss kept in mind"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Toddler with a recent cold, fever, and ear tugging", "Otoscopy shows a bulging, opacified tympanic membrane with loss of the light reflex", "No pain with manipulation of the outer ear and no swelling behind the ear"], "medium": ["Infant who cannot localize pain and presents only with inconsolable crying and poor feeding", "Older child with mild symptoms where watchful waiting is the right choice", "Equivocal otoscopy requiring pneumatic otoscopy or tympanometry to confirm effusion", "Concurrent upper respiratory infection with cough and nasal congestion"], "hard": ["Spontaneous perforation with otorrhea and sudden relief of pain", "Symptoms persisting or worsening after 48 to 72 hours of appropriate antibiotics", "Swelling or redness behind the ear with the auricle pushed forward suggesting mastoiditis", "Severe headache, stiff neck, or lethargy suggesting meningitis or intracranial extension", "Adult with ear fullness and hearing loss after a cold, with little fever", "Immunocompromised child with rapidly worsening pain and high fever"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
