 exertion, and no fainting while lying down", "No tongue biting, incontinence, or prolonged confusion after the event", "Orthostatic vital signs and a normal ECG", "Bedside glucose checked to exclude hypoglycemia", "Pregnancy considered in anyone who could be pregnant", "Red flags for a cardiac cause reviewed, including exertional fainting, palpitations, abnormal ECG, and family history of sudden cardiac death"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Teenager or young adult who faints while standing in a warm, crowded room", "Clear warning of lightheadedness, nausea, and tunnel vision", "Quick full recovery with no injury", "Normal exam, orthostatic vitals, and ECG"], "medium": ["Older adult on a diuretic with a drop in blood pressure on standing", "Fainting with brief jerking movements that raises concern for seizure", "Recurrent episodes with no obvious trigger", "Mildly abnormal ECG that needs interpretation"], "hard": ["Fainting during exercise or while lying down suggesting a cardiac cause", "Fainting with palpitations and a family history of sudden cardiac death", "Older adult with no warning symptoms and a fall with injury", "Young child who appears pale and limp after a fall or crying", "Pregnant patient who faints when lying flat"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
