ith the bell and diaphragm", "finding": "New murmur suggesting valvular disease or anemia-related flow murmur", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "s3-gallop", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the apex with the bell in the left lateral position", "finding": "S3 gallop suggesting volume overload or heart failure", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "crackles", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lung fields bilaterally", "finding": "Bibasilar crackles", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "wheezing", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lung fields during quiet and forced expiration", "finding": "Diffuse wheezing suggesting obstructive lung disease", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "hepatomegaly", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Percuss and palpate the liver edge below the right costal margin", "finding": "Enlarged or tender liver", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "splenomegaly", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Percuss Traube space and palpate the left upper quadrant", "finding": "Palpable spleen tip", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "occult-blood-positive", "region": "rectal", "maneuver": "Perform a digital rectal exam and test the stool for occult blood", "finding": "Guaiac-positive stool", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "peripheral-edema", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Press over the dorsum of each foot and the pretibial area for 5 seconds", "finding": "Pitting edema", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "muscle-tenderness", "region": "musculoskeletal", "maneuver": "Palpate the major muscle groups and apply gentle pressure to tender points", "finding": "Diffuse muscle tenderness without weakness", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "proximal-weakness", "region": "musculoskeletal", "maneuver": "Test strength of shoulder abduction and hip flexion against resistance", "finding": "Proximal muscle weakness", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "dry-skin", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect and palpate the skin of the forearms and shins", "finding": "Dry, coarse skin", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "hair-loss", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the scalp and eyebrows", "finding": "Diffuse hair thinning or loss of the lateral eyebrows", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "psychomotor-retardation", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Observe speech rate, movement and response latency during the interview", "finding": "Slowed speech and movements", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "flat-affect", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Observe facial expression and emotional reactivity", "finding": "Flat or blunted affect", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-orientation", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Assess orientation to person, place and time and perform a brief cognitive screen", "finding": "Alert and fully oriented with normal cognition", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-focal-neuro", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Test cranial nerves, strength, sensation and deep tendon reflexes", "finding": "No focal neurologic deficit", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-heart-sounds", "region": "cardiac", "maneuver": "Auscultate the heart", "finding": "Normal S1 and S2 without murmur or gallop", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-lung-sounds", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lungs", "finding": "Clear breath sounds bilaterally without crackles or wheezing", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-abdomen", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Palpate the abdomen", "finding": "Soft, non-tender abdomen without organomegaly or mass", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-lymphadenopathy", "region": "lymph", "maneuver": "Palpate the cervical, supraclavicular, axillary and inguinal lymph node basins", "finding": "No palpable lymphadenopathy", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}]}, "vitals": {"temp": {"mild": {"min": 97.8, "max": 99.1}, "moderate": {"min": 98.0, "max": 99.5}, "severe": {"min": 97.5, "max": 100.0}, "critical": {"min": 96.5, "max": 101.5}}, "hr": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 70, "max": 110}, "severe": {"min": 80, "max": 120}, "critical": {"min": 90, "max": 140}}, "rr": {"mild": {"min": 12, "max": 20}, "moderate": {"min": 14, "max": 22}, "severe": {"min": 16, "max": 26}, "critical": {"min": 18, "max": 32}}, "sbp": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 130}, "moderate": {"min": 95, "max": 135}, "severe": {"min": 85, "max": 140}, "critical": {"min": 70, "max": 150}}, "dbp": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 85}, "moderate": {"min": 55, "max": 88}, "severe": {"min": 50, "max": 90}, "critical": {"min": 40, "max": 95}}, "spo2": {"mild": {"min": 95, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 92, "max": 99}, "severe": {"min": 88, "max": 96}, "critical": {"min": 80, "max": 92}}}, "labs": [{"test_id": "hgb", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 10.5, "max": 12.0}, "moderate": {"min": 8.5, "max": 11.0}, "severe": {"min": 6.5, "max": 9.0}, "critical": {"min": 4.5, "max": 7.0}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Anemia is one of the most common organic causes of fatigue; a normal hemoglobin does not exclude iron deficiency without anemia."}, {"test_id": "mcv", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 75, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 70, "max": 105}, "severe": {"min": 65, "max": 110}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low MCV suggests iron deficiency or thalassemia; high MCV suggests B12/folate deficiency, alcohol or hypothyroidism."}, {"test_id": "ferritin", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 8, "max": 24}, "moderate": {"min": 5, "max": 20}, "severe": {"min": 2, "max": 15}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low ferritin is the most specific marker of iron deficiency; it can be falsely normal in inflammation."}, {"test_id": "tsh", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 4.5, "max": 10.0}, "moderate": {"min": 8.0, "max": 20.0}, "severe": {"min": 15.0, "max": 60.0}, "critical": {"min": 20.0, "max": 100.0}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Elevated TSH suggests hypothyroidism; a low TSH suggests hyperthyroidism. Both can present with fatigue."}, {"test_id": "ft4", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 0.3, "max": 0.7}, "severe": {"min": 0.1, "max": 0.5}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low free T4 with high TSH confirms overt hypothyroidism."}, {"test_id": "glucose", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 125}, "moderate": {"min": 126, "max": 200}, "severe": {"min": 180, "max": 300}, "critical": {"min": 250, "max": 500}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hyperglycemia suggests undiagnosed or poorly controlled diabetes; hypoglycemia can also cause fatigue."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "moderate": {"min": 6.5, "max": 8.0}, "severe": {"min": 7.5, "max": 10.0}, "critical": {"min": 9.0, "max": 14.0}}, "frequency": "common", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Reflects average glucose over 2–3 months; useful when diabetes is suspected as the cause of fatigue."}, {"test_id": "cr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.6}, "moderate": {"min": 1.5, "max": 2.5}, "severe": {"min": 2.0, "max": 4.0}, "critical": {"min": 3.0, "max": 8.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Elevated creatinine suggests chronic kidney disease, which commonly causes fatigue."}, {"test_id": "na", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 130, "max": 134}, "moderate": {"min": 125, "max": 129}, "severe": {"min": 120, "max": 124}, "critical": {"min": 110, "max": 119}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hyponatremia can cause fatigue, confusion and weakness."}, {"test_id": "k", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 3.2, "max": 3.4}, "moderate": {"min": 2.8, "max": 3.1}, "severe": {"min": 2.5, "max": 2.7}, "critical": {"min": 2.0, "max": 2.4}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hypokalemia causes weakness and fatigue; hyperkalemia can also cause fatigue and arrhythmias."}, {"test_id": "ca", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 10.3, "max": 11.0}, "moderate": {"min": 11.0, "max": 12.0}, "severe": {"min": 12.0, "max": 14.0}, "critical": {"min": 13.0, "max": 16.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hypercalcemia causes fatigue, confusion and weakness; consider hyperparathyroidism or malignancy."}, {"test_id": "b12", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 150, "max": 199}, "moderate": {"min": 100, "max": 149}, "severe": {"min": 50, "max": 99}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Low B12 causes fatigue, macrocytic anemia and neurologic symptoms; can occur with normal MCV."}, {"test_id": "crp", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 1.1, "max": 3.0}, "moderate": {"min": 3.0, "max": 10.0}, "severe": {"min": 10.0, "max": 30.0}, "critical": {"min": 20.0, "max": 100.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Nonspecific; elevation suggests inflammation or infection but does not identify the cause."}, {"test_id": "esr", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 21, "max": 40}, "moderate": {"min": 40, "max": 70}, "severe": {"min": 70, "max": 100}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Nonspecific marker of inflammation; may be elevated in infection, autoimmune disease or malignancy."}, {"test_id": "ck", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 200, "max": 500}, "moderate": {"min": 500, "max": 2000}, "severe": {"min": 2000, "max": 10000}, "critical": {"min": 5000, "max": 50000}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Elevated CK suggests muscle disease (myositis, rhabdomyolysis) or strenuous exercise; consider if muscle weakness or tenderness is present."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Positive in pregnancy, which is a common cause of fatigue; must be checked in anyone who could be pregnant before imaging or teratogenic treatment."}, {"test_id": "ua_protein", "qualitative": {"mild": "Trace", "moderate": "1+", "severe": "2+", "critical": "3+"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Proteinuria suggests renal disease, which can cause fatigue."}, {"test_id": "ua_blood", "qualitative": {"mild": "Trace", "moderate": "1+", "severe": "2+", "critical": "3+"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Hematuria may indicate urinary tract infection, glomerulonephritis or malignancy."}], "ecg": {"findings": [{"feature": "rate", "finding": "Sinus tachycardia", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate"}, {"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Sinus bradycardia", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate"}, {"feature": "st", "finding": "ST-segment depression or T-wave flattening suggesting ischemia or strain", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "severe"}, {"feature": "t_wave", "finding": "Peaked T waves (hyperkalemia) or flattened T waves (hypokalemia)", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "severe"}, {"feature": "qt", "finding": "Prolonged QT interval (hypocalcemia, hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia or drug effect)", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "severe"}]}, "imaging": [{"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "findings": [{"text": "Cardiomegaly or pulmonary vascular congestion suggesting heart failure", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Hyperinflation or flattened diaphragms suggesting COPD", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Hilar lymphadenopathy or pulmonary nodule suggesting malignancy or infection", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Normal study", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "CT chest", "modality": "ct", "preferred_when": "Suspected malignancy, interstitial lung disease or pulmonary embolism when chest x-ray is nondiagnostic", "findings": [{"text": "Pulmonary nodule or mass", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Mediastinal or hilar lymphadenopathy", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Interstitial lung disease or emphysema", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Polysomnography (sleep study)", "modality": "other", "preferred_when": "Suspected obstructive sleep apnea or other sleep disorder", "findings": [{"text": "Apnea-hypopnea index greater than 5 events per hour", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Frequent arousals and sleep fragmentation", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Periodic limb movements of sleep", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Ultrasound thyroid", "modality": "ultrasound", "preferred_when": "Palpable thyroid nodule or abnormal thyroid function tests", "findings": [{"text": "Diffusely enlarged or nodular thyroid", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Solitary thyroid nodule", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "Screens for anemia, infection and hematologic malignancy"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Evaluates electrolytes, renal function and glucose as causes of fatigue"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Screens for hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Screens for diabetes mellitus"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Rules out pregnancy as a cause of fatigue and guides further testing", "only_if": "patient is of childbearing potential"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Screens for urinary infection or renal disease"}, {"test": "ferritin", "why": "Evaluates for iron deficiency, a common cause of fatigue even without anemia"}, {"test": "b12", "why": "Evaluates for vitamin B12 deficiency, which can cause fatigue and anemia"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "Polysomnography (sleep study)", "why": "Confirms obstructive sleep apnea or other sleep disorder when symptoms suggest it", "only_if": "daytime sleepiness, snoring or witnessed apneas are present"}, {"test": "Chest x-ray", "why": "Confirms heart failure, COPD or malignancy when suspected", "only_if": "dyspnea, cough or abnormal lung exam is present"}], "supporting": [{"test": "ft4", "why": "Confirms overt hypothyroidism when TSH is elevated"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Assesses for inflammation or infection when the cause is unclear"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "Assesses for inflammation, autoimmune disease or malignancy"}, {"test": "ck", "why": "Evaluates for muscle disease when muscle weakness or tenderness is present", "only_if": "muscle weakness or tenderness is present"}, {"test": "CT chest", "why": "Evaluates for malignancy or interstitial lung disease when chest x-ray is abnormal or symptoms persist", "only_if": "chest x-ray is abnormal or malignancy is suspected"}, {"test": "Ultrasound thyroid", "why": "Evaluates thyroid nodules or structural abnormalities", "only_if": "palpable thyroid nodule or abnormal thyroid function tests"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "Chest x-ray", "why": "Not routinely needed for fatigue without respiratory symptoms or abnormal lung exam"}, {"test": "CT chest", "why": "Not routinely needed for fatigue without suspicion of malignancy or lung disease"}, {"test": "Polysomnography (sleep study)", "why": "Not routinely needed for fatigue without symptoms of sleep apnea or other sleep disorder"}, {"test": "Ultrasound thyroid", "why": "Not routinely needed for fatigue without a palpable nodule or abnormal thyroid function tests"}, {"test": "d_dimer", "why": "No role in the evaluation of fatigue unless pulmonary embolism is suspected"}, {"test": "lactate", "why": "Not routinely needed for fatigue unless sepsis or tissue hypoperfusion is suspected"}], "decision_points": ["Pregnancy test before imaging or teratogenic treatment in anyone who could be pregnant", "Screen for depression and anxiety as part of the initial evaluation", "Review all medications and supplements for fatigue as a side effect", "Assess sleep quality and screen for obstructive sleep apnea"], "criteria": [], "scores": []}, "differential": [{"name": "Major depressive disorder", "slug": "major-depressive-disorder", "why_considered": "Depression is one of the most common causes of persistent fatigue and often presents with tiredness before the patient recognizes low mood.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fatigue plus low mood, loss of interest, or sleep and appetite change lasting at least two weeks", "discriminators": {"history": ["Depressed mood or loss of interest most of the day, nearly every day", "Early morning waking or hypersomnia", "Appetite or weight change", "Feelings of guilt, worthlessness or hopelessness", "Fatigue is present even after adequate rest"], "exam": ["Flat or blunted affect", "Psychomotor retardation or agitation", "Poor eye contact and slowed speech"], "labs": ["Normal hemoglobin, TSH, glucose and metabolic panel", "No laboratory test confirms depression; workup is to exclude organic causes"]}}, {"name": "Hypothyroidism", "slug": "hypothyroidism", "why_considered": "Hypothyroidism is a classic endocrine cause of fatigue, often with subtle symptoms that the patient attributes to aging or stress.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fatigue with cold intolerance, weight gain, constipation or dry skin", "discriminators": {"history": ["Cold intolerance", "Weight gain despite unchanged diet", "Constipation", "Dry skin and hair thinning", "Menorrhagia"], "exam": ["Diffusely enlarged, nodular or firm thyroid", "Dry, coarse skin", "Bradycardia", "Delayed relaxation phase of deep tendon reflexes", "Periorbital puffiness"], "labs": ["Elevated TSH", "Low free T4 in overt disease", "Normocytic or macrocytic anemia"], "imaging": ["Diffusely enlarged or nodular thyroid on ultrasound when a nodule is palpable"]}}, {"name": "Anemia", "slug": "anemia", "why_considered": "Anemia reduces oxygen delivery and is a common, easily missed cause of fatigue, especially in menstruating or older patients.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fatigue with pallor, exertional dyspnea or heavy menstrual bleeding", "discriminators": {"history": ["Heavy or prolonged menstrual periods", "Pica or craving ice", "Black or bloody stools", "Family history of anemia or blood disorder", "Recent weight loss or GI symptoms suggesting occult bleeding"], "exam": ["Pale conjunctivae", "Pallor of the palmar creases", "Tachycardia", "Flow murmur", "Guaiac-positive stool"], "labs": ["Low hemoglobin and hematocrit", "Low MCV in iron deficiency", "Low ferritin", "High MCV with low B12 or folate"]}}, {"name": "Obstructive sleep apnea", "slug": "obstructive-sleep-apnea", "why_considered": "Sleep fragmentation from apnea causes daytime fatigue and sleepiness that patients often describe simply as tiredness.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Loud snoring", "Witnessed apneas or gasping at night", "Unrefreshing sleep despite adequate hours", "Morning headaches", "Daytime sleepiness while driving or reading"], "exam": ["Obesity or large neck circumference", "Crowded oropharynx or large tonsils", "Elevated blood pressure"], "labs": ["Normal hemoglobin and TSH", "Elevated bicarbonate in chronic hypercapnia"], "imaging": ["Apnea-hypopnea index greater than 5 events per hour on polysomnography", "Frequent arousals and sleep fragmentation on polysomnography"]}}, {"name": "Diabetes mellitus", "slug": "diabetes-mellitus", "why_considered": "Poorly controlled diabetes causes fatigue through hyperglycemia, osmotic diuresis and associated kidney or thyroid disease.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Excessive thirst and frequent urination", "Unexplained weight loss", "Blurred vision", "Recurrent infections", "Family history of diabetes"], "exam": ["Obesity", "Acanthosis nigricans", "Peripheral neuropathy", "Poorly healing wounds"], "labs": ["Elevated fasting glucose", "Elevated hemoglobin A1c", "Glucose or ketones in urine"]}}, {"name": "Chronic kidney disease", "slug": "chronic-kidney-disease", "why_considered": "Uremia, anemia of chronic disease and electrolyte abnormalities in kidney disease all produce fatigue.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Longstanding hypertension or diabetes", "Nocturia", "Swelling of the legs", "Poor appetite and nausea", "Family history of kidney disease"], "exam": ["Pitting peripheral edema", "Pallor", "Sallow skin", "Hypertension"], "labs": ["Elevated creatinine", "Low hemoglobin", "Proteinuria on urinalysis", "Hyperkalemia or metabolic acidosis"], "imaging": ["Small echogenic kidneys on ultrasound"]}}, {"name": "Medication side effect", "slug": "medication-side-effect", "why_considered": "Many commonly prescribed drugs cause fatigue, and the timing of symptoms often tracks with a new or increased medication.", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Fatigue began after starting or increasing a medication", "Use of antidepressants, antihistamines, beta blockers, opioids, diuretics or sedative-hypnotics", "Alcohol or substance use", "Symptoms improve when the drug is held"], "exam": ["Sedation or slowed cognition", "Orthostatic hypotension", "Bradycardia"], "labs": ["Normal hemoglobin, TSH and metabolic panel", "Drug levels when available"]}}, {"name": "Malignancy", "slug": "malignancy", "why_considered": "Occult cancer can present with fatigue alone, particularly in older adults, before any localizing symptom appears.", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fatigue with unintentional weight loss, night sweats or a new focal symptom in an older adult", "discriminators": {"history": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Night sweats", "New persistent pain", "Change in bowel habits", "Heavy or postmenopausal vaginal bleeding"], "exam": ["Firm, fixed or generalized lymphadenopathy", "Palpable mass or organomegaly", "Guaiac-positive stool", "Cachexia"], "labs": ["Anemia, often normocytic", "Elevated ESR or CRP", "Elevated calcium", "Abnormal liver enzymes"], "imaging": ["Mass, lymphadenopathy or organ lesion on CT", "Abnormal chest x-ray"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Intermittent tiredness that the patient notices but that does not limit work, school or self-care; normal vital signs and exam; labs may be normal or show a mild abnormality such as borderline anemia or a slightly elevated TSH.", "moderate": "Persistent fatigue that interferes with daily activities, concentration and mood; may be accompanied by mild tachycardia, pallor or other subtle exam findings; labs often show a treatable cause such as anemia, hypothyroidism or diabetes.", "severe": "Fatigue that prevents the patient from working or performing basic self-care; may be accompanied by weight loss, marked pallor, dyspnea on minimal exertion or significant psychomotor slowing; labs frequently show a serious underlying cause.", "critical": "Fatigue with hemodynamic instability, severe anemia, sepsis, adrenal crisis or another immediately life-threatening cause; the patient appears acutely unwell and requires urgent stabilization."}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Unintentional weight loss", "meaning": "Suggests malignancy, chronic infection or advanced organ disease"}, {"finding": "Fever or night sweats", "meaning": "Suggests infection, malignancy or inflammatory disease"}, {"finding": "Focal neurologic deficit or new severe headache", "meaning": "Suggests stroke, mass lesion or central nervous system infection"}, {"finding": "Chest pain or exertional dyspnea", "meaning": "Suggests cardiac ischemia, heart failure or pulmonary embolism"}, {"finding": "Syncope or near-syncope", "meaning": "Suggests arrhythmia, severe anemia or volume depletion"}, {"finding": "Suicidal thoughts", "meaning": "Requires immediate psychiatric evaluation and safety planning"}, {"finding": "Pallor with tachycardia or hypotension", "meaning": "Suggests severe anemia or acute blood loss"}, {"finding": "New lymphadenopathy or organomegaly", "meaning": "Suggests malignancy or serious systemic disease"}], "complications": [{"name": "Reduced work or school performance", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Difficulty concentrating", "Missed work or school days", "Falling behind on tasks"]}, {"name": "Depression or anxiety", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Persistent low mood", "Loss of interest", "Sleep disturbance"]}, {"name": "Motor vehicle or workplace injury", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Daytime sleepiness", "Falling asleep while driving", "Near-miss accidents"]}, {"name": "Progression of the underlying disease", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Worsening fatigue despite rest", "New focal symptoms", "Weight loss or fever"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Fatigue may be the only sign of serious illness such as infection, heart failure, anemia or malignancy; patients often underreport it as 'just getting older', so a lower threshold for workup is appropriate."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Fatigue is common and expected, especially in the first and third trimesters, but can also mask anemia, thyroid disease or depression; pregnancy itself must be considered as a cause."}, {"population": "children", "differences": "Children may present with irritability, poor school performance, falling asleep in class or refusal to play rather than saying they are tired; consider sleep disorders, anemia and infection."}, {"population": "diabetes", "differences": "Fatigue may reflect poor glycemic control, hypoglycemia or associated kidney or thyroid disease rather than a primary sleep or mood cause."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Fatigue is often driven by obstructive sleep apnea and deconditioning; daytime sleepiness may dominate over generalized weariness."}, {"population": "renal_impairment", "differences": "Anemia of chronic disease, uremia and electrolyte abnormalities are common contributors; fatigue may worsen as kidney function declines."}, {"population": "hepatic_impairment", "differences": "Fatigue is common in chronic liver disease and may precede other signs; consider hepatic encephalopathy if there is confusion or asterixis."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "When did the tiredness start, and has it been getting worse?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Gradual onset over weeks to months; persistent or progressive rather than a single bad night"}, {"question": "How long has this lasted?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Weeks to months; fatigue lasting more than several weeks warrants a workup"}, {"question": "Is the tiredness there all day, or does it come and go?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Present most of the day, often worse in the afternoon or after activity"}, {"question": "Does rest or a good night's sleep make it better?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Only partially relieved by rest; unrefreshing sleep suggests a sleep disorder or depression"}, {"question": "How much is this affecting your work, school or daily activities?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Interference with usual activities; severity and functional impact"}, {"question": "How many hours do you sleep, and do you snore or wake up gasping?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Loud snoring, witnessed apneas, unrefreshing sleep, daytime sleepiness suggesting obstructive sleep apnea"}, {"question": "Have you been feeling down, sad or losing interest in things you enjoy?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Low mood or anhedonia lasting at least two weeks, suggesting depression"}, {"question": "Have you had any fever, night sweats or weight loss you did not intend?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Constitutional symptoms suggesting infection, malignancy or inflammatory disease"}, {"question": "Have you noticed shortness of breath with activity, or chest pain?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Exertional dyspnea or chest pain suggesting anemia, heart failure or cardiac ischemia"}, {"question": "Have you had any heavy periods, blood in your stool or black stools?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Sources of blood loss suggesting iron deficiency anemia or GI bleeding"}, {"question": "Do you feel cold or hot when others do not, or has your weight changed?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Cold intolerance and weight gain suggest hypothyroidism; heat intolerance and weight loss suggest hyperthyroidism"}, {"question": "Have you had any dizziness or lightheadedness when standing up?", "category": "associated", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Orthostatic symptoms suggesting volume depletion, anemia or medication effect"}, {"question": "What medical conditions do you have, and how well are they controlled?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Diabetes, COPD, heart, liver or kidney disease, hypothyroidism, anemia, cancer or recent surgery"}, {"question": "What medications and supplements are you taking, and did any start around the time the fatigue began?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Antidepressants, antihistamines, opioids, beta blockers, diuretics, antiemetics, sedative-hypnotics or corticosteroids as a cause"}, {"question": "How much alcohol do you drink, and do you use any recreational drugs?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Heavy alcohol or substance use contributing to fatigue"}, {"question": "How much caffeine do you have each day, and how is your sleep schedule?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Excess caffeine, shift work or irregular sleep contributing to poor sleep quality"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have thyroid disease, anemia, depression or sleep apnea?", "category": "family", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Family history that raises suspicion for a hereditary or familial cause"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last menstrual period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy as a cause of fatigue and a reason to avoid teratogenic testing or treatment"}, {"question": "Have you had any thoughts of hurting yourself or that you would be better off dead?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Suicidal thoughts requiring immediate psychiatric evaluation and safety planning"}], "accepted_names": ["Fatigue", "Tiredness", "Weariness", "Lack of energy", "Generalized fatigue"], "reasoning_points": ["Fatigue is a symptom, not a diagnosis, so the workup is directed at finding the underlying cause", "Duration of more than several weeks and interference with daily activities make it clinically significant", "The differential spans anemia, thyroid disease, diabetes, kidney and liver disease, sleep disorders, depression and anxiety, medication side effects and malignancy", "A complete medication and supplement review is needed because many common drugs cause fatigue", "Sleep quality and symptoms of obstructive sleep apnea should be assessed directly", "Depression and anxiety should be screened for as part of the initial evaluation, not only after organic causes are excluded", "Pregnancy must be considered and tested for in anyone of childbearing potential", "Red flags such as unintentional weight loss, fever, night sweats, focal neurologic deficits, syncope or suicidal thoughts change the urgency of the evaluation", "Initial laboratory testing includes a CBC, metabolic panel, TSH, A1c, pregnancy test, urinalysis, ferritin and vitamin B12", "Normal initial labs do not end the evaluation; the history and exam guide further testing such as a sleep study or chest imaging"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Young or middle-aged adult with a clear story of poor sleep, high stress or a new medication", "Fatigue with obvious pallor and heavy menstrual bleeding pointing to iron deficiency anemia", "Fatigue with cold intolerance, weight gain and constipation pointing to hypothyroidism", "Fatigue with low mood and anhedonia pointing to depression", "Vital signs and physical exam are normal apart from the findings of the underlying cause"], "medium": ["Fatigue with a normal exam and normal initial labs, requiring a broader workup", "Older adult with fatigue as the only complaint and no localizing symptoms", "Fatigue in a patient with diabetes, COPD or kidney disease where the cause could be the disease itself or a complication", "Fatigue with daytime sleepiness and snoring where obstructive sleep apnea is the likely cause", "Fatigue in a patient taking several medications that could each contribute"], "hard": ["Fatigue with unintentional weight loss, night sweats or new lymphadenopathy raising concern for malignancy", "Fatigue with exertional dyspnea and tachycardia suggesting significant anemia or cardiac disease", "Fatigue with suicidal thoughts requiring immediate psychiatric evaluation", "Fatigue in pregnancy where the symptom is expected but can also mask anemia, thyroid disease or depression", "Fatigue in a child presenting with irritability, poor school performance or refusal to play rather than saying they are tired", "Fatigue with focal neurologic deficits or a new severe headache suggesting a central nervous system cause"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
