ns, chicks or ducklings", "Recent restaurant meal or catered event"], "risk_medications": ["proton pump inhibitors", "histamine-2 receptor antagonists", "immunosuppressants", "corticosteroids", "antibiotics"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I've been throwing up and having diarrhea", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "My stomach is cramping", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I feel like I can't keep anything down", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I've been running to the bathroom all night", "frequency": "common"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Sudden, over hours; often within 1–48 hours of the suspect meal, though some organisms cause symptoms days later", "duration": "Usually 1–7 days; most resolve without treatment", "progression": "Starts with nausea and abdominal discomfort, then vomiting and/or diarrhea; symptoms peak in the first day or two and gradually improve", "location": "Diffuse abdominal pain, often periumbilical or lower abdomen", "radiation": "Usually none", "quality": "Crampy, intermittent abdominal pain; watery stools", "severity": "Mild to moderate for most; can be severe with profuse diarrhea, vomiting or dehydration", "timing": "Cramps come in waves, often worse before a bowel movement", "aggravating": ["Eating or drinking", "Certain foods or dairy"], "relieving": ["Resting", "Sipping fluids", "Passing stool or vomiting"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Diarrhea", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Abdominal cramps", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Vomiting", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Low-grade fever or chills", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Muscle aches and headache", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Lightheadedness or dry mouth from dehydration", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Blood or mucus in the stool", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Bloody diarrhea", "High fever above 102°F", "Severe localized right lower quadrant pain", "