ar description of nausea", "Localized abdominal cramping"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "May have milder fever and less pain but dehydrate quickly; confusion or falls can be the presenting problem.", "missing_classic_features": ["Fever", "Prominent abdominal cramps"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "More severe, prolonged or invasive disease; higher risk of bacteremia and need for hospitalization.", "missing_classic_features": ["Self-limited course"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Dehydration and electrolyte loss are tolerated poorly; listeriosis can cause fever, myalgias and fetal loss with few GI symptoms.", "missing_classic_features": ["Prominent diarrhea"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Alert, comfortable, well hydrated; mild discomfort between cramps", "moderate": "Uncomfortable, frequent trips to the bathroom, dry lips, mild tachycardia", "severe": "Ill-appearing, weak, sunken eyes, dry mucous membranes, visibly dehydrated", "critical": "Lethargic or confused, cold clammy skin, minimal urine output, shock"}, "findings": [{"id": "diffuse-abdominal-tenderness", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Palpate all four quadrants, starting away from the area of maximal pain", "finding": "Diffuse, mild to moderate abdominal tenderness without localization", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "hyperactive-bowel-sounds", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Auscultate the abdomen in all four quadrants", "finding": "Hyperactive, high-pitched bowel sounds", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-guarding-rigidity", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Palpate deeply and ask the patient to cough", "finding": "No guarding, rigidity or rebound tenderness", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "no-localized-rlq-tenderness", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Press at McBurney point", "finding": "No point tenderness at McBurney point", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "dry-mucous-membranes", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the oral mucosa and tongue", "finding": "Dry, tacky mucous membranes", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "sunken-eyes", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the eyes and periorbital area", "finding": "Sunken eyes with reduced tear production", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "prolonged-capillary-refill", "region": "extremities", "maneuver": "Press the fingertip or nail bed and time the return of color", "finding": "Capillary refill longer than 2 seconds", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "reduced-skin-turgor", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Pinch the skin over the forearm or abdomen and release", "finding": "Skin tents and returns slowly", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-rash", "region": "skin", "maneuver": "Inspect the skin over the trunk and extremities", "finding": "No rash, hives or flushing", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-cva-tenderness", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Percuss the costovertebral angles", "finding": "No costovertebral angle tenderness", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "normal-mental-status", "region": "mental_status", "maneuver": "Assess orientation to person, place and time", "finding": "Alert and oriented, no confusion", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-focal-neuro-deficit", "reg