ive bacterial infection; guides resuscitation."}, {"test_id": "crp", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 1.0, "max": 5.0}, "severe": {"min": 4.0, "max": 15.0}, "critical": {"min": 10.0, "max": 30.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional"}, {"test_id": "procalcitonin", "ranges": {"severe": {"min": 0.5, "max": 2.0}, "critical": {"min": 2.0, "max": 10.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "A low value favors a viral or toxin-mediated cause; a high value favors invasive bacterial infection."}, {"test_id": "ua_sg", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 1.025, "max": 1.035}, "severe": {"min": 1.03, "max": 1.04}, "critical": {"min": 1.03, "max": 1.045}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "High specific gravity reflects concentrated urine from dehydration."}, {"test_id": "ua_ketones", "qualitative": {"moderate": "Small", "severe": "Moderate", "critical": "Large"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "From poor intake and vomiting; not specific."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Negative. Required in anyone who could be pregnant before imaging or medication choices; rules out ectopic pregnancy and hyperemesis gravidarum."}], "ecg": {"findings": [{"feature": "rate", "finding": "Sinus tachycardia from dehydration, fever or pain", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate"}, {"feature": "rhythm", "finding": "Sinus rhythm; irregularly irregular rhythm suggests atrial fibrillation from electrolyte disturbance or sepsis", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe"}, {"feature": "t_wave", "finding": "Flattened T waves and prominent U waves from hypokalemia", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "severe"}, {"feature": "st", "finding": "ST depression or nonspecific ST-T changes with severe hypokalemia or hypoperfusion", "frequency": "rare", "min_severity": "critical"}, {"feature": "qt", "finding": "Prolonged QT interval from hypokalem