g", "Unilateral pelvic pain", "No diarrheal illness or food exposure"], "exam": ["Adnexal tenderness or mass", "Peritoneal signs if ruptured", "Cervical motion tenderness"], "labs": ["Positive hCG", "Falling hematocrit if ruptured"], "imaging": ["No intrauterine pregnancy on transvaginal ultrasound", "Adnexal mass or free fluid"]}}, {"name": "Urinary tract infection or pyelonephritis", "slug": "urinary-tract-infection", "why_considered": "Abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting can accompany a urinary source", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Dysuria, urgency, frequency", "Flank pain", "No diarrhea or food exposure"], "exam": ["Costovertebral angle tenderness", "Suprapubic tenderness", "Fever"], "labs": ["Pyuria and bacteriuria on urinalysis", "Positive urine culture"], "imaging": ["Normal bowel on CT", "Perinephric stranding if pyelonephritis"]}}, {"name": "Mesenteric ischemia", "slug": "mesenteric-ischemia", "why_considered": "Severe abdominal pain with vomiting and diarrhea, especially in older adults", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Pain out of proportion to exam, older patient with vascular risk factors", "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden severe pain, often after meals", "Atrial fibrillation or vascular disease", "Little or no diarrhea initially"], "exam": ["Diffuse tenderness with a relatively benign abdomen early", "Peritoneal signs late", "Hypotension"], "labs": ["Marked leukocytosis", "Elevated lactate", "Metabolic acidosis"], "imaging": ["Vascular occlusion or bowel wall ischemia on CT angiography"]}}, {"name": "Scombroid (histamine) fish poisoning", "slug": "scombroid-fish-poisoning", "why_considered": "Sudden GI symptoms after eating fish, can be confused with infectious foodborne illness", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Symptoms within minutes to an hour of eating fish", "Flushing, headache, palpitations", "Often multiple people affected at the same meal"], "exam": ["Flushing, urticaria, tachycardia", "No fever", "No significant dehydration"], "labs": ["No specific lab test; diagnosis is clinical"], "imaging": ["Not indicated"]}}, {"name": "Viral gastroenteritis (norovirus, rotavirus)", "slug": "viral-gastroenteritis", "why_considered": "Overlapping presentation with foodborne illness; often indistinguishable without exposure history", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Sick contacts with similar illness before the patient's symptoms", "No specific food exposure", "Winter seasonality for norovirus"], "exam": ["Diffuse mild abdominal tenderness", "No focal findings"], "labs": ["Stool PCR may identify norovirus or rotavirus", "Stool culture negative"], "imaging": ["Not indicated"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Acute onset of nausea, vomiting or diarrhea with mild cramps, no fever or low-grade fever, able to tolerate oral fluids, no dehydration, symptoms lasting less than 48 hours", "moderate": "Persistent vomiting or diarrhea with moderate cramps, low-grade fever, mild dehydration (dry mucous membranes, tachycardia), able to take some oral fluids but may need IV fluids", "severe": "Profuse diarrhea or vomiting with severe cramps, high fever, marked dehydration (sunken eyes, prolonged capillary refill, reduced skin turgor), orthostatic hypotension, electrolyte abnormalities, unable to tolerate oral intake", "critical": "Hypovolemic shock, severe electrolyte derangements (hypokalemia, hyponatremia, metabolic acidosis), acute kidney injury, altered mental status, or signs of invasive bacterial infection with sepsis"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Bloody diarrhea", "meaning": "Suggests invasive bacterial infection (e.g., Shigella, Salmonella, E. coli O157:H7) or inflammatory colitis; requires stool testing and possible antibiotics"}, {"finding": "High fever above 102°F", "meaning": "Suggests invasive bacterial infection or systemic illness; warrants further workup"}, {"finding": "Severe dehydration (sunken eyes, prolonged capillary refill, reduced skin turgor, oliguria)", "meaning": "Requires immediate IV fluid resuscitation and electrolyte assessment"}, {"finding": "Hypotension or tachycardia", "meaning": "May indicate hypovolemic shock or sepsis; needs urgent resuscitation"}, {"finding": "Altered mental status or confusion", "meaning": "Suggests severe dehydration, electrolyte imbalance, or sepsis; urgent evaluation"}, {"finding": "Symptoms lasting more than 7 days", "meaning": "Suggests a non-infectious cause, parasitic infection, or post-infectious complication"}, {"finding": "Recent antibiotic use or hospitalization", "meaning": "Raises concern for C. difficile colitis"}, {"finding": "Immunocompromised state", "meaning": "Higher risk of severe, prolonged or invasive disease; lower threshold for testing and treatment"}], "complications": [{"name": "Dehydration and hypovolemic shock", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Poor oral intake", "Profuse diarrhea or vomiting", "Tachycardia, hypotension, oliguria", "Sunken eyes, dry mucous membranes"]}, {"name": "Electrolyte abnormalities (hypokalemia, hyponatremia, metabolic acidosis)", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Muscle weakness, cramps", "Cardiac arrhythmias", "Abnormal bicarbonate and potassium on BMP"]}, {"name": "Acute kidney injury", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Rising creatinine and BUN", "Oliguria", "Dehydration"]}, {"name": "Bacteremia and sepsis", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["High fever, hypotension, tachycardia", "Positive blood cultures", "Elevated lactate"]}, {"name": "Hemolytic uremic syndrome (HUS)", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Bloody diarrhea followed by anemia, thrombocytopenia, and renal failure", "Most commonly after E. coli O157:H7 infection"]}, {"name": "Reactive arthr