r bacterial infection"}, {"question": "What did you eat in the 1–3 days before you got sick?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Specific high-risk foods: undercooked poultry, eggs, ground beef, unpasteurized dairy, raw seafood, sprouts, leftovers left out"}, {"question": "Have you had diarrhea? Is there blood or mucus in it?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Bloody diarrhea suggests invasive bacterial infection (Shigella, Salmonella, E. coli O157:H7, Campylobacter) and changes management"}, {"question": "Have you been vomiting? How many times, and can you keep fluids down?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Profuse vomiting with inability to keep fluids down predicts dehydration and need for IV fluids"}, {"question": "How many stools have you had in the last 24 hours?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Frequency and volume help gauge severity and dehydration risk"}, {"question": "Any fever or chills?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "High fever above 102°F suggests invasive bacterial infection; low-grade or absent fever is typical of viral or toxin-mediated illness"}, {"question": "Has anyone else you ate with gotten sick?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Multiple people ill after the same meal points to a common food source or outbreak"}, {"question": "Have you recently taken antibiotics or been in the hospital?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Recent antibiotics or healthcare exposure raises concern for C. difficile colitis"}, {"question": "Have you traveled recently, or been around reptiles, amphibians, or farm animals?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Travel to areas with poor sanitation or animal contact suggests specific pathogens (Salmonella, Campylobacter, parasites)"}, {"question": "Do you have any conditions or take medicines that weaken your immune system?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Immunosuppression, diabetes, chronic kidney disease, or acid-suppressing medications increase risk of severe or invasive disease"}, {"question": "Are you pregnant, or could you be pregnant?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy changes the differential (listeriosis) and limits medication choices; also rules out ectopic pregnancy and hyperemesis"}, {"question": "How much are you urinating, and are you able to drink fluids?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Decreased urination, dry mouth, and lightheadedness indicate dehydration"}, {"question": "Any severe or localized abdominal pain, or pain out of proportion to the exam?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Severe localized pain, peritoneal signs, or pain out of proportion suggests a surgical abdomen or mesenteric ischemia"}, {"question": "Any confusion, weakness, or fainting?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Altered mental status or syncope suggests severe dehydration, electrolyte imbalance, or sepsis"}], "accepted_names": ["Foodborne illness", "Food poisoning", "Foodborne disease", "Foodborne infection", "Infectious gastroenteritis (foodborne)", "Acute gastroenteritis (foodborne)"], "reasoning_points": ["Acute onset of nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and abdominal cramps after a suspicious meal or food exposure", "Incubation period helps narrow the likely organism (toxin-mediated vs. infectious)", "Presence or absence of bloody diarrhea, high fever, and severe dehydration guides testing and treatment", "Risk factors such as undercooked meat, unpasteurized dairy, travel, animal contact, and immunosuppression are identified", "Red flags for invasive bacterial infection, C. difficile, or a surgical abdomen are specifically sought", "Pregnancy is excluded before imaging or medication choices", "Hydration status is assessed and oral rehydration is preferred when tolerated", "Stool testing is reserved for bloody diarrhea, high fever, severe or prolonged illness, immunocompromise, recent antibiotics or travel, or outbreak settings", "Antimotility agents are avoided when there is bloody diarrhea or high fever", "Alternative diagnoses such as appendicitis, ectopic pregnancy, urinary tract infection, mesenteric ischemia, and IBD flare are considered and ruled out"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Classic story: sudden nausea, vomiting, and watery diarrhea within hours of a suspect meal", "Multiple people ill after the same gathering", "Mild dehydration, able to tolerate oral fluids", "No blood in stool, no high fever", "Clear food exposure (e.g., undercooked chicken, leftover rice)"], "medium": ["Bloody diarrhea with fever, requiring stool testing and consideration of antibiotics", "Recent antibiotic use raising concern for C. difficile", "Older adult or young child with moderate dehydration and electrolyte abnormalities", "Symptoms lasting more than a week suggesting parasitic infection", "Pregnant patient with fever and myalgias suggesting listeriosis"], "hard": ["Immunocompromised patient with severe, prolonged diarrhea and risk of bacteremia", "Patient with severe abdominal pain out of proportion to exam suggesting mesenteric ischemia", "Overlap with appendicitis or ectopic pregnancy in a patient of reproductive age", "Scombroid fish poisoning presenting with flushing and GI symptoms after fish", "Patient with no clear food exposure and a non-infectious cause such as IBD flare"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
