 therapy", "Ceftriaxone", "Octreotide", "Fibrates"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "My stomach hurts under my right ribs", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "The pain comes in waves after I eat", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I feel sick to my stomach", "frequency": "common"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Sudden, often awakening the patient from sleep or starting within an hour after a meal", "duration": "Episodes last 30 minutes to several hours; symptoms may have been recurring for weeks to months", "progression": "Steady intense pain that plateaus rather than building continuously; resolves spontaneously or with pain medication, but recurs with subsequent fatty meals", "location": "Right upper quadrant or epigastrium", "radiation": "May radiate to the right shoulder, right scapula, or mid-back", "quality": "Constant, aching, or pressure-like; sometimes described as gripping", "severity": "Moderate to severe, often 6–9/10 at peak", "timing": "Postprandial, typically 30–60 minutes after eating, especially after fatty or fried foods; may occur at night", "aggravating": ["Eating fatty or greasy meals", "Large meals", "Lying flat or bending over"], "relieving": ["Nothing consistently; sometimes sitting upright or walking helps slightly", "Pain medication may partially relieve it"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Vomiting", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Belching or bloating", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Low-grade fever (if cholecystitis develops)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dark urine or light-colored stools (if bile duct obstruction)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Itching (if bile duct obstruction)", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Pain that starts in the epigastrium and migrates to the right lower quadrant", "Pain that is clearly pleuritic or positional", "Burning epigastric pain relieved by food or antacids", "Pain radiating to the left arm or jaw", "Dysuria, frequency, or hematuria", "Vaginal bleeding or discharge", "Weight loss or loss of appetite", "Hematemesis or melena"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Feeling tired during attacks", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["High fever", "Chills", "Night sweats", "Weight loss"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Vomiting", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Bloating or belching", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Jaundice", "Dark urine", "Light-colored stools", "Blood in vomit or stool", "Chronic diarrhea"], "argues_against": ["Pain that migrates to the right lower quadrant", "Pain relieved by bowel movement or antacids"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Chest pain", "Shortness of breath", "Palpitations"], "argues_against": ["Pain radiating to the left arm or jaw", "Exertional chest pressure"]}, {"system": "genitourinary", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Dysuria", "Frequency", "Hematuria", "Flank pain"], "argues_against": ["Colicky flank pain radiating to the groin"]}, {"system": "reproductive", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Vaginal bleeding", "Vaginal discharge", "Missed period"], "argues_against": ["Sudden one-sided pelvic pain", "Missed period"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "May present with vague abdominal discomfort, anorexia, or confusion rather than classic colicky pain; pain may be less severe.", "missing_classic_features": ["Severe postprandial right upper quadrant pain", "Nausea and vomiting"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Symptoms may be attributed to normal pregnancy discomfort; right upper quadrant pain can be mistaken for preeclampsia or HELLP syndrome.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear postprandial pattern"]}, {"population": "diabetes", "how_it_differs": "May have atypical or blunted pain due to autonomic neuropathy; higher risk of severe complications like emp