disease or obesity and may present with vague abdominal pain."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "Where exactly is the pain, and does it move anywhere?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Right upper quadrant or epigastric pain, sometimes radiating to the right shoulder, right scapula, or mid-back"}, {"question": "When did the pain start, and how long does an episode last?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Episodes lasting 30 minutes to several hours that resolve; pain lasting more than 6 hours suggests cholecystitis"}, {"question": "What were you doing when the pain started? Does it come on after eating?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Onset 30–60 minutes after a meal, especially a fatty or fried meal, or waking the patient at night"}, {"question": "Does the pain come in waves, or is it constant?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Steady, intense pain that plateaus rather than building continuously; recurring episodes over weeks to months"}, {"question": "Does anything make the pain better or worse?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Worse with fatty meals, large meals, lying flat, or bending over; nothing consistently relieves it"}, {"question": "Have you had nausea or vomiting with the pain?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Nausea and vomiting accompanying the pain"}, {"question": "Have you had a fever or chills?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Fever and chills suggest acute cholecystitis or cholangitis rather than simple biliary colic"}, {"question": "Have you noticed yellowing of your eyes or skin, dark urine, or pale stools?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Jaundice, dark urine, or light-colored stools suggest a common bile duct stone or obstruction"}, {"question": "Have you had any itching?", "category": "associated", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Pruritus from cholestasis when the bile duct is obstructed"}, {"question": "Have you had gallstones or gallbladder problems before, or any abdominal surgery?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prior episodes of biliary colic, prior cholecystitis, or prior cholecystectomy"}, {"question": "Do you take any estrogen-containing medications, such as birth control pills or hormone replacement therapy?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Estrogen exposure increases gallstone risk"}, {"question": "Has anyone in your family had gallstones or gallbladder surgery?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Gallstones in a first-degree relative"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant? When was your last menstrual period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy increases gallstone risk and must be excluded before imaging and any intervention"}, {"question": "What is your typical diet and activity level? Have you lost weight recently?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "High-fat diet, sedentary lifestyle, or rapid weight loss"}, {"question": "Any burning with urination, blood in the urine, or flank pain?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Absent; present suggests a urinary cause such as a kidney stone"}, {"question": "Any chest pain, shortness of breath, or pain radiating to the left arm or jaw?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Absent; present raises concern for acute coronary syndrome"}], "accepted_names": ["Gallstones", "Cholelithiasis", "Biliary colic", "Gallstone disease", "Gallbladder stones"], "reasoning_points": ["Recurrent episodes of right upper quadrant or epigastric pain lasting 30 minutes to several hours, coming on 30–60 minutes after fatty meals", "Pain may radiate to the rig