eastbone (mid-chest), sometimes rising into the throat", "radiation": "Can radiate upward toward the throat or neck; occasionally to the back", "quality": "Burning or warm, sometimes sour or acid-like", "severity": "Mild to moderate; usually 3–6/10, worse after meals", "timing": "Typically 30–60 minutes after meals and when lying down or bending over", "aggravating": ["Large or fatty meals", "Lying down or bending over soon after eating", "Spicy foods, chocolate, caffeine, citrus, tomato", "Alcohol", "Tight clothing around the waist"], "relieving": ["Antacids", "Sitting upright or standing", "Smaller meals", "Avoiding food close to bedtime", "Elevating the head of the bed"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Regurgitation of sour or bitter fluid", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Water brash (sudden excess saliva)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Chronic dry cough", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Hoarse or raspy voice, especially in the morning", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Sensation of a lump in the throat", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Belching", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Wheezing or asthma-like symptoms", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Trouble swallowing solid food", "Painful swallowing", "Vomiting blood or coffee-ground material", "Black or tarry stools", "Unintentional weight loss", "Chest pain with shortness of breath, sweating, or pain radiating to the jaw or arm", "Anemia", "Choking or coughing up food at night"]}, "ros": [{"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Heartburn after meals", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Regurgitation of sour fluid", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Belching", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Dysphagia", "Odynophagia", "Hematemesis", "Melena", "Early satiety", "Jaundice"], "argues_against": ["Progressive solid-food dysphagia", "Gastrointestinal bleeding"]}, {"system": "respiratory", "positives": [{"text": "Dry cough", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Wheezing", "frequency": "rare"}], "negatives": ["Productive cough with fever", "Hemoptysis", "Pleuritic chest pain"], "argues_against": ["Pneumonia or other acute lung infection"]}, {"system": "ent", "positives": [{"text": "Hoarseness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Sore throat", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Globus sensation", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Unilateral throat pain", "Drooling", "Difficulty opening the mouth"], "argues_against": ["Peritonsillar abscess or epiglottitis"]}, {"system": "cardiovascular", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Chest pain with exertion", "Shortness of breath with exertion", "Palpitations", "Leg swelling"], "argues_against": ["Acute coronary syndrome", "Heart failure"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Fever", "Unintentional weight loss", "Night sweats", "Fatigue"], "argues_against": ["Malignancy or chronic infection"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Older children may report heartburn, but younger children often present with recurrent vomiting, poor feeding, irritability, or respiratory symptoms rather than classic burning chest pain.", "missing_classic_features": ["Heartburn", "Clear relationship to meals and lying down"]}, {"population": "infants", "how_it_differs": "Infants typically present with spitting up, feeding refusal, arching of the back, irritability, or poor weight gain; classic heartburn cannot be reported.", "missing_classic_features": ["Heartburn", "Regurgitation described as sour or acid"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Symptoms may be milder or atypical, with more dysphagia, respiratory symptoms, or silent reflux; they are also more likely to have severe esophagitis or Barrett's esophagus.", "missing_classic_features": ["Prominent heartburn"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Heartburn