and supply-demand mismatch (type 2).", "items": ["Rise and fall of troponin above the 99th percentile", "Symptoms of ischemia", "New ischemic ECG changes", "New pathologic Q waves", "Imaging evidence of new regional wall motion abnormality or loss of viable myocardium"]}], "scores": ["timi_risk_score", "grace_score", "heart_score"]}, "differential": [{"name": "Unstable angina", "slug": "unstable-angina", "why_considered": "Same atherosclerotic cause and same symptom pattern, but no myocardial necrosis", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Chest pressure at rest or with minimal exertion that is new or worsening, with a normal or nondiagnostic troponin", "discriminators": {"history": ["Chest discomfort that is new, more frequent, longer or now occurs at rest", "Discomfort relieved by rest or nitroglycerin", "No prolonged unrelieved episode"], "exam": ["Often normal cardiac exam", "No signs of heart failure"], "labs": ["Serial troponin remains normal", "No rise and fall of troponin"], "ecg": ["Transient ST depression or T-wave inversion during pain", "ECG may be normal between episodes", "No ST elevation"]}}, {"name": "Aortic dissection", "slug": "aortic-dissection", "why_considered": "Severe chest pain that can radiate to the back and mimic myocardial infarction", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Sudden tearing or ripping pain that moves from the chest to the back between the shoulder blades, with a pulse or blood pressure difference between arms", "discriminators": {"history": ["Abrupt onset of severe tearing or ripping pain", "Pain migrates from the chest to the back or abdomen", "History of hypertension, connective tissue disease or cocaine use"], "exam": ["Pulse deficit or blood pressure difference between arms", "New aortic regurgitation murmur", "Focal neurologic deficit if the carotid arteries are involved"], "labs": ["Troponin usually normal unless the dissection involves a coronary ostium", "D-dimer often elevated"], "imaging": ["Intimal flap on CT angiography of the aorta", "Widened mediastinum on chest x-ray", "False lumen and aortic enlargement"]}}, {"name": "Pulmonary embolism", "slug": "pulmonary-embolism", "why_considered": "Sudden shortness of breath and chest pain with risk factors for venous thromboembolism", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Pleuritic chest pain with hypoxemia, tachycardia and a swollen tender calf", "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden dyspnea and pleuritic pain", "Recent surgery, immobility, cancer or prior venous thromboembolism", "Calf pain or swelling"], "exam": ["Tachycardia and hypoxemia", "Unilateral calf swelling or tenderness", "Clear lungs on auscultation"], "labs": ["D-dimer elevated", "Troponin usually normal or only mildly elevated", "Hypoxemia on arterial blood gas"], "imaging": ["Filling defect in a pulmonary artery on CT pulmonary angiography", "Right ventricular enlargement on echocardiogram"], "ecg": ["Sinus tachycardia", "S1Q3T3 pattern or right axis deviation", "No territorial ST elevation"]}}, {"name": "Pericarditis", "slug": "pericarditis", "why_considered": "Chest pain with ECG changes that can be mistaken for myocardial infarction", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Sharp pain worse with deep breathing and when lying flat", "Pain improved by sitting up and leaning forward", "Recent viral illness"], "exam": ["Pericardial friction rub", "Pain reproduced by pressure over the sternum or precordium"], "labs": ["Troponin usually normal or only mildly elevated", "Markers of inflammation such as CRP or ESR may be elevated"], "ecg": ["Diffuse concave ST elevation without a territorial pattern", "PR-segment depression", "No reciprocal ST depression"], "imaging": ["Pericardial effusion on echocardiogram"]}}, {"name": "Gastroesophageal reflux disease", "slug": "gastroesophageal-reflux-disease", "why_considered": "Burning chest discomfort that can feel like a heart attack", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Burning pain after meals or