ter a bowel movement", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual, often after a period of constipation or straining; external hemorrhoids can present acutely with sudden pain and a lump after thrombosis", "duration": "Days to weeks for acute episodes; recurrent or chronic for many patients", "progression": "Symptoms fluctuate with bowel habits; external hemorrhoids often improve within days, while internal hemorrhoids may progress from bleeding alone to prolapse that reduces spontaneously, then requires manual reduction, then remains prolapsed", "location": "Anus and lower rectum; external hemorrhoids at the anal margin, internal hemorrhoids inside the anal canal", "radiation": "Usually none; discomfort may be felt locally with sitting", "quality": "Bleeding is bright red and painless with internal hemorrhoids; external hemorrhoids cause a tender, hard lump and sharp or aching pain; itching and irritation are common", "severity": "Mild to moderate; thrombosed external hemorrhoids can be severe (7–10/10)", "timing": "Bleeding typically occurs with or right after a bowel movement; pain from a thrombosed external hemorrhoid is constant and worse with sitting", "aggravating": ["Straining during bowel movements", "Prolonged sitting on the toilet", "Sitting for long periods", "Constipation", "Diarrhea", "Heavy lifting", "Spicy foods or alcohol (sometimes)"], "relieving": ["Warm sitz baths", "Stool softeners or fiber supplements", "Topical hemorrhoid creams or suppositories", "Avoiding straining", "Lying down"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Bright red blood on toilet paper, stool surface, or in the toilet bowl", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Anal itching", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Tender lump or swelling near the anus", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Pain or discomfort with sitting", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Prolapse of tissue through the anus after a bowel movement", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Mucus discharge or soili