 problems"}, {"question": "Does your work or hobbies involve heavy lifting?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Occupational or recreational straining that contributes to the hernia"}, {"question": "Do you smoke?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Smoking with chronic cough, a risk factor for hernia"}, {"question": "Have you noticed any blood in your stool or black stools?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Bleeding that would suggest another cause or a complication"}, {"question": "Have you had any unexplained weight loss?", "category": "ros", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Weight loss that would raise concern for malignancy"}], "accepted_names": ["Hernia", "Abdominal wall hernia", "Inguinal hernia", "Umbilical hernia", "Incisional hernia", "Ventral hernia", "Hiatal hernia"], "reasoning_points": ["A visible or palpable bulge that is more prominent with standing, coughing or straining and reduces when lying down", "A soft, reducible mass with an expansile cough impulse on examination", "Risk factors such as male sex, older age, prior surgery, chronic straining, chronic cough or obesity", "Absence of systemic signs such as fever, severe constant pain or peritoneal findings in an uncomplicated hernia", "Recognition that a firm, tender, irreducible bulge with vomiting or systemic signs suggests incarceration or strangulation and needs urgent surgery", "Pregnancy excluded before imaging or surgery when relevant", "Imaging reserved for uncertain, occult or complicated cases"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Older man with a longstanding reducible groin bulge that appears with standing and coughing", "Bulge reduces when lying down and has a positive cough impulse", "No pain, fever or obstructive symptoms"], "medium": ["Obese patient with groin or abdominal pain but no clearly visible bulge", "Umbilical or incisional hernia at a prior surgical scar", "Hiatal hernia presenting with heartburn and regurgitation rather than a visible lump", "Small hernia with intermittent symptoms and a nondiagnostic exam"], "hard": ["Incarcerated hernia with an irreducible, tender bulge and vomiting", "Strangulated hernia with overlying skin changes, leukocytosis and elevated lactate", "Older adult with vague abdominal discomfort and a hidden hernia", "Pregnant patient with an umbilical or inguinal bulge masked by the gravid uterus", "Child with an umbilical hernia that may close spontaneously"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
