s or first seizure", "findings": [{"text": "Temporal lobe hypodensity or edema", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Normal study early in the course", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "MRI brain with and without contrast", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Suspected herpes encephalitis", "findings": [{"text": "T2/FLAIR hyperintensity in the medial temporal and inferior frontal lobes", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Patchy leptomeningeal or cortical enhancement", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Restricted diffusion in affected cortex", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "findings": [{"text": "Usually normal; may show focal or diffuse opacities if pneumonia complicates disseminated disease", "frequency": "rare"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "Hsv pcr", "why": "Swab of a fresh vesicle or ulcer base is the preferred test to confirm herpes simplex"}, {"test": "Hsv igg", "why": "Type-specific serology identifies HSV-1 versus HSV-2 and prior infection"}, {"test": "HIV", "why": "Standard testing with a new sexually transmitted infection"}, {"test": "RPR", "why": "Syphilis is a common look-alike for genital ulcers"}, {"test": "cbc", "why": "Assesses for leukocytosis in a severe primary episode", "only_if": "systemic symptoms or severe primary episode"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Supports an inflammatory or severe primary episode", "only_if": "systemic symptoms or severe primary episode"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "csf_wbc", "why": "Lymphocytic pleocytosis supports CNS involvement", "only_if": "headache with fever, confusion, seizure or neck stiffness"}, {"test": "csf_protein", "why": "Elevated protein supports CNS involvement", "only_if": "CNS involvement is suspected"}, {"test": "csf_glucose", "why": "Helps distinguish viral from bacterial meningitis", "only_if": "CNS involvement is suspected"}, {"test": "MRI brain with and without contrast", "why": "Temporal lobe changes support herpes encephal