: "Adrenal nodule or hyperplasia", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}, {"study": "Magnetic resonance imaging of the pituitary", "modality": "mri", "preferred_when": "Biochemical testing confirms Cushing disease", "findings": [{"text": "Pituitary microadenoma", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "Chest x-ray", "modality": "xray", "findings": [{"text": "Cardiomegaly with a left ventricular contour", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Rib notching from collateral vessels (coarctation)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Pulmonary vascular congestion or edema (hypertensive heart failure)", "frequency": "rare"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "bmp", "why": "Baseline potassium, sodium, bicarbonate and creatinine before starting a diuretic or renin-angiotensin blocker"}, {"test": "cbc", "why": "Screens for anemia or polycythemia that can accompany kidney disease"}, {"test": "lipids", "why": "Fasting lipid panel for global cardiovascular risk estimation"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Screens for diabetes and prediabetes, which change the treatment threshold"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Thyroid disease is a treatable secondary cause of hypertension"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Proteinuria, hematuria or casts point to kidney disease as a cause or consequence"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Rules out pregnancy before starting an ACE inhibitor, ARB or thiazide", "only_if": "the patient could be pregnant"}, {"test": "Echocardiogram, transthoracic", "why": "Assesses left ventricular hypertrophy, diastolic function and ejection fraction", "only_if": "there is a murmur, signs of heart failure, or an abnormal ECG"}, {"test": "Renal artery duplex ultrasound", "why": "Screens for renal artery stenosis", "only_if": "hypertension is resistant, an abdominal bruit is heard, or creatinine rises after starting an ACE inhibitor or ARB"}, {"test": "CT angiography of the renal arteries", "why": "Confirms renal artery stenosis when ultrasound is nondiagnostic", "only_if": "renal artery stenosis is strongly sus