upus, celiac disease)"], "social_history": ["Low dietary iodine intake (rare in the US because of iodized salt)", "High iodine intake from supplements, kelp, or contrast media"], "exposures": ["Iodinated contrast dye", "Amiodarone", "External beam radiation to the neck", "Radioactive iodine therapy"], "risk_medications": ["amiodarone", "lithium", "interferon alfa", "methimazole", "propylthiouracil", "carbimazole", "sunitinib", "sorafenib", "nivolumab", "pembrolizumab", "ipilimumab", "thalidomide", "bevacizumab", "tyrosine kinase inhibitors"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I'm tired all the time", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "I've been gaining weight even though I'm not eating more", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I just can't seem to get warm", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My skin is so dry and my hair is thinning", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I'm constipated all the time", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I feel down and foggy", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "My periods are heavier and irregular", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual and insidious, often over months; many patients cannot pinpoint when it started", "duration": "Usually 6 months to several years of subtle symptoms before diagnosis", "progression": "Slowly progressive; symptoms accumulate and worsen over time, and patients often attribute them to aging, stress, or being busy", "location": "Generalized; no focal pain", "radiation": "Not applicable", "quality": "A generalized slowing: fatigue, cold intolerance, mental fog, and body changes rather than a discrete pain", "severity": "Mild to moderate at diagnosis; can be severe if untreated for a long time", "timing": "Constant, present every day; worse in cold weather and in the morning", "aggravating": ["Cold environments", "Stress", "Exertion"], "relieving": ["Warm clothing and blankets", "Rest", "Nothing consistently helps"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Fatigue and low energy",