uation of hypothyroidism"}], "decision_points": ["A normal TSH makes primary hypothyroidism very unlikely; check free T4 when central hypothyroidism is suspected", "Check morning cortisol before starting thyroid hormone if adrenal insufficiency could coexist", "In myxedema coma, treat with thyroid hormone and stress-dose glucocorticoids while supporting ventilation and warming the patient"], "criteria": [], "scores": []}, "differential": [{"name": "Subclinical hypothyroidism", "slug": "subclinical-hypothyroidism", "why_considered": "Mild fatigue, weight gain, and cold intolerance with an elevated TSH on screening", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Symptoms are mild or absent", "Often found on routine screening rather than from complaints"], "labs": ["Elevated TSH with a normal free T4", "Thyroid peroxidase antibodies often positive"]}}, {"name": "Central hypothyroidism", "slug": "central-hypothyroidism", "why_considered": "Classic hypothyroid symptoms with low thyroid hormone levels", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Low free T4 with a low, normal, or only mildly elevated TSH", "discriminators": {"history": ["Headache, visual changes, or known pituitary disease", "Symptoms of other pituitary hormone deficiencies (adrenal insufficiency, hypogonadism)", "History of pituitary surgery or radiation"], "exam": ["Visual field defects", "Signs of hypopituitarism"], "labs": ["Low or inappropriately normal TSH with low free T4", "Low morning cortisol, low FSH/LH, low IGF-1", "Hyponatremia"]}}, {"name": "Subacute (painless or painful) thyroiditis", "slug": "subacute-thyroiditis", "why_considered": "Thyroid dysfunction with fatigue and neck discomfort", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent viral illness", "Neck pain radiating to the jaw or ear", "Often a transient hyperthyroid phase before hypothyroidism"], "exam": ["Tender, enlarged thyroid", "Low-grade fever"], "labs": ["Markedly elevated ESR and CRP", "Low TSH during the thyrotoxic phase, then elevated TSH later", "Low radioactive iodine uptake"]}}, {"name": "Hashimoto's thyroiditis", "slug": "hashimotos-thyroiditis", "why_considered": "The most common cause of primary hypothyroidism, with fatigue, cold intolerance, and goiter", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Gradual onset over months", "Family history of autoimmune thyroid disease", "Personal history of another autoimmune disease"], "exam": ["Diffusely enlarged, firm, non-tender goiter", "No thyroid tenderness"], "labs": ["Elevated TSH with low free T4", "Positive thyroid peroxidase antibodies", "Mildly elevated ESR"], "imaging": ["Diffusely heterogeneous, hypoechoic thyroid on ultrasound"]}}, {"name": "Depression", "slug": "major-depressive-disorder", "why_considered": "Fatigue, low mood, poor concentration, and weight change", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Pervasive low mood and anhedonia", "Sleep and appetite changes", "No cold intolerance or constipation"], "exam": ["Normal thyroid exam", "Normal reflexes"], "labs": ["Normal TSH and free T4"]}}, {"name": "Anemia", "slug": "anemia", "why_considered": "Fatigue, pallor, and reduced exercise tolerance", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Pallor, exertional dyspnea, or bleeding", "No cold intolerance or weight gain"], "exam": ["Pallor, tachycardia rather than bradycardia", "Normal thyroid exam"], "labs": ["Low hemoglobin with normal TSH and free T4"]}}, {"name": "Obstructive sleep apnea", "slug": "obstructive-sleep-apnea", "why_considered": "Daytime fatigue, snoring, and cognitive slowing", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Loud snoring, witnessed apneas, morning headaches", "No cold intolerance or constipation"], "exam": ["Obesity, crowded oropharynx", "Normal thyroid exam"], "labs": ["Normal TSH and free T4", "Polysomnography shows apneas and hypopneas"]}}, {"name": "Chronic kidney disease", "slug": "chronic-kidney-disease", "why_considered": "Fatigue, edema, and cognitive slowing", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Known kidney disease, hypertension, or diabetes", "No cold intolerance"], "exam": ["Pitting edema, uremic signs", "Normal thyroid exam"], "labs": ["Elevated creatinine and BUN with normal TSH and free T4"]}}, {"name": "Medication side effects", "slug": "medication-side-effects", "why_considered": "Fatigue, weight gain, and constipation from sedatives, beta blockers, or other drugs", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Temporal link to starting a new medication", "No cold intolerance or dry skin"], "exam": ["Normal thyroid exam", "Normal reflexes"], "labs": ["Normal TSH and free T4"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Subclinical or early overt disease: mild fatigue, cold intolerance, and constipation with an elevated TSH and normal or borderline-low free T4", "moderate": "Overt hypothyroidism: clear fatigue, weight gain, dry skin, bradycardia, and delayed reflexes with elevated TSH and low free T4", "severe": "Marked hypothyroidism: hypothermia, bradycardia, non-pitting edema, hoarse voice, cognitive slowing, and possible pericardial effusion", "critical": "Myxedema coma: obtundation or coma, hypothermia, bradycardia, hypoventilation, hyponatremia, and hypotension"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Altered mental status or coma", "meaning": "Myxedema coma; needs ICU-level care and immediate thyroid hormone replacement"}, {"finding": "Hypothermia", "meaning": "Severe hypothyroidism or myxedema coma; active warming and hormone replacement are needed"}, {"finding": "Bradycardia with hypotension", "meaning": "Cardiovascular collapse from severe hypothyroidism; monitor and support hemodynamics"}, {"finding": "Hypoventilation or respiratory failure", "meaning": "Myxedema coma with respiratory depression; may require mechanical ventilation"}, {"finding": "Hyponatremia with confusion or seizures", "meaning": "Severe hypothyroidism with impaired free water clearance; correct sodium carefully"}, {"finding": "Low free T4 with low or normal TSH", "meaning": "Central hypothyroidism; check cortisol before starting thyroid hormone to avoid precipitating adrenal crisis"}], "complications": [{"name": "Dyslipidemia and accelerated atherosclerosis", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Elevated total and LDL cholesterol", "Improves with thyroid hormone replacement"]}, {"name": "Pericardial effusion", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Low-voltage QRS on ECG", "Enlarged cardiac silhouette on chest x-ray", "Dyspnea or edema"]}, {"name": "Myxedema coma", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "life_threatening", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Obtundation", "Hypothermia", "Bradycardia", "Hypoventilation", "Hyponatremia"]}, {"name": "Infertility and menstrual irregularities", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Heavy or irregular periods", "Difficulty conceiving", "Improves with treatment"]}, {"name": "Pregnancy complications", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Miscarriage", "Preterm birth", "Gestational hypertension", "Impaired fetal neurodevelopment"]}, {"name": "Myopathy with elevated CK", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Muscle aches, cramps, or weakness", "Mildly elevated CK", "Resolves with treatment"]}, {"name": "Carpal tunnel syndrome", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Numbness and tingling in the hands", "Nocturnal symptoms", "Improves with thyroid hormone replacement"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Symptoms are often subtle and attributed to aging; may present with cognitive slowing, depression, falls, or unexplained heart failure rather than classic cold intolerance and weight gain."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Symptoms overlap with normal pregnancy, so screening is important; untreated hypothyroidism increases the risk of miscarriage, preterm birth, gestational hypertension, and impaired fetal neurodevelopment. Levothyroxine requirements often increase during pregnancy."}, {"population": "children", "differences": "May present with poor growth, delayed puberty, school problems, or goiter; congenital hypothyroidism is usually asymptomatic at birth and is detected by newborn screening, but can cause prolonged jaundice, constipation, poor feeding, and hypotonia if missed."}, {"population": "infants", "differences": "Congenital hypothyroidism is typically identified on newborn screening; early treatment is critical to prevent irreversible neurodevelopmental impairment."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Weight gain and fatigue are attributed to obesity itself, delaying diagnosis; consider hypothyroidism when these symptoms worsen or are accompanied by cold intolerance and constipation."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "How has your energy level been over the past few months?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Gradual, persistent fatigue and low energy over weeks to months"}, {"question": "Have you noticed any change in your weight, even though your appetite hasn't changed?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Weight gain despite unchanged or reduced appetite"}, {"question": "Do you feel cold when others around you are comfortable?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Cold intolerance, a fairly specific clue to hypothyroidism"}, {"question": "How often are you having bowel movements? Any constipation?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Constipation or reduced stool frequency"}, {"question": "Have you noticed dry skin, thinning hair, or brittle nails?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Dry, coarse skin and hair thinning or loss"}, {"question": "Has your voice changed, or have you felt any fullness or swelling in your neck?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Hoarseness or a goiter suggesting thyroid enlargement"}, {"question": "How has your mood and thinking been? Any trouble concentrating or feeling down?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Depressed mood, slowed thinking, or memory problems"}, {"question": "Have your menstrual periods changed in flow or regularity?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Heavy or irregular periods, or difficulty conceiving"}, {"question": "Have you had any palpitations, racing heart, heat intolerance, or unintentional weight loss?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Absent; their presence points toward hyperthyroidism instead"}, {"question": "Have you ever had thyroid surgery, radioactive iodine, or radiation to the neck or chest?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Prior thyroid ablation or surgery, a strong cause of hypothyroidism"}, {"question": "Do you take any medications such as amiodarone, lithium, or interferon, or have you had recent iodinated contrast?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Drugs that can cause or worsen hypothyroidism"}, {"question": "Does anyone in your family have thyroid disease or another autoimmune condition?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Family history of Hashimoto's thyroiditis, Graves' disease, or other autoimmune disease"}, {"question": "Do you have any other autoimmune conditions such as type 1 diabetes, celiac disease, or pernicious anemia?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Coexisting autoimmune disease raising suspicion for Hashimoto's thyroiditis"}, {"question": "Could you be pregnant, or have you delivered a baby in the past 6 months?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Pregnancy or recent delivery, which raises risk and changes management"}, {"question": "Have you had any confusion, severe drowsiness, or been told you were very cold or slow to wake?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Altered mental status or hypothermia suggesting myxedema coma"}], "accepted_names": ["Hypothyroidism", "Underactive thyroid", "Primary hypothyroidism", "Hashimoto's thyroiditis", "Hashimoto thyroiditis", "Chronic lymphocytic thyroiditis", "Myxedema"], "reasoning_points": ["Gradual onset over months of fatigue, cold intolerance, weight gain, constipation, and dry skin", "Risk factors such as female sex, older age, family history of thyroid or autoimmune disease, prior thyroid surgery or radiation, and medications like amiodarone or lithium", "Exam findings of bradycardia, delayed relaxation of deep tendon reflexes, dry coarse skin, and possibly a non-tender goiter", "Elevated TSH with low free T4 confirming overt primary hypothyroidism", "Positive thyroid peroxidase antibodies supporting Hashimoto's thyroiditis as the cause", "Look-alikes such as depression, anemia, obstructive sleep apnea, and chronic kidney disease excluded by history and normal thyroid function tests", "Red flags for myxedema coma (altered mental status, hypothermia, bradycardia, hypoventilation, hyponatremia) recognized and treated urgently", "Central hypothyroidism considered when free T4 is low with a low or inappropriately normal TSH, with cortisol checked before starting thyroid hormone"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Middle-aged woman with classic fatigue, cold intolerance, weight gain, and constipation", "Bradycardia and delayed deep tendon reflexes on exam", "Elevated TSH with low free T4 on labs", "Known Hashimoto's thyroiditis or prior thyroid surgery"], "medium": ["Older adult whose symptoms are attributed to aging, presenting with cognitive slowing or depression", "Patient with a non-tender goiter and nonspecific complaints", "Coexisting anemia or dyslipidemia that partially explains the symptoms", "Pregnancy with fatigue and weight gain overlapping normal pregnancy symptoms"], "hard": ["Subclinical hypothyroidism with an elevated TSH but normal free T4 and minimal symptoms", "Central hypothyroidism with low free T4 and a low or normal TSH", "Myxedema coma presenting with altered mental status, hypothermia, and hypoventilation", "Child with poor growth or delayed puberty and few classic adult features", "Symptoms attributed to obesity, delaying the diagnosis"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
