re often needed. Transvaginal ultrasound may be technically limited; transabdominal views or MRI may be required."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "Where is the pain, and is it on one side or both?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Unilateral lower abdominal or pelvic pain on the side of the cyst; bilateral pain suggests pelvic inflammatory disease or another cause"}, {"question": "When did the pain start, and was the onset sudden or gradual?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Gradual, vague onset favors an uncomplicated cyst; sudden severe onset raises concern for rupture or torsion"}, {"question": "How severe is the pain, and does it come and go or stay constant?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Mild to moderate intermittent pain typical of a simple cyst; severe constant pain suggests a complication"}, {"question": "Does the pain get worse with activity, intercourse, or sudden movements?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Worse with movement, exercise or intercourse from pressure or peritoneal irritation"}, {"question": "Have you had nausea or vomiting, especially right when the pain started?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Vomiting at the onset of severe pain suggests ovarian torsion"}, {"question": "Have you felt bloated, full, or noticed increasing abdominal girth?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Bloating and fullness are common with cysts; persistent bloating with early satiety or weight loss raises concern for malignancy"}, {"question": "Have you had any fever or chills?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Fever suggests infection such as pelvic inflammatory disease or tubo-ovarian abscess rather than an uncomplicated cyst"}, {"question": "When was your last menstrual period, and could you be pregnant?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "A missed period or possible pregnancy redirects the workup to ectopic pregnancy or a pregnancy-related cyst"}, {"question": "Have your periods been regular, and have you had any bleeding between periods or after intercourse?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Irregular or heavier menses can accompany cysts; abnormal bleeding raises concern for other causes"}, {"question": "Have you had any vaginal discharge or pain with intercourse?", "category": "sexual", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Purulent discharge suggests pelvic inflammatory disease; dyspareunia is common with cysts and endometriosis"}, {"question": "Have you had ovarian cysts, endometriosis, pelvic infections, or pelvic surgery before?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prior cysts, endometriosis or pelvic infection increase the likelihood of cyst-related pain"}, {"question": "Have you taken fertility medications such as clomiphene, letrozole, or gonadotropins?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Ovulation-inducing medications increase the risk of functional and theca lutein cysts"}, {"question": "Has anyone in your family had ovarian, breast, or colon cancer?", "category": "family", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "A family history of breast or ovarian cancer raises concern for a hereditary cancer syndrome and malignancy"}, {"question": "Do you smoke, and how much alcohol do you drink?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Smoking is a weak risk factor for cysts and is relevant to overall risk assessment"}, {"question": "Have you had any unintentional weight loss, early fullness with meals, or night sweats?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "These suggest malignancy rather than a benign cyst and require urgent evaluation"}, {"question": "Have you fainted, felt lightheaded, or had a racing heart?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Syncope, lightheadedness or palpitations suggest a ruptured cyst with significant bleeding"}], "accepted_names": ["Ovarian cyst", "Ovarian cysts", "Functional ovarian cyst", "Follicular cyst", "Corpus luteum cyst", "Simple ovarian cyst", "Adnexal cyst"], "reasoning_points": ["Unilateral lower abdominal or pelvic pain or pressure in a woman of reproductive age", "Gradual onset of mild to moderate, intermittent pain that may worsen with activity or intercourse", "Associated bloating, fullness, urinary frequency, or irregular menses", "No fever, no peritoneal signs, and a negative pregnancy test", "Bimanual exam may reveal a palpable adnexal mass or focal adnexal tenderness on one side", "Transvaginal ultrasound shows a simple cyst with a thin smooth wall, anechoic fluid, no septations, and no solid components", "Pregnancy excluded before imaging or intervention", "Red flags for torsion or rupture (sudden severe pain, vomiting, syncope, hemodynamic instability) are absent or appropriately evaluated"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Reproductive-age woman with mild unilateral pelvic pressure and bloating", "Pain worse with activity or intercourse", "Bimanual exam reveals a palpable adnexal mass", "Transvaginal ultrasound shows a simple cyst with a thin wall and no solid components", "Negative pregnancy test"], "medium": ["Incidental cyst found on imaging done for another reason, with minimal or no symptoms", "Hemorrhagic cyst with internal echoes or a lacy pattern on ultrasound", "Irregular menses with mild pelvic pain and a normal exam", "Cyst in a postmenopausal woman requiring evaluation for malignancy", "Overlapping symptoms with urinary tract infection or endometriosis"], "hard": ["Sudden severe unilateral pain with vomiting suggesting ovarian torsion", "Ruptured cyst with tachycardia, hypotension, or falling hemoglobin", "Fever and purulent discharge suggesting pelvic inflammatory disease or tubo-ovarian abscess", "Complex or solid adnexal mass with ascites or elevated CA-125 suggesting ovarian cancer", "Right lower quadrant pain mimicking appendicitis", "Cyst discovered during pregnancy with limited imaging options"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
