y with regular urge incontinence, marked nocturia and sleep disruption; patient avoids social activities, wears protective pads, and is significantly distressed", "critical": "Not applicable; overactive bladder is not a life-threatening condition"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Gross or persistent microscopic hematuria", "meaning": "Suggests bladder cancer, stone or other urothelial pathology and requires urologic evaluation"}, {"finding": "Fever, chills or flank pain", "meaning": "Suggests urinary tract infection or pyelonephritis rather than overactive bladder"}, {"finding": "Sudden severe pelvic or abdominal pain", "meaning": "Suggests stone, torsion or another acute process and needs urgent evaluation"}, {"finding": "New neurologic deficits or saddle anesthesia", "meaning": "Suggests spinal cord or cauda equina pathology and is an emergency"}, {"finding": "Inability to urinate with a palpable bladder", "meaning": "Suggests urinary retention or obstruction and requires immediate catheterization and evaluation"}, {"finding": "Unintentional weight loss", "meaning": "Raises concern for malignancy and warrants further workup"}], "complications": [{"name": "Sleep disruption and daytime fatigue", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Nocturia two or more times per night", "Reports of poor sleep quality", "Daytime somnolence"]}, {"name": "Skin irritation or breakdown from incontinence", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Chronic urine leakage", "Perineal or buttock erythema", "Use of protective pads"]}, {"name": "Urinary tract infection", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Incomplete bladder emptying", "Dysuria and cloudy urine", "Positive urine culture"]}, {"name": "Falls and fractures", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Older adult rushing to the toilet at night", "Nocturia", "History of a fall"]}, {"name": "Depression and social isolation", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Avoiding social activities", "Embarrassment about leakage", "Low mood"]}, {"name": "Urinary retention", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Inability to void", "Palpable bladder", "Elevated post-void residual"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Symptoms are often attributed to normal aging; nocturia and falls may be the main concerns rather than urgency. Antimuscarinic side effects such as confusion and constipation are more likely, so beta-3 agonists or behavioral therapy may be preferred."}, {"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Frequency and urgency are common in pregnancy from uterine pressure and increased fluid volume and often resolve postpartum; treatment focuses on behavioral measures and pelvic floor exercises."}, {"population": "diabetes", "differences": "Polyuria from hyperglycemia can mimic frequency; urgency may be less prominent than large-volume urination. Optimizing glycemic control may improve symptoms."}, {"population": "obesity", "differences": "Increased intra-abdominal pressure worsens urgency and incontinence; weight loss can improve symptoms and should be encouraged."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "Do you get a sudden, strong urge to urinate that you can't put off?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Urgency, the defining symptom of overactive bladder"}, {"question": "How many times a day do you urinate, and how many times do you get up at night?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Eight or more voids a day and two or more episodes of nocturia"}, {"question": "Do you ever leak urine before you can reach the toilet?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Urge incontinence, which may or may not be present"}, {"question": "When did this start, 