 "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Cramping starts a day or two before or on the first day of bleeding; in primary dysmenorrhea it began within the first year or two after periods started", "duration": "Typically 1–3 days per cycle, sometimes longer", "progression": "Pain is worst on the first day or two of the period and eases over the next few days; it recurs in a similar pattern each cycle rather than steadily worsening", "location": "Lower abdomen, often midline or slightly to one side", "radiation": "May spread to the lower back, inner thighs, or upper legs", "quality": "Cramping, throbbing, or aching; comes in waves", "severity": "Mild to severe; often 5–8/10 at its worst and enough to interfere with usual activities", "timing": "Cyclical, tied to the menstrual period; not present between periods", "aggravating": ["The first day or two of bleeding", "Standing or moving around", "Fatigue or lack of sleep"], "relieving": ["Heating pad or hot bath on the lower abdomen", "Ibuprofen or naproxen started at the first sign of cramps", "Resting or lying down", "Exercise or stretching", "Hormonal birth control"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Lower back pain", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Nausea", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Headache", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Diarrhea", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Fatigue", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dizziness or lightheadedness", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Vomiting", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Pain or bleeding between periods", "Pain with intercourse", "Fever or chills with the period", "Foul-smelling vaginal discharge", "Sudden severe one-sided pelvic pain", "Missed period or positive pregnancy test", "Pain that has been getting steadily worse over months", "Postmenopausal bleeding", "Pain that continues after the period ends"]}, "ros": [{"system": "constitutional", "positives": [{"text": "Fatigue during the period", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "neg