eral eye pain with headache, nausea or vomiting, halos around lights, and a mid-dilated fixed pupil", "discriminators": {"history": ["Sudden severe eye or brow pain", "Nausea and vomiting", "Colored halos around lights", "Decreased vision", "History of hyperopia or prior angle-closure attack"], "exam": ["Markedly elevated intraocular pressure on tonometry", "Mid-dilated, fixed pupil", "Corneal haze or edema", "Ciliary flush", "Decreased visual acuity"], "labs": [], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Anterior uveitis (iritis)", "slug": "anterior-uveitis", "why_considered": "Red, painful, photophobic eye that can be mistaken for conjunctivitis when redness is the main complaint", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Deep eye pain, photophobia, and ciliary flush with a relatively quiet discharge", "discriminators": {"history": ["Deep, aching eye pain", "Marked photophobia", "Blurred vision", "Associated autoimmune disease or prior episodes"], "exam": ["Ciliary flush", "Cells and flare in the anterior chamber on slit-lamp examination", "Constricted pupil or posterior synechiae", "Decreased visual acuity", "Minimal discharge"], "labs": ["Testing for underlying systemic disease (for example HLA-B27, ANA) when recurrent or bilateral"], "imaging": []}}, {"name": "Orbital or preseptal cellulitis", "slug": "orbital-cellulitis", "why_considered": "Eyelid swelling and redness with a red eye that can be mistaken for conjunctivitis when swelling is prominent", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Fever, marked eyelid swelling, proptosis, painful or restricted eye movements, or systemic toxicity", "discriminators": {"history": ["Fever and systemic illness", "Rapidly progressive eyelid swelling", "Pain with eye movement", "Recent sinusitis or skin infection"], "exam": ["Proptosis", "Restricted or painful extraocular movements", "Marked periorbital swelling and erythema", "Decreased visual acuity in orbital involvement"], "labs": ["CBC with differential and blood cultures when systemic infectio