od positive"], "imaging": ["Not routinely needed", "Endoscopy with biopsy may show eosinophilic inflammation if performed"]}}, {"name": "Laryngomalacia", "slug": "laryngomalacia", "why_considered": "Noisy breathing, coughing, and feeding difficulty can be attributed to reflux", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Inspiratory stridor that worsens when supine or crying", "Symptoms present from birth or early weeks", "Feeding difficulty with choking or cyanotic spells"], "exam": ["High-pitched inspiratory stridor", "Worsening of stridor with neck flexion or agitation"], "labs": ["Not routinely needed"], "imaging": ["Flexible laryngoscopy showing omega-shaped epiglottis and prolapsing arytenoids"]}}, {"name": "Gastroenteritis", "slug": "gastroenteritis", "why_considered": "Vomiting and irritability in an infant can be mistaken for reflux", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Acute onset of vomiting and diarrhea", "Sick contacts", "Fever"], "exam": ["Signs of dehydration", "Diffuse abdominal tenderness without mass"], "labs": ["Electrolyte abnormalities if dehydrated", "Stool studies if indicated"], "imaging": ["Not routinely needed"]}}, {"name": "Increased intracranial pressure", "slug": "increased-intracranial-pressure", "why_considered": "Vomiting and irritability in an infant can be attributed to reflux when a neurologic cause is present", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Vomiting with lethargy, bulging fontanelle, abnormal tone, or seizures", "discriminators": {"history": ["Vomiting without relation to feeds", "Lethargy or irritability", "Seizures or developmental regression"], "exam": ["Bulging anterior fontanelle", "Abnormal tone or posture", "Sunsetting eyes or cranial nerve abnormalities"], "labs": ["Not routinely diagnostic"], "imaging": ["Head ultrasound or CT/MRI showing ventricular dilation or mass"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Frequent effortless spitting up in a thriving, well-appearing infant; no feeding 