is or discomfort"}, {"question": "Does your baby cough, choke, gag, or wheeze with feeds?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Respiratory symptoms suggesting aspiration or airway involvement"}, {"question": "How much and how often are you feeding, and do you burp during feeds?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Overfeeding or large-volume feeds that worsen reflux; opportunities for feeding changes"}, {"question": "What have you tried so far, such as holding upright, smaller feeds, or thickened feeds?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Response to conservative feeding measures before considering medication"}, {"question": "Was your baby born early, or does she have any neurologic or lung conditions?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prematurity, cerebral palsy, cystic fibrosis, hiatal hernia, or prior esophageal surgery"}, {"question": "Is there any blood or green color in the vomit, or blood in the stool?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Bilious or bloody emesis or bloody stools, which suggest obstruction, esophagitis, or a bleeding source"}, {"question": "Has your baby had spells of stopping breathing, turning blue, or becoming limp?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Apnea, cyanotic spells, or apparent life-threatening events suggesting aspiration or severe disease"}, {"question": "Is your baby lethargic, difficult to wake, or having seizures?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Neurologic warning signs such as lethargy, poor responsiveness, or seizures"}, {"question": "Does anyone in the family have reflux or food allergies?", "category": "family", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Family history of gastroesophageal reflux disease or atopy"}, {"question": "Does anyone smoke around the baby?", "category": "social", "importance": "opti