ce visual acuity one eye at a time with a Snellen or picture chart, with and without correction", "finding": "Reduced distance acuity that improves with a pinhole or with the patient's glasses or contact lenses", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "reduced-near-va", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Check near visual acuity with a near card at reading distance, one eye at a time", "finding": "Reduced near acuity, most prominent in patients over 40 (presbyopia) or with hyperopia", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "pinhole-improvement", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Repeat the acuity test through a pinhole occluder", "finding": "Vision improves through the pinhole, indicating a refractive rather than a retinal or optic nerve cause", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "squinting", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Observe the patient while they attempt to read the chart", "finding": "Squinting, head tilting, or partially closing one eye to see better", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-pupils", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Test pupillary light and accommodation responses", "finding": "Pupils equal, round, and reactive to light and accommodation; no afferent pupillary defect", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-ocular-motility", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Test extraocular movements in all directions of gaze", "finding": "Full, conjugate, painless eye movements without diplopia", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-confrontation-fields", "region": "neuro", "maneuver": "Confrontation visual field testing in all four quadrants of each eye", "finding": "Full visual fields to confrontation", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-fundoscopy", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Perform direct ophthalmoscopy of the optic disc, macula, vessels, and periphery", "finding": "Clear media, sharp disc margins, normal macula and vessels; no hemorrhage, edema, or detachment", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "normal-anterior-segment", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the conjunctiva, cornea, anterior chamber, and lens with a penlight or slit lamp", "finding": "White conjunctiva, clear cornea, no cells or flare, no discharge; lens may show age-related changes but no acute opacity", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-iop", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Measure intraocular pressure by tonometry when available", "finding": "Normal intraocular pressure without pain or corneal edema", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {}, "labs": [], "imaging": [{"study": "Ocular ultrasound", "modality": "ultrasound", "preferred_when": "Media opacity (dense cataract, corneal scar, vitreous hemorrhage) prevents a view of the retina", "findings": [{"text": "Normal globe contour and axial length; no retinal detachment, mass, or vitreous hemorrhage", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Axial length measurement used to calculate intraocular lens power before cataract or refractive surgery", "frequency": "common"}]}, {"study": "Optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic nerve", "modality": "other", "preferred_when": "Blurred vision that does not fully correct with refraction, or when macular or optic nerve disease is suspected", "findings": [{"text": "Normal retinal nerve fiber layer and macular architecture; no edema, hole, or epiretinal membrane", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Thinning of the retinal nerve fiber layer sugges