 driving", "May be asymmetric between eyes"], "exam": ["Reduced visual acuity that may not fully improve with pinhole or refraction", "Lens opacity or nuclear sclerosis on slit-lamp examination", "Reduced red reflex"], "labs": [], "imaging": ["Ocular ultrasound showing lens opacity when the view is poor"]}}, {"name": "Diabetic retinopathy", "slug": "diabetic-retinopathy", "why_considered": "Blurred vision in a patient with diabetes, which can fluctuate with glucose control and mimic a refractive change", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Diabetes with blurred vision, especially if acuity does not fully correct with refraction", "discriminators": {"history": ["Known diabetes, often long-standing", "Blur that fluctuates with blood sugar control", "Floaters or visual distortion"], "exam": ["Reduced acuity that may not fully correct with pinhole", "Microaneurysms, dot-blot hemorrhages, hard exudates, or neovascularization on dilated fundoscopy"], "labs": ["Elevated hemoglobin A1c or fluctuating glucose"], "imaging": ["Optical coherence tomography showing macular edema", "Fluorescein angiography showing leakage or ischemia"]}}, {"name": "Glaucoma", "slug": "glaucoma", "why_considered": "Blurred vision and halos around lights, especially in older adults", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Halos, eye pain, or visual field loss with reduced acuity that does not correct with refraction", "discriminators": {"history": ["Gradual peripheral vision loss (open-angle) or sudden painful vision loss with nausea (angle-closure)", "Halos around lights", "Family history of glaucoma"], "exam": ["Elevated intraocular pressure", "Cupping of the optic disc", "Reduced visual fields", "Mid-dilated fixed pupil and corneal edema in acute angle-closure"], "labs": [], "imaging": ["Optical coherence tomography showing retinal nerve fiber layer thinning", "Automated perimetry showing field defects"]}}, {"name": "Age-related macular degeneration", "slug": "age-related-macular-degeneration", "why_