ual field or acuity", "Retinal tear or detachment on dilated fundoscopy"], "labs": [], "imaging": ["Ocular ultrasound showing retinal detachment when the view is obscured"]}}, {"name": "Optic neuritis", "slug": "optic-neuritis", "why_considered": "Subacute unilateral vision loss with pain on eye movement, often in young adults", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Pain with eye movement and reduced color vision", "discriminators": {"history": ["Unilateral vision loss over hours to days", "Pain with eye movement", "Reduced color vision", "May have prior neurologic symptoms"], "exam": ["Afferent pupillary defect", "Reduced color vision on Ishihara testing", "Swollen or normal optic disc"], "labs": ["May have elevated inflammatory markers if associated with systemic disease"], "imaging": ["MRI showing enhancement of the optic nerve"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Blurred vision only with specific tasks (driving at night, reading small print); acuity corrects to normal with lenses; no functional limitation", "moderate": "Blurred vision interferes with daily activities such as reading, schoolwork, or driving; headaches and eye strain with prolonged visual tasks; corrects with lenses", "severe": "Marked blurring that limits activities even with effort; high refractive error or anisometropia; may be associated with amblyopia in children or difficulty functioning without correction", "critical": "Not applicable to uncomplicated refractive error; sudden severe vision loss or painful red eye suggests another diagnosis"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Sudden painless loss of vision in one eye", "meaning": "Suggests retinal artery occlusion, retinal detachment, or vitreous hemorrhage; needs urgent ophthalmology evaluation"}, {"finding": "Eye pain, redness, or photophobia", "meaning": "Suggests keratitis, uveitis, or acute angle-closure glaucoma; not a simple refractive error"}, {"finding": "Flashes of light or new floaters", "meaning": "Suggests retinal tear or detachment; n