llary defect", "Normal fundoscopic examination and full visual fields, ruling out retinal or optic nerve disease", "Refraction confirms the diagnosis when acuity corrects to normal or near-normal with lenses", "Red flags such as sudden vision loss, flashes, floaters, or a curtain over the vision are absent"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["School-age child who squints at the board and fails a vision screening", "Young adult with clear distance blur that corrects with a pinhole and with glasses", "Healthy 48-year-old who must hold reading material at arm's length", "Normal eye examination apart from reduced acuity"], "medium": ["Patient with astigmatism and blur at all distances plus glare and night vision difficulty", "Young adult with latent hyperopia unmasked only on cycloplegic refraction", "Patient with diabetes whose blur fluctuates with glucose control", "Adult with an outdated prescription and eye strain from prolonged screen use"], "hard": ["Child with unilateral reduced acuity from anisometropic amblyopia rather than simple refractive error", "Older adult whose blur does not fully correct with refraction because of an underlying cataract", "Patient with reduced acuity that persists through a pinhole, pointing to retinal or optic nerve disease", "Patient with irregular astigmatism and poor best-corrected acuity suggesting keratoconus", "Pregnant patient with temporary refractive fluctuation from hormonal corneal changes"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
