ease rather than prominent wheezing.", "missing_classic_features": ["High fever", "Prominent wheezing"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "Illness can be more severe and prolonged, with higher viral loads and progression to pneumonia; shedding may last weeks.", "missing_classic_features": ["Self-limited one-week course"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Older children often have a mild cold or tracheobronchitis rather than bronchiolitis, and may wheeze if they have asthma.", "missing_classic_features": ["Apnea", "Severe respiratory distress"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Alert, playful or interactive, feeding well, no respiratory distress", "moderate": "Mildly irritable or tired, feeding less than usual, mild tachypnea with intercostal retractions", "severe": "Irritable or lethargic, poor feeding, marked tachypnea with nasal flaring and retractions, audible wheeze", "critical": "Lethargic or unresponsive, unable to feed, grunting, apnea or cyanosis, impending respiratory failure"}, "findings": [{"id": "nasal-congestion-discharge", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the nasal passages and nares", "finding": "Clear rhinorrhea and congested nasal mucosa", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "pharyngeal-erythema", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Inspect the oropharynx with a tongue blade", "finding": "Mild pharyngeal erythema without exudate or tonsillar enlargement", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "otitis-media", "region": "heent", "maneuver": "Perform pneumatic otoscopy of both tympanic membranes", "finding": "Bulging, erythematous, immobile tympanic membrane suggesting acute otitis media", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "tachypnea", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Count the respiratory rate for a full 60 seconds while the patient is calm", "finding": "Elevated respiratory rate for age", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "wheezing", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate all lung fields with the bell and diaphragm during quiet breathing", "finding": "Diffuse expiratory wheezing, often with a prolonged expiratory phase", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "crackles", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Auscultate the lung bases", "finding": "Fine inspiratory crackles", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "prolonged-expiration", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Listen for the ratio of inspiration to expiration", "finding": "Prolonged expiratory phase", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "moderate", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "retractions", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Observe the chest wall for suprasternal, intercostal, or subcostal indrawing", "finding": "Intercostal, subcostal, or suprasternal retractions", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "nasal-flaring", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Observe the nares during breathing", "finding": "Nasal flaring with each breath", "frequency": "common", "min_severity": "severe", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "grunting", "region": "lung", "maneuver": "Listen for expiratory grunting without a stethoscope", "finding": "Audible expiratory grunting", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "critical", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "head-bobbing", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Observe the head and neck during breathing", "finding": "Head bobbing with each breath (infants)", "frequency": "sometimes", "min_severity": "se