r vegetation suggesting infective endocarditis", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Reduced ejection fraction or global hypokinesis from septic cardiomyopathy", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Normal cardiac function", "frequency": "common"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "White count with differential and platelets; leukocytosis or leukopenia and thrombocytopenia support sepsis and organ dysfunction"}, {"test": "bmp", "why": "Assesses kidney function, electrolytes and acid-base status; a rising creatinine indicates organ dysfunction"}, {"test": "lactate", "why": "Marker of tissue hypoperfusion; guides fluid resuscitation and reassessment"}, {"test": "abg", "why": "Assesses oxygenation, ventilation and acid-base status in a seriously ill or hypoxemic patient"}, {"test": "coag", "why": "Baseline PT/INR, aPTT and fibrinogen; abnormal values suggest coagulopathy or disseminated intravascular coagulation"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Screens for a urinary source, a common cause of sepsis"}, {"test": "Blood cultures", "why": "Two sets from separate sites before antibiotics to identify the organism and guide therapy"}, {"test": "Chest x-ray, portable anteroposterior", "why": "Looks for pneumonia, the most common source"}, {"test": "Urine culture", "why": "Confirms a urinary source and guides antibiotic choice", "only_if": "urinary symptoms, pyuria or an indwelling catheter"}, {"test": "hcg", "why": "Required in anyone who could be pregnant before imaging and to guide antibiotic and imaging choices", "only_if": "patient is of childbearing potential"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "procalcitonin", "why": "Supports a bacterial cause and can help guide antibiotic duration"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Nonspecific marker of inflammation; useful for trending"}, {"test": "cmp_extra", "why": "Liver tests and albumin assess hepatic organ dysfunction and a hepatobiliary source"}, {"test": "cardiac", "why": "Troponin and natriuretic peptide assess 