specially young cats or dogs)"], "exposures": ["Infected household member or close contact", "Infected pet (kitten, puppy, rodent)", "Damp floors (showers, locker rooms, pools)", "Shared personal items (combs, hats, towels)", "Farm animals or soil"], "risk_medications": ["Topical corticosteroids (can mask or worsen tinea)", "Systemic corticosteroids", "Immunosuppressants", "TNF inhibitors"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I have an itchy rash", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "There's a red ring on my skin", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "The skin between my toes is itchy and peeling", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "My groin is itchy and burning", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I have a bald spot on my head", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "My toenails are thick and discolored", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual, over days to weeks", "duration": "Weeks to months if untreated", "progression": "Slowly enlarges; may spread to other body sites or to close contacts", "location": "Depends on type: tinea corporis on trunk or limbs; tinea pedis between toes or on soles; tinea cruris in groin; tinea capitis on scalp; onychomycosis on nails", "radiation": "Not applicable", "quality": "Itchy, sometimes burning; rash may be scaly or ring-shaped", "severity": "Mild to moderate; usually not severe but can be very uncomfortable", "timing": "Constant; itching may be worse at night or after sweating", "aggravating": ["Heat", "Sweating", "Tight clothing", "Occlusive footwear", "Scratching"], "relieving": ["Cooling", "Drying the area", "Loose clothing", "Over-the-counter antifungal creams (partial relief)"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Itching", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Scaling or flaking skin", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Redness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Burning or stinging", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Cracked or peeling skin between toes", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Hair loss or broken hairs (scalp)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Thickened, discolored nails", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Secondary bacterial infection with pus or pain", "frequency": "rare"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Fever", "Weight loss", "Night sweats", "Joint pain", "Mouth sores", "Recent antibiotic use", "New medication before rash", "History of psoriasis or eczema", "Travel to areas with endemic fungal disease"]}, "ros": [{"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Itchy rash", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Ring-shaped lesion with central clearing", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Scaling", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Hair loss on scalp", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Nail thickening or discoloration", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Blisters", "Pustules", "Skin pain out of proportion", "Mucosal involvement"], "argues_against": ["Well-demarcated silvery plaques on extensor surfaces (psoriasis)", "Vesicles in a dermatomal distribution (herpes zoster)"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Fever", "Chills", "Weight loss", "Fatigue"], "argues_against": ["Systemic infection"]}, {"system": "allergic_immunologic", "positives": [], "negatives": ["New medication", "Recent antibiotic use", "Known allergies"], "argues_against": ["Drug eruption", "Contact dermatitis"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Tinea capitis is common and presents with scaly patches and broken hairs rather than a classic ring; may have little itching.", "missing_classic_features": ["Ring-shaped lesion with central clearing", "Prominent itching"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Onychomycosis and tinea pedis are more common; skin may be dry and fissured rather than inflamed.", "missing_classic_features": ["Active border", "Significant erythema"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "Lesions can be extensive, atypical, and deeper, sometimes with nodules or 