ing", "Tinea cruris with an inguinal plaque and scrotal sparing, mimicking erythrasma or candidal intertrigo", "Tinea capitis in a child with scaly patches and broken hairs but little itching", "Partial improvement from an over-the-counter antifungal cream, obscuring the classic appearance"], "hard": ["Tinea incognito: atypical, poorly demarcated rash after topical corticosteroid use", "Onychomycosis with thickened, crumbling nails and no skin findings", "Immunocompromised patient with extensive or deeper lesions, nodules, or abscesses", "Tinea pedis complicated by bacterial cellulitis with fever, warmth, and spreading erythema", "Annular rash that is actually erythema migrans from Lyme disease or nummular eczema"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
