kening of pelvic floor and bladder muscles", "strength": "strong"}, {"text": "Obesity", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Prostate enlargement or prior prostate surgery in men", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Diabetes mellitus", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Chronic constipation", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Smoking", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Neurologic disease such as multiple sclerosis, stroke or spinal cord injury", "strength": "moderate"}, {"text": "Congenital abnormality of the urinary tract", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Diabetes mellitus", "Obesity", "Chronic constipation", "Benign prostatic hyperplasia", "Multiple sclerosis or other neurologic disease", "Prior pelvic or prostate surgery", "Recurrent urinary tract infection", "Obstructive sleep apnea"], "family_history": ["Urinary incontinence in a mother or sister", "Bedwetting in childhood in the patient or a parent"], "social_history": ["High caffeine or alcohol intake", "Smoking", "Limited mobility or difficulty reaching a toilet", "Occupational or recreational heavy lifting"], "exposures": [], "risk_medications": ["furosemide", "hydrochlorothiazide", "oxybutynin", "doxazosin", "terazosin", "tamsulosin", "duloxetine", "amitriptyline", "diphenhydramine", "prednisone"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I leak urine when I don't mean to", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "I can't make it to the bathroom in time", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I have to wear a pad every day", "frequency": "common"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual over months to years; often noticed after childbirth, weight gain, menopause or prostate problems", "duration": "Usually months to years by the time the patient seeks care", "progression": "Slowly worsens over time; may fluctuate with fluid intake, caffeine, activity and weight", "location": "Bladder and urethra; leakage felt at the opening of the urethra", "radiation": "None", "quality": "Involuntary loss of urine; stress type leaks in small spurts with pressure, urge type leaks in larger amounts with a sudden need to go, overflow type is a constant dribble", "severity": "Mild to moderate for most; can be severe enough to limit work, exercise and social life", "timing": "Stress type with coughing, sneezing, laughing, lifting or exercise; urge type with sudden urgency day or night; overflow type continuous dribbling", "aggravating": ["Coughing, sneezing or laughing", "Lifting or bending", "Exercise or walking", "Running water or cold weather", "Caffeine or alcohol", "Full bladder or rushing to the toilet"], "relieving": ["Emptying the bladder on a schedule", "Pelvic floor muscle exercises", "Wearing a pad or protective underwear", "Crossing legs or sitting down when the urge hits"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Going to the bathroom often during the day", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Waking up at night to urinate", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Sudden strong urge to urinate", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Feeling that the bladder is not completely empty", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Needing to urinate again soon after finishing", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Leaking during sleep", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Avoiding activities because of fear of leaking", "frequency": "common"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Burning or pain with urination", "Blood in the urine", "Fever or chills", "Flank or back pain", "Sudden inability to urinate at all", "New numbness, weakness or trouble walking", "Weight loss", "Vaginal bleeding after menopause", "Penile discharge"]}, "ros": [{"system": "genitourinary", "positives": [{"text": "Leaking urine with coughing, sneezing or lifting", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Sudden urge to urinate with leakage before reaching the toilet", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Urinating frequently during the day", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Getting up at night to urinate", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Weak urinary stream or dribbling after urination", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Dysuria", "Hematuria", "Flank pain", "Fever", "Complete urinary retention"], "argues_against": ["Urinary tract infection", "Bladder stone or tumor", "Acute urinary obstruction"]}, {"system": "neurologic", "positives": [{"text": "Numbness or tingling in the legs or feet", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["New weakness in the legs", "Loss of sensation in the saddle area", "Trouble with bowel control", "Sudden confusion"], "argues_against": ["Cauda equina syndrome", "Spinal cord compression", "Acute stroke"]}, {"system": "musculoskeletal", "positives": [{"text": "Pelvic or low back pressure", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Severe back pain", "Difficulty walking"], "argues_against": ["Spinal cord injury or compression"]}, {"system": "psychiatric", "positives": [{"text": "Embarrassment or worry about leaking in public", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Avoiding social activities", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Depressed mood most days", "Suicidal thoughts"], "argues_against": ["Major depression as the primary cause"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [{"text": "Constipation", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Blood in stool", "Unintentional weight loss"], "argues_against": ["Colorectal cancer or severe bowel disease"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Leakage may be mixed or functional rather than a single type, and is often accompanied by mobility problems, cognitive impairment or medication effects.", "missing_classic_features": ["Clear stress or urge pattern", "Ability to describe the trigger"]}, {"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Stress leakage is common in late pregnancy and after delivery because of pelvic floor pressure and stretching; it often improves in the months after birth.", "missing_classic_features": ["Long-standing symptoms", "Symptoms unrelated to pregnancy"]}, {"population": "obesity", "how_it_differs": "Increased abdominal pressure worsens stress leakage, and symptoms often improve with weight loss.", "missing_classic_features": ["Leakage only with severe exertion"]}, {"population": "diabetes", "how_it_differs": "Can cause both urge leakage from bladder nerve damage and overflow leakage from incomplete bladder emptying; high blood sugar also increases urine volume.", "missing_classic_features": ["Single clear incontinence type"]}, {"population": "children", "how_it_differs": "Daytime or nighttime wetting is common and usually reflects delayed bladder control rather than adult-type incontinence; it is more common in boys and when a parent had the same problem.", "missing_classic_features": ["Adult pattern of stress or urge leakage"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable, well-groomed, no distress; may mention needing a bathroom soon", "moderate": "Mild embarrassment or anxiety when discussing leakage; may wear a pad or protective underwear", "severe": "Reluctant to sit through a long exam; may smell of urine; visibly distressed about leakage", "critical": "Not applicable; urinary incontinence itself is not a critical illness, though a patient with acute retention or cord compression would appear uncomfortable or toxic"}, "findings": [{"id": "stress-leak-on-cough", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "With a comfortably full bladder, ask the patient to cough forcefully while you observe the urethral meatus", "finding": "Immediate small spurt of urine from the urethra with the cough", "frequency": "common", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "urge-leak-on-hand-wash", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "Ask the patient to run water or imagine running water while observing for leakage", "finding": "Leakage of urine with a sudden urge before reaching the toilet", "frequency": "sometimes", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "postvoid-dribble", "region": "genitou