 sensation and anal sphincter tone", "finding": "Normal strength, sensation, reflexes and sphincter tone", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-costovertebral-tenderness", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Percuss the costovertebral angles", "finding": "No costovertebral angle tenderness", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-suprapubic-tenderness", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Palpate the suprapubic area", "finding": "No suprapubic tenderness", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}, {"id": "no-fever", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Measure temperature and inspect for systemic signs of infection", "finding": "Afebrile, no chills or rigors", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {"temp": {"mild": {"min": 97.8, "max": 99.1}, "moderate": {"min": 97.8, "max": 99.1}, "severe": {"min": 97.8, "max": 99.1}}, "hr": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 90}, "moderate": {"min": 60, "max": 95}, "severe": {"min": 65, "max": 100}}, "rr": {"mild": {"min": 12, "max": 18}, "moderate": {"min": 12, "max": 18}, "severe": {"min": 12, "max": 20}}, "sbp": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 130}, "moderate": {"min": 100, "max": 135}, "severe": {"min": 100, "max": 140}}, "dbp": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 80}, "moderate": {"min": 60, "max": 85}, "severe": {"min": 60, "max": 90}}, "spo2": {"mild": {"min": 95, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 95, "max": 100}, "severe": {"min": 95, "max": 100}}}, "labs": [{"test_id": "ua_le", "qualitative": {"moderate": "1+", "severe": "2+"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Positive leukocyte esterase with nitrite and bacteriuria suggests a urinary tract infection as a transient cause of urgency and leakage; treat and reassess before labeling chronic incontinence."}, {"test_id": "ua_nitrite", "qualitative": {"moderate": "Positive"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Supports a urinary tract infection, a reversible cause of urge leakage."}, {"test_id": "ua_bacteria", "qualitative": {"moderate": "Moderate", "severe": "Many"}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional"}, {"test_id": "ua_wbc", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 6, "max": 20}, "severe": {"min": 10, "max": 50}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Pyuria points to infection or inflammation rather than to the incontinence itself."}, {"test_id": "ua_blood", "qualitative": {"moderate": "1+", "severe": "2+"}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Microscopic hematuria without infection needs evaluation for stone or urothelial tumor; it is not explained by uncomplicated incontinence."}, {"test_id": "glucose", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 125}, "moderate": {"min": 126, "max": 200}, "severe": {"min": 180, "max": 350}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Hyperglycemia causes osmotic diuresis and can worsen both urgency and overflow leakage."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "moderate": {"min": 6.5, "max": 9.0}, "severe": {"min": 8.0, "max": 12.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Screens for undiagnosed diabetes, a treatable contributor."}, {"test_id": "cr", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 1.2, "max": 1.8}, "severe": {"min": 1.6, "max": 3.5}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "A rising creatinine suggests obstructive uropathy or chronic kidney disease from incomplete bladder emptying; check a postvoid residual."}, {"test_id": "bun", "ranges": {"moderate": {"min": 21, "max": 35}, "severe": {"min": 30, "max": 60}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Rises with dehydration or obstructive uropathy."}, {"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "important", "caveat": "Negative. C