sed anal sphincter tone", "Lower extremity weakness or areflexia"], "labs": ["Not diagnostic; urgent imaging is the priority"], "imaging": ["MRI lumbar spine showing disc herniation, mass or compression of the cauda equina"]}}, {"name": "Bladder or urothelial cancer", "slug": "bladder-cancer", "why_considered": "A bladder tumor can cause urgency, frequency and leakage, and may present with hematuria", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Gross or microscopic hematuria, especially in a smoker or older adult", "discriminators": {"history": ["Visible blood in the urine", "Smoking history", "Irritative voiding symptoms that do not respond to usual therapy", "Weight loss"], "exam": ["Usually normal; may have a palpable pelvic mass in advanced disease"], "labs": ["Hematuria on urinalysis without infection", "Anemia in chronic bleeding"], "imaging": ["Bladder mass on ultrasound or CT urography", "Cystoscopy with biopsy confirming malignancy"]}}, {"name": "Fecal impaction", "slug": "fecal-impaction", "why_considered": "A loaded rectum can press on the bladder and cause urgency, frequency and overflow leakage", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Chronic constipation", "Straining with bowel movements", "Sensation of incomplete evacuation"], "exam": ["Hard stool palpable on rectal exam", "Abdominal distension or palpable stool"], "labs": ["Not diagnostic"], "imaging": ["Abdominal x-ray showing fecal loading", "Resolution of leakage after disimpaction"]}}, {"name": "Diabetes mellitus", "slug": "diabetes-mellitus", "why_considered": "Hyperglycemia causes osmotic diuresis and nerve damage that can produce urgency and overflow leakage", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Polydipsia and polyuria", "Known diabetes or risk factors", "Symptoms worsen with poor glycemic control"], "exam": ["Signs of peripheral neuropathy", "Obesity or other metabolic features"], "labs": ["Elevated fasting glucose or hemoglobin A1c", "Glucosuria on urinalysis"], "imaging": ["Not diagnostic; bladder ultrasound may show elevated postvoid residual"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Occasional small leaks with strong triggers such as coughing or heavy lifting; no pads or only rare pad use; does not limit daily activities", "moderate": "Regular leakage requiring daily pads; avoids some activities or plans routes around bathrooms; quality of life noticeably affected", "severe": "Frequent or continuous leakage requiring protective garments; withdraws from work, exercise and social life; skin irritation or recurrent urinary tract infections may develop", "critical": "Not applicable; urinary incontinence itself is not life-threatening, but acute urinary retention with overflow or cauda equina syndrome requires urgent evaluation"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Gross hematuria or persistent microscopic hematuria", "meaning": "Needs evaluation for bladder or urothelial cancer, stone or other structural lesion"}, {"finding": "New saddle anesthesia, leg weakness or bowel incontinence", "meaning": "Possible cauda equina syndrome; obtain urgent MRI"}, {"finding": "Fever, chills or flank pain", "meaning": "Suggests urinary tract infection or pyelonephritis rather than uncomplicated incontinence"}, {"finding": "Sudden inability to urinate with a palpable bladder", "meaning": "Acute urinary retention; requires immediate bladder decompression"}, {"finding": "Leakage that is new and severe in an older adult with confusion", "meaning": "Consider infection, medication effect or neurologic event rather than chronic incontinence"}], "complications": [{"name": "Skin breakdown and dermatitis", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "common", "clues": ["Chronic dampness in the perineal area", "Redness, maceration or fungal rash", "Use of absorbent products"]}, {"name": "Recurrent urinary tract infection", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Repeated dysuria and positive urine cultures", "In