ncontinence; leakage after a sudden strong urge points to urge incontinence; continuous dribbling points to overflow"}, {"question": "Do you leak before you can reach the toilet after a sudden urge to go?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "A sudden, uncontrollable urge with leakage before reaching the toilet suggests urge incontinence or overactive bladder"}, {"question": "How much urine leaks each time, and how often?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Small spurts with activity suggest stress; larger volumes with urgency suggest urge; constant dribbling suggests overflow"}, {"question": "Do you feel like your bladder is not completely empty after you urinate?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Incomplete emptying suggests overflow incontinence and should prompt a postvoid residual check"}, {"question": "How many times do you urinate during the day and at night?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Frequency and nocturia support urge incontinence or overactive bladder"}, {"question": "Do you use pads or protective underwear, and how many per day?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Quantifies severity and impact on daily life"}, {"question": "Does it burn or hurt when you urinate, or have you had fever or chills?", "category": "associated", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Dysuria, fever or chills suggest a urinary tract infection as a reversible cause of urgency and leakage"}, {"question": "Have you seen blood in your urine?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Gross or microscopic hematuria requires evaluation for bladder or urothelial cancer, stone or other structural lesion"}, {"question": "Have you had any new numbness in the saddle area, leg weakness or loss of bowel control?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Saddle anesthesia, leg weakness or bowel incontinence suggests cauda equina syndrome and needs urgent MRI"}, {"question": "Have you been unable to urinate at all, or do you feel a constant need to go with a very full bladder?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Acute urinary retention with a palpable bladder requires immediate decompression"}, {"question": "How many pregnancies and vaginal deliveries have you had?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Multiple vaginal deliveries increase risk of pelvic floor weakness and stress incontinence"}, {"question": "Have you gone through menopause?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Menopause with genitourinary syndrome of menopause contributes to stress and urge symptoms"}, {"question": "Have you had prostate surgery or problems with your prostate?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Prostate enlargement or prior prostate surgery in men suggests overflow incontinence or sphincter injury"}, {"question": "Do you have diabetes, multiple sclerosis, stroke or a spinal cord injury?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Neurologic disease or diabetes can cause urge or overflow incontinence from bladder neuropathy"}, {"question": "What medicines do you take, including diuretics, sedatives or bladder medicines?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Diuretics, sedatives, anticholinergics and alpha-blockers can worsen or cause leakage"}, {"question": "How much caffeine and alcohol do you drink each day?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "High caffeine or alcohol intake can worsen urgency and frequency"}, {"question": "Do you smoke?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Smoking is a risk factor for stress incontinence and for bladder cancer"}, {"question": "How often do you have a bowel movement, and do you strain?", "catego