pressure and fullness in my lower belly", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "I have to pee all the time", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "My periods are much more painful than they used to be", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "My lower back aches", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Sex has become painful", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "We've been trying to get pregnant and it hasn't happened", "frequency": "rare"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual over months to years; often noticed when periods become heavier or a mass effect develops", "duration": "Usually present for many months by the time of diagnosis; may be an incidental finding", "progression": "Slowly progressive; bleeding and pressure symptoms worsen as fibroids enlarge, and symptoms typically improve after menopause", "location": "Lower abdomen and pelvis; bleeding is uterine in origin", "radiation": "Pelvic or lower back pain may radiate to the sacrum, buttocks or thighs", "quality": "Heavy, sometimes clotted menstrual bleeding; pelvic pressure or fullness; dull, crampy pelvic pain", "severity": "Variable; bleeding can be heavy enough to cause anemia, and bulk symptoms can be moderate to severe", "timing": "Bleeding occurs with menses and may be prolonged; pressure and urinary symptoms are often constant and worse with a full bladder", "aggravating": ["Menses", "Full bladder", "Lying flat", "Intercourse (for dyspareunia)"], "relieving": ["Emptying the bladder", "NSAIDs for cramping", "Rest"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Pelvic pressure or feeling of fullness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Urinary frequency or urgency from bladder compression", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dysmenorrhea (painful periods)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Lower back pain", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Dyspareunia (pain with intercourse)", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Constipation or tenesmus from rec