sabdominal and transvaginal)", "why": "First-line imaging to confirm fibroids and map their size and location"}, {"test": "tsh", "why": "Thyroid disease is a common reversible cause of abnormal uterine bleeding"}], "confirmatory": [{"test": "MRI pelvis without and with IV contrast", "why": "Clarifies atypical findings or maps fibroids before surgery or embolization", "only_if": "ultrasound is indeterminate, or surgery or uterine artery embolization is planned"}, {"test": "Saline infusion sonohysterography", "why": "Defines submucosal fibroids when heavy bleeding or infertility is the main problem", "only_if": "submucosal fibroid is suspected and ultrasound is inconclusive"}], "supporting": [{"test": "ferritin", "why": "Confirms iron deficiency as the cause of anemia"}, {"test": "Endometrial biopsy", "why": "Excludes endometrial cancer", "only_if": "abnormal uterine bleeding in a woman over 45, or any postmenopausal bleeding"}, {"test": "Hysteroscopy", "why": "Directly visualizes and can treat submucosal fibroids", "only_if": "submucosal fibroid is suspected or hysteroscopic resection is planned"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast", "why": "Not needed for diagnosis; fibroids are usually an incidental finding and CT adds radiation without improving characterization"}, {"test": "Ca 125", "why": "No role in evaluating fibroids; may be mildly elevated by fibroids and lead to unnecessary concern for ovarian cancer"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "Not part of the routine workup; normal fibroids do not cause significant inflammation"}, {"test": "coagulation panel", "why": "Not routine; consider only if a bleeding disorder is suspected from the history"}], "decision_points": ["Pregnancy test before imaging and before any treatment in a reproductive-age woman", "Pelvic ultrasound is the first-line study; MRI is reserved for indeterminate findings or surgical planning", "Endometrial biopsy is required for abnormal uterine bleeding in women over 45 