tic underwear", "strength": "weak"}], "comorbidities": ["Diabetes mellitus", "Immunosuppression", "Pregnancy"], "family_history": [], "social_history": ["Sexual activity, including new or multiple partners", "Douching practices", "Use of scented feminine hygiene products"], "exposures": ["Antibiotics", "Vaginal sprays, douches, spermicides, soaps, detergents, or fabric softeners"], "risk_medications": ["antibiotics", "corticosteroids", "oral contraceptives", "spermicides"]}, "presentation": {"chief_complaints": [{"text": "I have vaginal discharge that won't go away", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "My vagina and vulva itch and burn", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "There is a bad smell down there", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "It hurts when I pee", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Sex is painful", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "hpi": {"onset": "Gradual over a few days", "duration": "Days to weeks; often recurrent or persistent", "progression": "Discharge and irritation develop over several days; symptoms may fluctuate with menstrual cycle or after intercourse", "location": "Vagina and vulva", "radiation": "Usually none", "quality": "Discharge may be thin and gray, thick and white like cottage cheese, or gray-green; itching and burning are common", "severity": "Mild to moderate; can be severe with marked itching or soreness", "timing": "Persistent; may worsen after intercourse or at certain points in the menstrual cycle", "aggravating": ["Intercourse", "Urination", "Tight clothing", "Scented products"], "relieving": ["Nothing consistently relieves it", "Avoiding irritants may help"], "associated_symptoms": [{"text": "Abnormal vaginal discharge (color, amount, or odor change)", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Vaginal or vulvar itching", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Vaginal or vulvar burning or soreness", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Fishy or foul odor, especially after sex", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Pain or burning with urination", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Pain with intercourse", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Redness or swelling of the vulva", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "pertinent_negatives": ["Fever", "Pelvic or abdominal pain", "Heavy vaginal bleeding or bleeding between periods", "Genital ulcers or sores", "Nausea or vomiting", "Symptoms in a sexual partner"]}, "ros": [{"system": "genitourinary", "positives": [{"text": "Abnormal vaginal discharge", "frequency": "almost_always"}, {"text": "Vaginal itching", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Burning with urination", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Hematuria", "Flank pain", "Urinary frequency or urgency"], "argues_against": ["Upper urinary tract infection"]}, {"system": "reproductive", "positives": [{"text": "Pain with intercourse", "frequency": "sometimes"}, {"text": "Vulvar redness or swelling", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Missed period", "Vaginal bleeding between periods", "Pelvic mass"], "argues_against": ["Pregnancy", "Pelvic inflammatory disease", "Malignancy"]}, {"system": "constitutional", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Fever", "Chills", "Weight loss", "Fatigue"], "argues_against": ["Systemic infection"]}, {"system": "gastrointestinal", "positives": [], "negatives": ["Abdominal pain", "Nausea", "Vomiting", "Diarrhea"], "argues_against": ["Gastrointestinal infection"]}, {"system": "skin", "positives": [{"text": "Vulvar irritation or rash", "frequency": "sometimes"}], "negatives": ["Genital ulcers", "Skin blisters"], "argues_against": ["Herpes simplex virus", "Other dermatologic conditions"]}], "atypical": [{"population": "pregnancy", "how_it_differs": "Vaginitis may be asymptomatic or symptoms may be attributed to normal pregnancy changes; bacterial vaginosis and trichomoniasis increase risk of preterm labor and preterm birth.", "missing_classic_features": ["Marked discharge or itching"]}, {"population": "older_adults", "how_it_differs": "Postmenopausal women may have atrophic vaginitis with dryness, burning, and dyspareunia rather than discharge; symptoms overlap with other causes.", "missing_classic_features": ["Profuse discharge", "Odor"]}, {"population": "diabetes", "how_it_differs": "Poorly controlled diabetes predisposes to recurrent yeast infections; symptoms may be more severe and persistent.", "missing_classic_features": ["Rapid resolution with standard treatment"]}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "how_it_differs": "May have more severe or atypical symptoms, including extensive candidiasis or mixed infections.", "missing_classic_features": ["Typical discharge characteristics"]}]}, "exam": {"general": {"mild": "Comfortable, no distress; normal general appearance", "moderate": "Mild discomfort or restlessness from itching or burning; otherwise well-appearing", "severe": "Visibly uncomfortable, guarding the perineum, reluctant to sit still", "critical": "Not typical for uncomplicated vaginitis; if toxic-appearing, consider another diagnosis such as pelvic inflammatory disease or systemic infection"}, "findings": [{"id": "vulvar-erythema", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "Inspect the vulva and perineum with good lighting", "finding": "Erythema and edema of the vulva and vaginal introitus", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "abnormal-discharge", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "Inspect the vaginal vault and note discharge character, color, and amount", "finding": "Abnormal vaginal discharge (thin gray, thick white cottage-cheese, or gray-green)", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "strongly_supports", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "discharge-odor", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "Assess discharge odor, including after adding potassium hydroxide (whiff test)", "finding": "Fishy or foul odor, often accentuated by KOH", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "vaginal-ph-elevated", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "Test vaginal fluid pH with pH paper", "finding": "pH greater than 4.5 (suggests bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis)", "frequency": "common", "significance": "supports", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "cervical-motion-tenderness", "region": "pelvic", "maneuver": "Perform bimanual exam and move the cervix", "finding": "Cervical motion tenderness", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "adnexal-tenderness-mass", "region": "pelvic", "maneuver": "Palpate the adnexa bimanually", "finding": "Adnexal tenderness or mass", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "essential"}, {"id": "normal-uterus-adnexa", "region": "pelvic", "maneuver": "Bimanual exam to assess uterine size, mobility, and adnexa", "finding": "Normal-sized, mobile, non-tender uterus and no adnexal masses", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-genital-ulcers", "region": "genitourinary", "maneuver": "Inspect the vulva, vagina, and cervix for ulcers or vesicles", "finding": "No genital ulcers, vesicles, or erosions", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "no-fever", "region": "general", "maneuver": "Measure temperature and assess for systemic signs", "finding": "Afebrile, no systemic toxicity", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "normal-abdomen", "region": "abdomen", "maneuver": "Palpate the abdomen for tenderness, guarding, or masses", "finding": "Soft, non-tender abdomen without guarding or rebound", "frequency": "almost_always", "significance": "neutral", "importance": "important"}, {"id": "inguinal-lymphadenopathy", "region": "lymph", "maneuver": "Palpate the inguinal lymph nodes", "finding": "Inguinal lymphadenopathy", "frequency": "rare", "significance": "argues_against", "importance": "optional"}]}, "vitals": {"temp": {"mild": {"min": 98.0, "max": 99.5}, "moderate": {"min": 98.0, "max": 100.0}, "severe": {"min": 98.0, "max": 100.4}}, "hr": {"mild": {"min": 60, "max": 100}, "moderate": {"min": 60, "max": 100}, "severe": {"min": 60, "max": 110}}}, "labs": [{"test_id": "hcg", "frequency": "almost_always", "importance": "essential", "caveat": "Negative. Required in anyone of reproductive age who could be pregnant; pregnancy changes the differential and the treatment choices."}, {"test_id": "a1c", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 5.7, "max": 6.4}, "moderate": {"min": 6.5, "max": 8.0}, "severe": {"min": 7.5, "max": 10.0}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Ordered when recurrent or refractory candidiasis suggests undiagnosed or poorly controlled diabetes."}, {"test_id": "glucose", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 100, "max": 125}, "moderate": {"min": 126, "max": 180}, "severe": {"min": 160, "max": 250}}, "frequency": "sometimes", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Fasting glucose; supports the same suspicion of diabetes as HbA1c."}, {"test_id": "wbc", "ranges": {"mild": {"min": 10.5, "max": 13.0}, "moderate": {"min": 12.0, "max": 15.0}}, "frequency": "rare", "importance": "optional", "caveat": "Uncomplicated vaginitis does not raise the white count; a marked leukocytosis should push toward pelvic inflammatory disease or another systemic process."}], "imaging": [{"study": "Pelvic ultrasound (transvaginal or transabdominal)", "modality": "ultrasound", "preferred_when": "Pelvic pain, adnexal tenderness or mass, suspected pelvic inflammatory disease, or pregnancy concern", "findings": [{"text": "Normal uterus and ovaries with no adnexal mass or free fluid", "frequency": "common"}, {"text": "Thickened, fluid-filled fallopian tube or tubo-ovarian complex (suggests pelvic inflammatory disease)", "frequency": "rare"}, {"text": "Simple ovarian cyst or other incidental adnexal finding", "frequency": "sometimes"}]}], "workup": {"initial": [{"test": "hcg", "why": "Rules out pregnancy before treatment and imaging decisions"}, {"test": "Vaginal pH testing", "why": "pH above 4.5 supports bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis; normal pH favors candidiasis"}, {"test": "Saline wet mount microscopy", "why": "Identifies clue cells, motile trichomonads, or budding yeast and pseudohyphae"}, {"test": "10% KOH wet mount microscopy", "why": "Highlights yeast and pseudohyphae and supports the whiff test"}, {"test": "Whiff test (KOH amine odor)", "why": "Fishy amine odor supports bacterial vaginosis"}, {"test": "NAAT for Trichomonas vaginalis", "why": "Most sensitive test for trichomoniasis when wet mount is negative or suspicion is high"}, {"test": "NAAT for Chlamydia trachomatis and Neisseria gonorrhoeae", "why": "Screens for coexisting sexually transmitted infection in anyone at risk"}], "confirmatory": [], "supporting": [{"test": "Vaginal culture for Candida species", "why": "Used when recurrent or refractory candidiasis is suspected and microscopy is negative", "only_if": "recurrent or treatment-refractory symptoms with negative microscopy"}, {"test": "a1c", "why": "Looks for undiagnosed or poorly controlled diabetes driving recurrent yeast infections", "only_if": "recurrent or complicated candidiasis"}, {"test": "Pelvic ultrasound (transvaginal or transabdominal)", "why": "Evaluates for pelvic inflammatory disease, tubo-ovarian abscess, or other pelvic pathology", "only_if": "pelvic pain, adnexal tenderness or mass, or suspicion of pelvic inflammatory disease"}], "not_indicated": [{"test": "cbc", "why": "Uncomplicated vaginitis does not cause leukocytosis; reserve for systemic symptoms"}, {"test": "crp", "why": "No role in the diagnosis of uncomplicated vaginitis"}, {"test": "esr", "why": "No role in the diagnosis of uncomplicated vaginitis"}, {"test": "ua", "why": "Dysuria here is from vaginal inflammation, not a urinary tract infection; urinalysis is not routinely needed"}, {"test": "Pelvic ultrasound (transvaginal or transabdominal)", "why": "Not needed when the presentation is classic and the pelvic exam is normal", "only_if": "pelvic pain, adnexal tenderness or mass, or suspicion of pelvic inflammatory disease"}], "decision_points": ["Pregnancy test before treatment or imaging in anyone who could be pregnant", "Vaginal pH above 4.5 points to bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis; normal pH points to candidiasis", "Wet mount showing clue cells, motile trichomonads, or yeast directs therapy; if nondiagnostic, send NAAT for Trichomonas", "Cervical motion tenderness, adnexal tenderness, fever, or systemic illness should redirect the workup toward pelvic inflammatory disease", "Recurrent or refractory candidiasis should prompt testing for diabetes and consideration of non-albicans Candida"], "criteria": [{"name": "Amsel criteria for bacterial vaginosis", "summary": "Diagnosis requires at least three of: thin homogeneous gray-white discharge, vaginal pH above 4.5, a positive whiff test (fishy amine odor after KOH), and clue cells on saline wet mount.", "items": ["Thin, homogeneous, gray-white discharge", "Vaginal pH greater than 4.5", "Positive whiff test with KOH", "Clue cells on saline wet mount"]}, {"name": "Nugent score for bacterial vaginosis", "summary": "A Gram stain scoring system based on the relative amounts of Lactobacillus morphotypes, Gardnerella/Bacteroides morphotypes, and curved gram-variable rods; higher scores indicate bacterial vaginosis.", "items": ["Lactobacillus morphotypes (score 0–4)", "Gardnerella/Bacteroides morphotypes (score 0–4)", "Curved gram-variable rods (score 0–2)"]}], "scores": []}, "differential": [{"name": "Bacterial vaginosis", "slug": "bacterial-vaginosis", "why_considered": "Most common cause of vaginal discharge in reproductive-age women; thin gray discharge with fishy odor", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Thin gray-white discharge", "Fishy odor, worse after intercourse", "Often minimal itching or burning", "Recent antibiotics, douching, IUD, or new sexual partner"], "exam": ["Thin homogeneous gray discharge coating the vaginal walls", "Positive whiff test (fishy amine odor after KOH)", "Vaginal pH greater than 4.5", "Vulva and vagina usually not markedly inflamed"], "labs": ["Clue cells on saline wet mount", "Positive whiff test", "Vaginal pH greater than 4.5", "Nugent score 7-10 on Gram stain"]}}, {"name": "Vulvovaginal candidiasis", "slug": "vulvovaginal-candidiasis", "why_considered": "Common cause of intense vulvar itching with thick white discharge", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Intense vulvar itching and burning", "Thick white cottage-cheese discharge", "No odor", "Recent antibiotics, pregnancy, diabetes, or corticosteroid use"], "exam": ["Vulvar and vaginal erythema and edema", "Thick white curd-like discharge", "Vaginal pH normal (4.0-4.5)", "Negative whiff test"], "labs": ["Budding yeast and pseudohyphae on KOH wet mount", "Normal vaginal pH", "Negative amine odor"]}}, {"name": "Trichomoniasis", "slug": "trichomoniasis", "why_considered": "Sexually transmitted infection causing discharge, itching, and dysuria", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Gray-green or yellow frothy discharge", "Offensive odor", "Vulvar itching and burning", "Dysuria and dyspareunia", "New or multiple sexual partners"], "exam": ["Frothy gray-green discharge", "Vulvar and vaginal erythema", "Strawberry cervix (punctate hemorrhages) in some cases", "Vaginal pH greater than 4.5", "Positive whiff test"], "labs": ["Motile trichomonads on saline wet mount", "Positive NAAT for Trichomonas vaginalis", "Vaginal pH greater than 4.5"]}}, {"name": "Atrophic vaginitis", "slug": "atrophic-vaginitis", "why_considered": "Vaginal dryness, burning, and dyspareunia in postmenopausal or estrogen-deficient women", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Postmenopausal or breastfeeding", "Gradual onset of vaginal dryness and burning", "Dyspareunia", "Minimal or no discharge"], "exam": ["Pale, thin, dry vaginal mucosa", "Loss of vaginal rugae", "Vaginal pH elevated (greater than 4.5)", "No abnormal discharge"], "labs": ["Normal wet mount without clue cells, trichomonads, or yeast", "Elevated vaginal pH", "Negative NAAT for Trichomonas"]}}, {"name": "Pelvic inflammatory disease", "slug": "pelvic-inflammatory-disease", "why_considered": "Lower abdominal pain, discharge, and dyspareunia in a sexually active woman", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Pelvic or lower abdominal pain with cervical motion tenderness, adnexal tenderness, or fever", "discriminators": {"history": ["Lower abdominal or pelvic pain", "Fever and chills", "New or multiple sexual partners", "Abnormal vaginal bleeding"], "exam": ["Cervical motion tenderness", "Adnexal tenderness or mass", "Fever", "Mucopurulent cervical discharge"], "labs": ["Positive NAAT for Chlamydia trachomatis or Neisseria gonorrhoeae", "Elevated white blood cell count", "Elevated inflammatory markers (ESR, CRP)"], "imaging": ["Thickened, fluid-filled fallopian tube or tubo-ovarian complex on pelvic ultrasound"]}}, {"name": "Genital herpes simplex virus infection", "slug": "genital-herpes", "why_considered": "Vulvar pain, burning, and dysuria that can be mistaken for vaginitis", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Prodrome of tingling or burning", "Painful genital sores or blisters", "Dysuria", "Flu-like symptoms with primary episode"], "exam": ["Vesicles, ulcers, or erosions on vulva, vagina, or cervix", "Inguinal lymphadenopathy", "Vulvar tenderness"], "labs": ["Positive NAAT or PCR for herpes simplex virus from lesion swab", "Negative wet mount for clue cells, trichomonads, or yeast"]}}, {"name": "Vaginal cancer", "slug": "vaginal-cancer", "why_considered": "Persistent vaginal discharge or bleeding that does not respond to treatment for common vaginitis", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Persistent or bloody discharge, postcoital bleeding, or a visible vaginal lesion that fails to improve with standard therapy", "discriminators": {"history": ["Persistent or bloody vaginal discharge", "Postcoital or postmenopausal bleeding", "Symptoms not responding to treatment for vaginitis", "History of HPV or cervical cancer"], "exam": ["Visible ulcerated or exophytic vaginal lesion", "Indurated or friable mass", "Bleeding on contact"], "labs": ["Biopsy of lesion showing malignancy"], "imaging": ["Pelvic MRI or CT showing vaginal mass and extent of disease"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Mild discharge or itching without significant discomfort; normal daily activities unaffected; no fever or pelvic pain", "moderate": "Persistent discharge, itching, burning, or odor causing bother and some interference with daily activities; no systemic symptoms", "severe": "Marked vulvar and vaginal inflammation with intense itching, burning, dysuria, or dyspareunia; may have extensive candidiasis or recurrent symptoms; no systemic toxicity", "critical": "Not typical for uncomplicated vaginitis; if toxic-appearing with fever, hypotension, or severe pelvic pain, consider pelvic inflammatory disease, tubo-ovarian abscess, or sepsis"}, "red_flags": [{"finding": "Fever, chills, or systemic toxicity", "meaning": "Suggests pelvic inflammatory disease or another systemic infection rather than uncomplicated vaginitis"}, {"finding": "Pelvic or lower abdominal pain", "meaning": "Suggests pelvic inflammatory disease, tubo-ovarian abscess, or another pelvic process"}, {"finding": "Cervical motion tenderness or adnexal tenderness or mass", "meaning": "Suggests pelvic inflammatory disease or tubo-ovarian abscess; requires prompt evaluation and treatment"}, {"finding": "Heavy vaginal bleeding or bleeding between periods", "meaning": "Requires evaluation for malignancy, pregnancy complications, or other bleeding source"}, {"finding": "Genital ulcers or vesicles", "meaning": "Suggests herpes simplex virus or another ulcerative genital condition"}, {"finding": "Persistent or bloody discharge not responding to treatment", "meaning": "Suggests vaginal cancer or another malignancy; requires biopsy"}, {"finding": "Positive pregnancy test with symptoms", "meaning": "Changes treatment choices and raises risk of preterm labor with bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis"}], "complications": [{"name": "Increased risk of HIV and other sexually transmitted infections", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis", "Ongoing sexual activity without barrier protection"]}, {"name": "Preterm labor and preterm birth", "timing": "any", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Pregnancy with bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis", "Symptoms of preterm labor"]}, {"name": "Recurrent or refractory infection", "timing": "late", "seriousness": "minor", "frequency": "sometimes", "clues": ["Repeated episodes despite treatment", "Underlying diabetes or immunosuppression", "Non-albicans Candida species"]}, {"name": "Pelvic inflammatory disease", "timing": "early", "seriousness": "serious", "frequency": "rare", "clues": ["Fever", "Pelvic pain", "Cervical motion tenderness", "Adnexal tenderness"]}], "special_populations": [{"population": "pregnancy", "differences": "Bacterial vaginosis and trichomoniasis increase the risk of preterm labor and preterm birth; treatment is recommended. Symptoms may be attributed to normal pregnancy changes, and treatment choices must be pregnancy-safe."}, {"population": "older_adults", "differences": "Postmenopausal women may have atrophic vaginitis with dryness, burning, and dyspareunia rather than discharge; symptoms overlap with other causes and may respond to estrogen cream."}, {"population": "diabetes", "differences": "Poorly controlled diabetes predisposes to recurrent yeast infections; symptoms may be more severe and persistent, and glycemic control is part of management."}, {"population": "immunocompromised", "differences": "May have more severe or atypical symptoms, including extensive candidiasis or mixed infections, and may require longer or alternative treatment."}]}, "teaching": {"key_questions": [{"question": "What does the discharge look like — color, thickness, and amount?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Thin gray-white suggests bacterial vaginosis; thick white cottage-cheese suggests candidiasis; frothy gray-green suggests trichomoniasis"}, {"question": "Is there an odor, and is it worse after sex?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Fishy amine odor worse after intercourse points to bacterial vaginosis; absent odor favors candidiasis"}, {"question": "How bad is the itching?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Intense vulvar itching favors candidiasis; minimal itching favors bacterial vaginosis"}, {"question": "When did the symptoms start and how have they changed?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Gradual onset over days; chronic or recurrent symptoms suggest atrophic vaginitis, recurrent candidiasis, or a noninfectious cause"}, {"question": "Do you have pain or burning with urination?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "External dysuria from inflamed vulvar tissue; trichomoniasis commonly causes dysuria"}, {"question": "Is sex painful?", "category": "associated", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Dyspareunia, common with candidiasis, trichomoniasis, and atrophic vaginitis"}, {"question": "Have you taken antibiotics recently?", "category": "medications", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Recent antibiotics predispose to both bacterial vaginosis and candidiasis"}, {"question": "Do you use corticosteroids, immunosuppressants, or hormonal medicines?", "category": "medications", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Corticosteroids and immunosuppression predispose to candidiasis; hormonal status matters for atrophic changes"}, {"question": "Do you have diabetes, or is your blood sugar poorly controlled?", "category": "pmh", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Diabetes, especially uncontrolled, predisposes to recurrent yeast infections"}, {"question": "Are you pregnant, or could you be? When was your last period?", "category": "obstetric", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Pregnancy changes treatment choices and raises the risk of preterm labor with bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis"}, {"question": "Are you sexually active, and do you have a new or multiple partners?", "category": "sexual", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "New or multiple partners raises concern for trichomoniasis and coexisting sexually transmitted infections"}, {"question": "Do you douche or use vaginal sprays, scented soaps, spermicides, or new detergents?", "category": "social", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Irritant or allergic vaginitis and a strong risk factor for bacterial vaginosis"}, {"question": "Do you have any fever, pelvic pain, or bleeding between periods?", "category": "red_flag", "importance": "essential", "looking_for": "Fever, pelvic pain, or abnormal bleeding suggests pelvic inflammatory disease or malignancy rather than uncomplicated vaginitis"}, {"question": "Have you had genital sores or blisters?", "category": "ros", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Ulcerative lesions suggest herpes simplex virus rather than vaginitis"}, {"question": "Have you had these symptoms before, and did treatment help?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Recurrent or treatment-refractory symptoms suggest diabetes, non-albicans Candida, or another diagnosis"}], "accepted_names": ["Vaginitis", "Vulvovaginitis", "Vaginal infection", "Vaginal discharge"], "reasoning_points": ["Abnormal vaginal discharge with itching, burning, or odor in a reproductive-age woman", "Discharge character narrows the cause: thin gray-white with fishy odor suggests bacterial vaginosis, thick white cottage-cheese suggests candidiasis, frothy gray-green suggests trichomoniasis", "Vaginal pH above 4.5 points to bacterial vaginosis or trichomoniasis; normal pH points to candidiasis", "Saline wet mount findings of clue cells, motile trichomonads, or budding yeast and pseudohyphae direct therapy", "Positive whiff test with KOH supports bacterial vaginosis", "Pregnancy excluded before treatment and imaging decisions", "Absence of fever, pelvic pain, cervical motion tenderness, and adnexal tenderness argues against pelvic inflammatory disease", "Recurrent or refractory candidiasis should prompt testing for diabetes and consideration of non-albicans Candida"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Reproductive-age woman with classic discharge and itching", "Discharge character matches one cause exactly", "Vaginal pH and wet mount confirm the diagnosis", "No fever, pelvic pain, or systemic symptoms"], "medium": ["Mixed or overlapping symptoms that do not fit one cause cleanly", "Postmenopausal woman with dryness, burning, and dyspareunia suggesting atrophic vaginitis", "Recurrent yeast infections prompting evaluation for diabetes", "Dysuria that could be mistaken for a urinary tract infection"], "hard": ["Asymptomatic bacterial vaginosis found incidentally", "Persistent or bloody discharge not responding to treatment, raising concern for vaginal cancer", "Pregnant patient where treatment choices and preterm risk must be weighed", "Immunocompromised patient with extensive or atypical candidiasis", "Symptoms that overlap with pelvic inflammatory disease or herpes simplex virus"]}}}$rounds_kb$::jsonb)
