": "Pregnancy changes treatment — topical azoles for 7 days instead of oral fluconazole"}, {"question": "Have you noticed any sores, blisters, or ulcers on the genitals?", "category": "associated", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Absent; painful vesicles or ulcers suggest genital herpes"}, {"question": "Do you have a new sexual partner, or any concern about a sexually transmitted infection?", "category": "sexual", "importance": "important", "looking_for": "Risk factors for chlamydial or gonococcal cervicitis and trichomoniasis"}, {"question": "Have you used any new soaps, detergents, or feminine hygiene products?", "category": "social", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Irritant exposure suggesting contact dermatitis rather than infection"}, {"question": "Have you tried any over-the-counter yeast treatment, and did it help?", "category": "hpi", "importance": "optional", "looking_for": "Partial or no response raises concern for a non-albicans species or the wrong diagnosis"}], "accepted_names": ["Vulvovaginal candidiasis", "Vaginal yeast infection", "Candidal vaginitis", "Candidiasis", "Moniliasis", "Yeast infection"], "reasoning_points": ["Intense vulvar itching with a thick, white, clumpy discharge and no foul odor", "Recent antibiotic use, diabetes, pregnancy, or immunosuppression as a predisposing factor", "Vulvar and vaginal erythema with thick white discharge on speculum exam and no cervical motion tenderness", "Normal vaginal pH (4.0–4.5) with budding yeast, pseudohyphae, or hyphae on wet mount", "No clue cells, no motile trichomonads, and a negative whiff test", "Pregnancy excluded before systemic azole therapy in a reproductive-age patient", "Red flags such as fever, pelvic pain, or mucopurulent cervical discharge are absent"], "difficulty": {"easy": ["Reproductive-age woman with classic intense itching and cottage-cheese discharge", "Recent course of antibiotics as a clear trigger", "Vulvar erythema with thick white discharge on exam", "W